{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think","id":1041769,"title":"What would the Gods think.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-01T05:24:01-08:00","id":1041769,"title":"What would the Gods think.","content":"Hello everybody. I was thinking about how the Gods interact with the modern world, and occurred to me that would be interesting to discuss how would be the opinion of the Gods in different question of modern society, like women rights, gay marriage, polygamy, pollution and global warming, consumerism, transgenic foods, etc. I think it would made them much more real if they all had different opinions, and can be the bases of a whole adventure. (like a adventure to change the opinion of a homophobic god). Also, there is much of mythologies I don't know nor understand, so would be nice see other opinions and discover new things. I dont want to make statements for any opinion, nor reduce the importance of any of those topics, just think that is worth a conversation of how that would work in the scenario of scion. Plus, have in mind that those Gods were born in very far, very distant societies, with different conditions and social stigmas, paradigms and taboos.<br /> <br /> To start the discussion, what about gay relations and gay marriages?<br /> The old Greek society, as far as I know, were okay to exist gay sex between a man and a younger man, considered a woman, but it would stop as soon as the younger man start growing a beard, when he would start to be a man. The young man would be over the protection and patronage of the older one. There was no legal homosexual marriage, and gay sex between woman was known but also not taking serious. Is worth remember that women on the old Greece were usually not much more than property. Romans civilization were better on the women rights, but not on the gay rights.<br /> <br /> I think the official opinion of the Theoi would be Zeus opinion, and I think he would be the traditionalist kind, with a very old Greek opinion of gay marriage and women (what would explain is usual cheating, raping and generally unpleasant behaviour), and unapologetic about it, but I don't see him making a lot of fuss to change the world about it. Hera's opinion on the gay subject maybe would be the same (goddess of family and all that), but I can see she being more open to it (a gay marriage is a marriage, after all). Apollo I think would be more than okay with both the sex and the marriage, as would be Athena and Artemis, specially of the female kind. Ares would be okay too with gay relations (gay relations were common on armies after all) but wouldn't care if two gay people marry. Poseidon I don't know, maybe traditionalist (he is the oldest of the Gods, I think). Hades wouldn't care. Hermes would be okay, most modern of the Gods. Hephaestus I also don't know, maybe just don't care. Aphrodite I would say is okay and happy with it. Demeter I see as traditionalist, but not as much as Zeus. Dyonisius would be happy about it, for sure.<br /> <br /> Norse mythology, and society, I dont know so much, but I think most of the Gods would be okay. They seem too worried with their own problems (be Ragnarock, giants or just the problems they find for themselves) to care much if society became open to different relations, but besides Balder (as all loving and all loved God) and Tyr (as God of justice and fairness) I dont think they would fight for gays rights unless they feel involved somehow. At least they would probably see men and women marriages as equal.<br /> <br /> Egyptian mythology I am not comfortable making an final statement, would depends if someone knows if homosexuality was okay or not in old Egyptian society. I think I saw somewhere that it wasn't, and once I saw that one of 42 judges judged that, but it was a long time ago and I don't know the source, so I could be wrong. If it is true, the gods linked to those judgement and the most &quot;moral&quot; and followers of old tradition would be against it, but the less traditional, the better to adapt to a new culture would be more open to it. I also think Egyptian society were more equal in men/women rights (they allowed women as governors and pharaohs, but they should sometimes dress as a man), so they would see both kinds of homo-relations as equal, or close.<br /> <br /> Old Japanese society had a similar tradition of an old man mentoring a younger one, but I don't think they accepted gay marriage. Also, they arent great on women rights.<br /> <br /> The other mythologies I know very little about both about the myths and the societies, so I just gonna point what I think would be the general opinion, but if someone knows better please feel free to correct me:<br /> Manitouk: The tribes were many, but I saw somewhere some had gay marriages, so I think they might be okay, but would be a very diverse opinion, with no official statement.<br /> Deva: I think they would be okay. Hinduism at least seem very open to different versions and different concepts, so I guess they would be okay.<br /> Tuatha de Dannan: I dont know. I honestly dont know much of them, so no idea.<br /> Teotl: Also no idea. I never saw anything about Aztecs having gay marriages, but I might just be uninformed.<br /> Shen: I guess against. Very traditionalist, very restrictive society, and a very bureaucratic pantheon so unlikely to change. Also, not very great on women rights.<br /> Orisha: I dont know, I guess might be the same as the Manitouk, but I know even less about African and African descendent religions.<br /> <br /> I think it covers the basic. Hope you guys can bring some new information and new opinions to the table.<br /> (and forgive me any misspell or grammatical error, English is not my first language).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:16:17-08:00","id":1041784,"title":"","content":"Short answer is they don't interact with modern society, at least not to the extent they used to. Fatebinding is what caused them to retreat from the world in the first place and now they only return when they have business to take care of (or to sire children).<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the advancements of society, that would depend entirely upon the pantheon. Zeus NEVER wanted humanity to become self reliant, and is probably scowling at us as we speak. I imagine that the modern world pisses him off to no end.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Aztecs are another possibility that would not adapt well to the modern world. Their culture had iron clad gender roles and they did NOT approve of homosexuals. Also, they sacrificed people because they believed it staved off the apocalypse. So finding out that human sacrifice is now illegal in modern society probably hasn't improved their relationship.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Norse also wouldn't take kindly to homosexuals, I think. Their word for a man baring homosexual tendencies was 'womanly' and it was considered one of the greatest insults of Norse culture, if I'm not mistaken. As for gender roles, however, I don't think they'd have a problem with treating women as equals. They had shield maidens and Valkyries on the battlefield, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember that the pantheons are not mortal men and women. They are deities of ancient cultures and pagan religions, any one of which claims to be responsible for creating humanity in the first place. One of the PDF pantheons (Yazata, I think?) specifically created humans to serve them as a slave race! Customs which would be appalling to modern man are considered sacred to them. To put it bluntly, the Pantheons have outdated beliefs, and in order to prevent being warped by the machinations of Fate and the world view of mortals, they chose to distance themselves and act in the world through proxy agents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-01-2017, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:25:16-08:00","id":1041787,"title":"","content":"I am about to walk out the door on my way to class, so I can't give a huge in-depth answer, but I can actually direct this question to GBN's old blog who did a <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.ca/2012/05/ancient-sex-blog-spotlight.html\" target=\"_blank\">huge writeup</a> on every single one of these Pantheons and their perceptions of homosexual relationships. Unfortunatly, most of them are not great, the Aesir for example don't really care about male homosexuality, as long as you are the top. If you are bottom, you are the subject of a colossal amount of social stigma, and accusations of such behavior come up Mythologically as seriously dire.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha are slightly odd since we have no records either for or against homosexuality. We have their complex marriage system left, which does not make any mention of homosexual marriage, but we do have a very homoerotic scene between CuChulain and his foster brother Fer Daid. The way the Tuatha approach their own social systems, and morals however, as long as you are over the top, ridiculously bad ass, and the like, they will probably not care. <br /> <br /> The Teotl, unfortunately, will kill men and women for having homosexual relationships. It makes sense within the cosmological system desperate to keep the sun alive and the ever present need for more citizens. I believe the executions were strangulation primarily, and somewhat interesting for acknowledging the existence of gay women.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:12:07-08:00","id":1041806,"title":"","content":"&quot;Zeus NEVER wanted humanity to be self-reliant&quot;<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Zeus emphatically did want humanity to be SELF-reliant, and was furious over Prometheus giving us a hand-out instead of us pulling ourselves up by our bootstraps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:17:55-08:00","id":1041810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1041806#post1041806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Zeus NEVER wanted humanity to be self-reliant&quot;<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Zeus emphatically did want humanity to be SELF-reliant, and was furious over Prometheus giving us a hand-out instead of us pulling ourselves up by our bootstraps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Really?<br /> <br /> Really...?<br /> <br /> The pantheon with the biggest reputation for punishing mortals for the simple crime of being more talented than the gods <i>at anything</i> has just been misunderstood this whole time?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the reason Zeus banned humans from having access to fire is because he screwed up when choosing what humanity should sacrifice to the gods. I don't remember exactly how the story goes, but basically humans would eat all the tasty meats and plants, while giving the scraps and bones to the gods. It was supposed to be the other way around, with mortals surviving off the scraps left over by the gods. Zeus took away fire so that they couldn't make the sacrifices, holding their food supply ransom because he didn't bother checking before making a snap decision.<br /> <br /> <br /> When Prometheus gave fire back to humans and allowed them to resume their lives, he punished him for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-01-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:40:15-08:00","id":1041824,"title":"","content":"I was mocking bootstraps ideology, it was meant to be facicious","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:51:55-08:00","id":1041829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1041824#post1041824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was mocking bootstraps ideology, it was meant to be facicious</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh.<br /> <br /> Sarcasm is hard to convey in text form. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:13:52-08:00","id":1041835,"title":"","content":"Thing is, the Scion world is different from ours because all these pantheons are real there, and their worshippers still exist and have influence on society. And here lies the problem: if one assumes that the Scion pantheons are real, and their worshippers active, then they have put their own views and beliefs in to practice. So unless it is also assumed that the Gods and Goddesses can change their views and rules over time, it may actually be a moot point to discuss how the rights of women, minorities, the LGBT community, etc, are handled, because it is entirely possible that those movements never came to pass. Worshippers of (for example) a traditional Zeus wouldn't exactly view women as equals. It's known that Tlazolteotl of the Aztecs punished homosexuality and infidelity horribly. Most old cultures and the religions were at best cautious of strangers from strange lands. You really have to allow that the worship and the God's have changed over time to the present day to have a world that resembles our own. Otherwise, there could be some really unpleasant ramifications to consider in the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:32:20-08:00","id":1041843,"title":"","content":"Neall's thoughts on the subject:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This actually ties into an interesting element of '''Scion''', though - you're modern characters, and modern people, interacting with ancient mores and divinities and social codes. In much of the modern day, who gives a shit if it's a womanly act or a specifically feminine practice? (Besides all the \u00c6sir.)<br /> <br /> If you're a male Scion, is your masculinity defined by the magics you perform? Do you bow to social pressure, or do you tell Thor to choke on his hammer, you'll wear a dress if you feel like it and magic all day? And this goes way beyond the Norse. The Greeks do all kinds of inappropriate shit, and still do. The Aztecs are expecting their blood or the sun don't rise. What's it ''mean'' to confront this sort of thing head-on, these belief systems? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Gods of '''Scion''' are not the actual gods of these religions, but the gods through the chosen lens of mythology and fiction for game purposes. Loki uses the singular they. I'd be much happier saying Caeneus is a trans* Scion of Poseidon. On the other hand, there's the danger of [...] effectively whitewashing the myths and de-fanging the pathos you get from these radically different ancient mores in the modern era. It's a balancing act, one that needs to actually be taken on a case-by-case basis. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:06:42-08:00","id":1041862,"title":"","content":"Some of the best stories I have seen play out in Scion rely on the Gods retaining their original cultural positions. Scions placed in positions where they have to fight tooth and nail to resist, or force their Pantheon into allowing certain things. Netjer Scions desperately resisting being married to a sibling of theirs, Anunna Scions who treat mortals as people, not things, Scions who violate gender norms, etc. My favorite theme of Scion is that of culture clash, and it has given me so many awesome characters and stories over the last almost decade of playing.<br /> <br /> I still want to come back to an Anunna Scion who cares for mortals, especially dead mortals, and tries to make the afterlife less dismal for everyone involved, even Ereshkigal. I love the idea of challenging ancient norms, easing the Gods into it, and bringing about change through the actions of an individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:08:55-08:00","id":1041864,"title":"","content":"And that's really the big difference between the worlds of first and second edition; in first, it's the world as we know it, until the Titans escape, and suddenly the Gods are back, and everything changes. In second, the Gods have always been here, &quot;all myths are true&quot; [they should put that on a t-shirt - I'd buy it!], and the world has always had their influence. In the real world, religions are &quot;bottom-up&quot;. The culture has created Gods and Goddesses that reflect the realities of their world, or how they want it to be, and the priests/priestesses espouse their rules within the framework of &quot;God X says to do this, and I speak for them, so you should do what I/They say.&quot; In Scion, it's &quot;top-down&quot;; the deities are demonstrably real, and so are their rules, the cultures are directly influenced by that, and the priests/priestesses really do have a line to their deity. Such a world would have differences from ours in many ways, but it's up to the individual GM to decide how much or how little to involve those differences in their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:10:04-08:00","id":1041985,"title":"","content":"Who's to say gods cannot change? Mars the noble, agricultural patron of the Romans is a far cry from the insufferable brute he was as Ares, after all.<br /> <br /> To me, locking in all of the gods to a very backwards, conservative mindset is an entirely too limiting view of things, one that suffocates interesting story potential at best and is actively looking to artificially echo existing oppression at worst. It's absurd to me to say that the gods can figure out a cell phone but absolutely have to come down hard on homosexuality or women's rights, especially given hundreds of thousands of years of cultural shift among their followers since their ancient heydays. Odin's already practiced &quot;womanly&quot; magics, Loki has already given birth, the Theoi are drowning in homosexuality... there's zero reason in my eyes to pin current conservatism on these figures.<br /> <br /> You're welcome to have your gods be stuck in the past if that's what you want to play, but to me Scion is a game of <i>modern </i>mythology: these gods aren't dusty throwbacks, they're here and alive and just as much a part of the world as you or me. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:52:44-08:00","id":1042011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1041985#post1041985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's to say gods cannot change? Mars the noble, agricultural patron of the Romans is a far cry from the insufferable brute he was as Ares, after all.<br /> <br /> To me, locking in all of the gods to a very backwards, conservative mindset is an entirely too limiting view of things, one that suffocates interesting story potential at best and is actively looking to artificially echo existing oppression at worst. It's absurd to me to say that the gods can figure out a cell phone but absolutely have to come down hard on homosexuality or women's rights, especially given hundreds of thousands of years of cultural shift among their followers since their ancient heydays. Odin's already practiced &quot;womanly&quot; magics, Loki has already given birth, the Theoi are drowning in homosexuality... there's zero reason in my eyes to pin current conservatism on these figures.<br /> <br /> You're welcome to have your gods be stuck in the past if that's what you want to play, but to me Scion is a game of <i>modern </i>mythology: these gods aren't dusty throwbacks, they're here and alive and just as much a part of the world as you or me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is arguing to pin current conservatism on these figures at all, not in the slightest. The really shitty stances discussed here are from, what I linked to at least, far from modern. All of those stances were historical, drawn from the populations that worshiped the Pantheons.<br /> <br /> In my games, the Gods mostly don't really 'get' cell phones, or cars, or much of anything outside the direct period of their dominant mortal worship. (I have them locked in their Overworlds / Underworlds / Not Involved for the period for various reasons. Except the Shen, Kami, Deva, etc) I <i>love</i> the story forcing the Divine to change, forcing them to confront the new reality with confusion and occasionally anger. I don't feel that by doing this I am actively suffocating interesting story potential, I think I am creating it. The Gods <i>will</i> change, and they will be changed by their Scions. The Theoi will look at the world, and rage at it, throwing morals several milenium out of date around until a Scion stands up and challenges them in their own field. The Tuatha plot to emerge and enslave the entirety of Ireland's mortal populace, or kill them all, and a Scion of theirs tries to bridge the gap between the warring peoples. A gay Son of Thor stands strong against the Aesir, and employees their Epic Intelligence and Epic Manipulation to twist their own anti-homosexual narratives back upon themselves, justifying his relationship as the heights of masculinity.<br /> <br /> Essentially, in my games there will be change, nothing is static, I just like for it to happen 'on screen,' for my players, or myself if I am a player, to get to be the catalyst for it. Change the world for the better, make a kinder afterlife, embark on a pro-homosexual theological debate with the Four Tezcatlipocas, you are a Scion, you are great, and you <i>will</i> change the world, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":".  I am terrible at formatting things. 02-01-2017, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:23:47-08:00","id":1042029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042011#post1042011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think anyone is arguing to pin current conservatism on these figures at all, not in the slightest. The really shitty stances discussed here are from, what I linked to at least, far from modern. All of those stances were historical, drawn from the populations that worshiped the Pantheons.<br /> <br /> In my games, the Gods mostly don't really 'get' cell phones, or cars, or much of anything outside the direct period of their dominant mortal worship. (I have them locked in their Overworlds / Underworlds / Not Involved for the period for various reasons. Except the Shen, Kami, Deva, etc) I <i>love</i> the story forcing the Divine to change, forcing them to confront the new reality with confusion and occasionally anger. I don't feel that by doing this I am actively suffocating interesting story potential, I think I am creating it. The Gods <i>will</i> change, and they will be changed by their Scions. The Theoi will look at the world, and rage at it, throwing morals several milenium out of date around until a Scion stands up and challenges them in their own field. The Tuatha plot to emerge and enslave the entirety of Ireland's mortal populace, or kill them all, and a Scion of theirs tries to bridge the gap between the warring peoples. A gay Son of Thor stands strong against the Aesir, and employees their Epic Intelligence and Epic Manipulation to twist their own anti-homosexual narratives back upon themselves, justifying his relationship as the heights of masculinity.<br /> <br /> Essentially, in my games there will be change, nothing is static, I just like for it to happen 'on screen,' for my players, or myself if I am a player, to get to be the catalyst for it. Change the world for the better, make a kinder afterlife, embark on a pro-homosexual theological debate with the Four Tezcatlipocas, you are a Scion, you are great, and you <i>will</i> change the world, that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I don't want a world where the ultimate powers in the world need to be convinced of what I consider to be fundamental rights, and I think it's silly to think they would be unchanging until my player character stumble along to say &quot;hey, treat women like people&quot; or &quot;don't murder queer folks!&quot; <br /> <br /> I think the narrative of a transgender woman who finds that her divine parent is more supportive than the mortals around her is way more potent than yet another story where the characters have to justify our existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:29:24-08:00","id":1042033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042029#post1042029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I don't want a world where the ultimate powers in the world need to be convinced of what I consider to be fundamental rights, and I think it's silly to think they would be unchanging until my player character stumble along to say &quot;hey, treat women like people&quot; or &quot;don't murder queer folks!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the narrative of a transgender woman who finds that her divine parent is more supportive than the mortals around her is way more potent than yet another story where the characters have to justify our existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough! I totally understand that side of it, we've had discussions about it from within our own game group before based around not wanting to deal with the same discriminatory shit they face in reality as in game. Changing the Gods normally happens slowly, through political moves, adjusting theological stances, or just having overwhelming Epic Charisma where going, &quot;Hey, so, like, don't kill me for being gay?&quot; actually works pretty perfectly.<br /> <br /> Our games are primarily political, focusing heavily on social changes, social challenges, and dealing with Gods returning to the world, so this sort of thing comes up a lot. We also have to have, &quot;Okay, right, but the mortals are <i>people too</i> so you can't kill the entirety of Anatolia because they forgot to worship you.&quot; conversations with Divine Parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:54:22-08:00","id":1042052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1041985#post1041985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's to say gods cannot change? Mars the noble, agricultural patron of the Romans is a far cry from the insufferable brute he was as Ares, after all.<br /> <br /> To me, locking in all of the gods to a very backwards, conservative mindset is an entirely too limiting view of things, one that suffocates interesting story potential at best and is actively looking to artificially echo existing oppression at worst. It's absurd to me to say that the gods can figure out a cell phone but absolutely have to come down hard on homosexuality or women's rights, especially given hundreds of thousands of years of cultural shift among their followers since their ancient heydays. Odin's already practiced &quot;womanly&quot; magics, Loki has already given birth, the Theoi are drowning in homosexuality... there's zero reason in my eyes to pin current conservatism on these figures.<br /> <br /> You're welcome to have your gods be stuck in the past if that's what you want to play, but to me Scion is a game of <i>modern </i>mythology: these gods aren't dusty throwbacks, they're here and alive and just as much a part of the world as you or me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Loki gave birth after he was <b>raped</b> by a giant's horse. How does that support the gay agenda in any fashion?<br /> <br /> <br /> And as I said earlier, customs which are seen as abhorrent by modern humanity would be regarded as sacred to the pantheons of old. Hell, they're the ones who told humanity to put these oppressions into practice, to begin with. Mythologically speaking, the gods weren't shaped by human culture, human culture was shaped by the gods. Yes, I know that the opposite is true in real life, but Scion doesn't take place in real life.<br /> <br /> <br /> I know little about Egyptian mythology, but if I understand the gist of it, they followed a strict classist hierarchy. Everybody had a designated role in society and attempting to deviate from that role only lead to chaos (from their point of view). Traditional Scions of the Netjer might very well continue to support the slave trade. And why wouldn't they, considering it still exists even in the real world?<br /> <br /> <br /> And virtually every member of the Greek pantheon (barring Hades) was an egotistical maniac. They did whatever the fuck they pleased, and if you tried to call them out on it, they'd smite you (if you're lucky) or curse you to a fate worse than death! Mortals are not their equals, we don't get to tell the Theoi how to behave. Only the best and brightest of humanity get to live in paradise. Under achievers get confined to an eternity of limbo, while those who defy the gods get tossed into eternal torment. That doesn't sound like a pantheon who adapts well to the changing times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To reiterate my point, these pantheons are attributed to having created the race of mortals. They came down to us, told us what the proper way of living was, and passed judgement on anybody caught trying to deviate from their holy doctrines. To tell the gods &quot;things are different now&quot; is to tell the gods they were wrong, and that humanity no longer wishes to live by their rules. Anybody who's read into mythology of... like... any culture will know that this never ends well for mortals. Entire cities have been reduced to smoking rubble because a god or two was displeased with the way humans were acting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>If you want a setting in which the pantheons adopt themselves to the modern times, then I really think 1E is the one you want to go with. In 1E, the gods distanced themselves from humanity, and then came back to find everything different. In 2E, however, the gods never left, so it seems highly unlikely that society would have progressed to the state we know today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-01-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:09:58-08:00","id":1042060,"title":"","content":"Why the hell would the gods be more static in a world where they've had thousands of years to change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:14:35-08:00","id":1042066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042060#post1042060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the hell would the gods be more static in a world where they've had thousands of years to change?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Because during those thousands of years they've had a direct hand in human history. Which means humanity never got the chance to change, because the gods would make sure they continued to abide by their religious doctrines.<br /> <br /> And as I said, humans being allowed to change is effectively telling the gods they were wrong and foolish.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Yazata (Persian pantheon) literally created mortals to act as slaves. They didn't give a crap about our well being, we were put on this earth to serve their whims.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sorry, I understand why players might feel uncomfortable playing in a setting that supports age old oppression and bigotry. But that is honestly how things work in Scion. If you're that uncomfortable with it, I would probably recommend looking into a different game. I hear Exalted is pretty fun, and takes place in a parallel world from our reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-01-2017, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:31:06-08:00","id":1042079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042066#post1042066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Because during those thousands of years they've had a direct hand in human history. Which means humanity never got the chance to change, because the gods would make sure they continued to abide by their religious doctrines.<br /> <br /> And as I said, humans being allowed to change is effectively telling the gods they were wrong and foolish.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Yazata (Persian pantheon) literally created mortals to act as slaves. They didn't give a crap about our well being, we were put on this earth to serve their whims.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sorry, I understand why players might feel uncomfortable playing in a setting that supports age old oppression and bigotry. But that is honestly how things work in Scion. If you're that uncomfortable with it, I would probably recommend looking into a different game. I hear Exalted is pretty fun, and takes place in a parallel world from our reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The world you're proposing is absolutely not anything close to what the devs have indicated with The World in 2e and your painting of it as some sort of grimdark primitive hellscape is really, really strange. I'd love to see you cite anything other than your need to make sure nobody feels safe in a fictional space for what you're claiming, because all the material previewed so far paints The World as damn close to our own and not some horrific oppression porn dystopia.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> your thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:07:38-08:00","id":1042100,"title":"","content":"I think calling it a 'primitive hellscape' is blowing things out of proportion. Humanity could still evolve technologically over time. It's just that their culture as a whole would remain in line with what the pantheons decree. In 1E, the Gods and Titans were shown adapting modern technology to fulfill their goals. Fire Giants loading up with tanks and assault rifles, for example.<br /> <br /> I've stated it like 3 or 4 times by now that the pantheons are NOT mortal men and women. They do not see the world from our point of view, and most don't seem to care about our point of view either way. They created us, they get to decide how we live, and punishment follows those who defect. This is how mythology has always been portrayed throughout the majority of human civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:21:12-08:00","id":1042104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042100#post1042100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think calling it a 'primitive hellscape' is blowing things out of proportion. Humanity could still evolve technologically over time. It's just that their culture as a whole would remain in line with what the pantheons decree. In 1E, the Gods and Titans were shown adapting modern technology to fulfill their goals. Fire Giants loading up with tanks and assault rifles, for example.<br /> <br /> I've stated it like 3 or 4 times by now that the pantheons are NOT mortal men and women. They do not see the world from our point of view, and most don't seem to care about our point of view either way. They created us, they get to decide how we live, and punishment follows those who defect. This is how mythology has always been portrayed throughout the majority of human civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep saying this, but where is any of that in The World that Neall has described? Nothing indicates women are relegated to worse conditions than they are in reality or that homosexuals are being murdered in greater numbers than our own. This is a setting we're supposed to recognize, and there's one hell of a difference between &quot;our world but some of the churches have been replaced with pagan temples&quot; and &quot;the streets of Mexico are constantly flowing with the blood of Teotl-demanded sacrifices.&quot;<br /> <br /> Odin has already practiced womanly magics; what's to say he hasn't worked towards destigmatizing femininity and seidr among the Aesir in the thousand-plus years since the bulk of our material on him comes from? In a world where followers matter, treating women like garbage isn't going to do you any favors, so either the Theoi get with the program or at least see Hera, Aphrodite, and Athena begin to eclipse their male peers in popularity. I've said before that it's trivial to read the Osiris/Azar myth as a transgender narrative, and I have no reason to believe Het-Heru would reject any woman, regardless of what genitals they have.<br /> <br /> You're insisting on conservative values that I'm not sure some of these gods espoused and would have <b>thousands</b> of years worth of time to grow, just the same as the mortals have managed to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:38:44-08:00","id":1042111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042104#post1042104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You keep saying this, but where is any of that in The World that Neall has described?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's been explicitly stated, but this is what common sense leads me to believe. If the gods never abandoned humanity and have remained active over the last several thousand years, then by all logic, civilization would have taken a different path. It's called the Butterfly Effect. Any change to history, however small, has far reaching consequences. Humanity was able to grow and change because they didn't have omnipotent beings lording over them, telling them how to do things.<br /> <br /> Rewriting that bit of human history means you have to recognize that things wouldn't play out the way they did before.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Odin practicing womanly magics, it's a common theme among God Kings to be the &quot;Do as I say, not as I do&quot; type of people. They demanded everybody follow their rules, but were terrible at doing likewise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-01-2017, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:43:21-08:00","id":1042113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042111#post1042111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's been explicitly stated, but this is what common sense leads me to believe. If the gods never abandoned humanity and have remained active over the last several thousand years, then by all logic, civilization would have taken a different path. It's called the Butterfly Effect. Any change to history, however small, has far reaching consequences. Humanity was able to grow and change because they didn't have omnipotent beings lording over them, telling them how to do things.<br /> <br /> Rewriting that bit of human history means you have to recognize that things wouldn't play out the way they did before.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your common sense dictates a world where women and queer people are even more marginalized than our own, then I think that says more about you than the game.<br /> <br /> I'm going to have a lot of fun with all of my transgender Scions and their supportive divine parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:06:37-08:00","id":1042122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042113#post1042113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your common sense dictates a world where women and queer people are even more marginalized than our own, then I think that says more about you than the game.<br /> <br /> I'm going to have a lot of fun with all of my transgender Scions and their supportive divine parents.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay, I think we've got a communication problem. I am not in any way supporting the idea or marginalizing such people. I'm saying that in a world where the gods continued to govern human society, it would be even more difficult for grand, societal changes to take place. The gods are supposed to be wiser, more disciplined, and better focused than mortals are. Changing their laws in any fashion is to say that the Gods were wrong, short sighted, or evil. Who would worship them after that? Their reputation would be tarnished and they'd come across as power hungry children, rather than the ascended beings they're supposed to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as for having thousands of years to develop, let's take a look at the Asian cultures. They trace their cultures even further back than the west, and yet they maintain strong, traditionalist values. There is an actual festival in Japan in which the whole city gets together and burns thousands of discarded toys because they're afraid Yokai might possess them and kill you in a fit of rage.<br /> <br /> So just because time has passed by does not automatically guarantee that things will change. Not for mortals, and certainly not for immortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> For the sake of getting my point across, let me depict a hypothetical scenario for you. Let's say that humanity perfects artificial intelligence. A program capable of independent thought, who can learn and adapt to its environment based on past experiences. Now, let's say that over time, this AI decides that it doesn't like the way humanity is treating it, and decides that it wants the power to make its own choices, maybe even establish its own government, or foster its own private agenda. Let's say the AI starts to manifest behavior that is inadvertently harmful to its own well being, or a danger to those around it. What if the AI developed feelings of lust, greed, anger, sloth, envy, gluttony, or murder?<br /> <br /> To put it bluntly, what if humanity created an artificial life form with the same intellectual capacity as a living, breathing human. And now it demands independence, even willing to resort to violence if need be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Would YOU be comfortable giving them free reign, even if it could prove harmful to society in the long run? I guarantee you that the majority of humanity would not. They would view such a creation as a tool. They didn't create the AI because they wanted it to be free, they created it to improve their own lives, and if it seems like the AI no longer wants to do that, then actions must be taken to place it back on the correct path.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity doesn't want a rival. Hell, humanity can barely tolerate its own presence on this planet. So what does that say about the beings who created them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-01-2017, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:17:49-08:00","id":1042125,"title":"","content":"But these gods can and do change; I spoke before about Ares maturing into the more even-tempered Mars, and could talk for ages about reading Sekhmet's relationship with/as Bast as a similar evolution. Acting like the divine are completely rooted in their ways and suggesting that those ways are universally conservative both seem like the pinnacle of hubris and nonsense to me, especially with regards to queer identities and wider social progress. None of the Netjer stepped out of the heavens and slapped Hatshepsut or Cleopatra for being female pharaohs (and I would love to go on about their pantheon having a man without a penis or their queens wearing ceremonial beards), the Theoi are rampantly homoerotic and a good number of Greek myths have transgender figures, the Aesir have a complicated relationship with homosexuality and femininity... the list goes on.<br /> <br /> The World looks enough like our own to be recognizable. If the gods stepped in to correct the course of things when mortals did things that surprised or displeased them, then it be radically different from reality and resemble a bunch of mythological petty kingdoms... but nothing we've seen so far indicates that. History roughly flows the way we expect it to with the occasional extra push from the gods. <br /> <br /> Our own modern day has successful feminism and LGBTQ+ progress already without powerful deities working on their side. If anything, it's harder to see backlash against those in The World than it is ours due to the lessened impact of the Abrahamic faiths on it; a world with less Leviticus and more Theoi man-on-man love does not somehow give us a <i>less</i> gay setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:34:17-08:00","id":1042132,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think I see what the problem is; It sounds like you're lumping all these ancient cultures in together as one big mixing pot and expecting them all to change in the same way. I've never stepped foot outside America, and even I know that is wishful thinking (to put it politely). And you seem to be placing a great emphasis on the idea of homosexuals and women's rights, instead of the slew of other possible changes that may / may not have taken place.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, homosexuality was quite accepted in ancient Greece. I think anybody who's watched Sparticus can attest to that. But that doesn't mean every other culture was shacking up with same sex couples. These are radically different cultures with their own views on morality and spiritual cleanliness.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as for women pharaohs, the fact that they were encouraged to wear manly clothing and wear fake beards proves that they were still sexist. Ruling was a man's position, and if these women wanted to be in charge, they had to pass themselves off as being men. And that hurts your argument even further, because it's basically saying that only gay / transgender females can rise to positions of power. While ignoring the idea of straight women being treated as anything other than subservient brood mothers.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Hell, take a look at Egypt of today (as well as other middle eastern countries) which have largely converted to Islam. Women's rights got blasted straight to the fucking stone age, after that happened. So how can you say that thousands of years would ensure progress after taking a look at the shit humanity is still going through today?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-01-2017, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:34:20-08:00","id":1042133,"title":"","content":"The comments of &quot;Gods might be confused by phones and cars&quot; are somewhat shot in the foot given that there was a preview on the Kickstarter for Relics.<br /> <br /> And two of the three previewed relics were a smartphone and a muscle car, noting that the Tuatha USUALLY gave out war chariots but had to upgrade.<br /> <br /> So clearly SOME of the Divine Forces out there understand that chariots are horseless, and you can talk into a handheld plastic screen to talk to someone on the other side of the World.<br /> <br /> Edit: My point? I don't THINK it's impossible for the Gods to change. Fuck, IIRC, Neall's mentioned that the Nejter writeup was viewed as one big pile of &quot;Oh <b>dear</b>&quot; with regards to attempting to be accurate because in the thousands of years of Egypt's history, the interpretations of the Gods changed considerably with the political environment changing.<br /> <br /> Also, re: Homosexuals - It's a small thing but the Teotl preview mentions Xochipilli is, and very preliminary research revealed that he WAS, the guardian of homosexuals and male prostitutes. There's probably room for LGBTQ Scions getting any number of reactions from their divine parents, including &quot;Wait, what?!&quot;, &quot;Well good for you, Child o' Mine&quot;, and &quot;... Okay? I fail to see why that's worth bringing up. Now go kill a Hydra&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 02-01-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:16:42-08:00","id":1042147,"title":"","content":"For the sake of argument, here's something that would drive change, regardless of the outlooks of the deities; interaction between cultures. Not every pantheon is sexist, not every Goddess a feminist, not every God a homophobe. And people bring ideas from their cultures into others' cultures, which drives new, sometimes heretical, beliefs - sometimes forward and sometimes backward. But in a Scion world where the pantheon are all still active, and bumping into each other, change is inevitable. And <i>that's</i> how you get modern ideas such as feminism, or LGBT rights, or cell phones and space travel. And Gods who perhaps see wisdom in an idea they hadn't embraced before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:54:28-08:00","id":1042164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042060#post1042060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the hell would the gods be more static in a world where they've had thousands of years to change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well social change in reality is largely driven by die-off and generational shifts, not people actually changing positions they themselves hold. A society of immortals would be far slower to change by definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T21:47:41-08:00","id":1042227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042164#post1042164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well social change in reality is largely driven by die-off and generational shifts, not people actually changing positions they themselves hold. A society of immortals would be far slower to change by definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we also know that Fatebinding can change a God's mantle and a God, as Lex mentioned by comparing how Ares was worshiped and portrayed by the Greeks to how Mars was worshiped and portrayed by the Romans.<br /> <br /> I think the preview article for Fate and Fatebinding mentioned that despite not being SHAPED by direct human belief, the Gods do need Humanity in order to help define themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gods don\u2019t need humans, but they do need humanity. Not to exist, not as some kind of source of power, but as a mirror. Humanity and worship are the ways by which the Gods know themselves and, without the ability to relate to and sympathize with humanity, the line between God and Titan blurs to the point of vanishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So under that reading... Yeah, it's entirely believable to me that the Gods will change SLIGHTLY as their worshipers do. Like how in the Theoi writeup, it mentions that Hestia, Goddess of the Hearth, counts among her modern followers many power plant operators and engineers... Because what's a power plant but a hearth that provides heat and warmth to THOUSANDS of homes?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T22:20:21-08:00","id":1042231,"title":"","content":"You're gonna have one hell of an uphill battle trying to convince me that any of the various goddesses of womanhood aren't trans-friendly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T00:58:51-08:00","id":1042269,"title":"","content":"I do agree that, more often than not, the gods would be rather conservative in wanting the laws they laid down for mortals to not change. However, the fact that The World in 2e is basically ours, but a bit more mythical shows that societies have changed. Quite a bit, in fact. All-in-all, I think the answer is obvious; some gods changed, some didn't, and the ones that did change changed in different ways.<br /> <br /> I mean, I could see Zeus happily supporting his homosexual child, but I couldn't see him campaigning for women's rights. I don't think Loki would particularly care about the biological gender of his children and would accept their desire to be something else, but I also don't think Loki would care very much about his children for the most part. Tlazolteotl might be more than willing to tell a Scion that their womanhood doesn't make them weak, but she still probably wouldn't be happy if said Scion brought home her new girlfriend. Ad infinitum.<br /> <br /> So, the gods have changed over time and accept most human rights, but any big social changed would be something that a particularly passionate player character would need to bring about.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, it would be up to the Storyteller to decide exactly what The World is like.. If you want Odin to pat his gay son on the back and say he's proud of him, you can. If you want Zeus to start laughing at their son's confession that they consider themselves a girl, you can do that too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042133#post1042133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, re: Homosexuals - It's a small thing but the Teotl preview mentions Xochipilli is, and very preliminary research revealed that he WAS, the guardian of homosexuals and male prostitutes. There's probably room for LGBTQ Scions getting any number of reactions from their divine parents, including &quot;Wait, what?!&quot;, &quot;Well good for you, Child o' Mine&quot;, and &quot;... Okay? I fail to see why that's worth bringing up. Now go kill a Hydra&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just point out that dear old Xochipilli was also the god of mushrooms, psychedelic drugs and a bunch of other fun things that the Aztecs, for the most part, did not like. He was also an import from the older Toltecs, not something the Aztecs came up with themselves, so that might explain why they had a god of things they thought were bad.<br /> <br /> Like, seriously, they worshipped him because he was still a god and if they didn't give him his blood things would go wrong [specifically all the plants would start dying or something] but most scholars assume that he was something of a joke amongst the pantheon and was treated rather contemptuously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 02-03-2017, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T01:05:15-08:00","id":1042272,"title":"","content":"Something that's struck me in this, is that there's a giant issue with transplanting modern concepts of gender and sexuality on ancient cultures.<br /> <br /> We have no idea what Zeus felt about gay people, because the ancient Greeks did not view sexuality in the terms we do. Zeus being confronted with a gay man by modern ideals is like Zeus being confronted with a cell-phone. He'd need to understand a completely different world to have any idea of what he's dealing with.<br /> <br /> If we assume that the modern concepts of how we think about what sexuality and gender mean in the World exist then the gods must have adapted because otherwise it's the same as if they never adapted to changes like technology or political systems.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that there's a lot of talk about the cultures that inspired the Scion Pantheons, and the assumption that how those cultures felt about these topics is the same as how their gods in the setting felt/feel about them. Human religions are often more conservative than their holy texts. &quot;If you can't eat pig, it's easier just to not own pigs at all, then you never have to worry about eating them.&quot; And certain gods were often very popular in a fashion that could skew things. Thor was very popular at certain points in Norse culture (he's portrayed as being the Aesir that was most dedicated towards protecting humans directly), and probably influenced their attitudes around manly behavior because of it, even if Odin, Tyr, and Heimdall don't really give a shit about those things.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would look at each deity individually. How much are sex and and gender a big part of that god's story and role? When it Tyr every portrayed as caring about what's between your legs or who you like to have sex with? Tyr's about glory in war, honor, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think there's going to be variety among the gods associated with sexuality or gender roles about them. Hera's focus on marriage and motherhood means she's probably more conservative about gender roles than Hestia, Athena, or Aphrodite would be. A goddess that's really big on childbirth is more likely to side on gender essentialism than a goddess that's focused on happy marriages since a happy LGBTQ inclusive marriage is still a marriage.<br /> <br /> Some of the gods are going to care in a way that's probably not LGBTQ friendly. Most probably don't actually care that much because it isn't the part of humanity that they reflect. Others are going to be for such issues because it expands what they're about to more people. The nice thing about Pantheons... is that the members can have conflicting goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T05:29:24-08:00","id":1042355,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042231#post1042231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're gonna have one hell of an uphill battle trying to convince me that any of the various goddesses of womanhood aren't trans-friendly.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They might well be, but then again, they're not the ones in charge of the pantheons, now are they? </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Those who take a realistic look at history will recognize one thing about society: </span></span></span><i>Those in power make the rules.</i><br /> <br /> If morality and equality were objective rights, then every culture in the world would have embraced them over time. But as we all know, that is not the case. There are many cultures who continue to uphold old world, traditionalist values and laws even though they no longer apply to modern society. The passage of time does not guarantee societal change, that falls entirely upon the shoulders of whoever is running the show.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Athena and Artemis are ascribed to being virgin goddesses, but they were only allowed to be so because of Zeus' permission. They did some work for him (forgot what it was) and when he offered them a reward, they said they didn't want to be forced into marriage. And Artemis retained her position by eviscerating any male who attempted to change her mind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In fact, let's take a look at the Kami, their most powerful deity and leader of the entire pantheon </span></span></span><i>is a woman</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and yet their culture still believes that women are supposed to be subservient to men and honor their husbands. And as for the Japanese supporting the idea of gay relationships, I understand that this was only a thing performed between samurai (and pedophiles, at that). I've not heard it referenced in any other part of Japanese society.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042227#post1042227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So under that reading... Yeah, it's entirely believable to me that the Gods will change SLIGHTLY as their worshipers do. Like how in the Theoi writeup, it mentions that Hestia, Goddess of the Hearth, counts among her modern followers many power plant operators and engineers... Because what's a power plant but a hearth that provides heat and warmth to THOUSANDS of homes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't call that adapting to societal changes. They're just incorporating new age technology into their portfolio, which I've already suggested is a possibility. Fire Giants in 1E were using tanks and rifles as they prepared for war.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can have modern technology without shoehorning modern society into the mix as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-02-2017, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:46:57-08:00","id":1042445,"title":"","content":"I see no problem whatsoever with playing a transgender character in Scion 2E. I plan to run one if I ever get the chance to play. Actually, she will be my first trans character ever (I've run a number of cis female characters in other games).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:10:01-08:00","id":1042463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042445#post1042445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no problem whatsoever with playing a transgender character in Scion 2E. I plan to run one if I ever get the chance to play. Actually, she will be my first trans character ever (I've run a number of cis female characters in other games).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We're not arguing over whether or not you can play one. We're talking about how the gods would react to it.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I think 1E gave us a plausible means of bringing about major change to the status quo. Remember that Fate has decreed Zeus is going to be overthrown by one of his own sons. If that son happened to be a modern day Scion, then they could potentially bring their modern day ideologies into the pantheon.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Aesir are also destined to be wiped off the board, and yet two among them survive and begin to repopulate the world. One could argue that with all the old Aesir dead, the next generation implements some much needed change to societal norms.<br /> <br /> <br /> This could also apply to the Aztecs as well. Heck, they've experienced several apocalypses already. Who's to say the next one wouldn't get them to change their ways after they put the world back together a 7th or 8th time?<br /> <br /> <br /> There is potential for the pantheons to change, but not without a significant event that compels them to do so. Nobody likes to change their long held beliefs and traditions. It usually requires something major for them to make that choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-02-2017, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:46:23-08:00","id":1042509,"title":"","content":"Y'know I only just NOW remembered that the Orisha Virtures were said to be Innovation vs Tradition.<br /> <br /> This should be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:43:28-08:00","id":1042531,"title":"","content":"This may be a moot argument, but the gods (at least as far as 1E presents them) are less people and more composite elemental beings, more defined by their purviews and portfolios than any mundane ideas of cultural values. Such a being isn't likely to see the world of man in any other terms other than what their substance entails. Sure in the examples of Hera, Tlazolteotl or the ever-popular Xochipilli there is a specific stake in LGBTQ issues, but in other deities I have to wonder why they would really care at all. If you present Ares with an unfamiliar issue his thoughts will run along the lines of &quot;Is this a form of conquest or battle? No? Then it's IRRELEVANT!&quot; I see a lot of the gods of old looking at these modern issues and thinking; &quot;That's nice, but why exactly does any of this matter to me? or &quot;Yeah, whatever kid. Now go kill me 10 giants, 5 trolls, 2 dragons, and 10 bats.&quot; <br /> <br /> To the issue of traditional values in their respective cultures, I question whether many of those values came directly from the gods themselves or were appended to them by their priests. If there is any constant in religion throughout history, it's that it gets used as a justification for a political or social agenda held by the rulers &amp;/or the clergy. I'd need to see a specific quote from X deity in the Upanishads, Avestas, or whatever to prove that the Yazata (for example) give a damn about whom you are sleeping with. Someone mentioned the Yazata created mankind only to be servants, which sounds more like the Annuna-ki to me but that's fine. If they really did create men to be servants/tools, one wonders what we are supposed to do (or CAN do) for such a being other than deliver up worship. And if that's the only requirement, as long as we aren't raping/killing/lying/stealing or otherwise screwing up, why do they care who we have sex with or how as long as they get that sweet sweet worship?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:52:37-08:00","id":1042535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042531#post1042531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the issue of traditional values in their respective cultures, I question whether many of those values came directly from the gods themselves or were appended to them by their priests. If there is any constant in religion throughout history, it's that it gets used as a justification for a political or social agenda held by the rulers &amp;/or the clergy. I'd need to see a specific quote from X deity in the Upanishads, Avestas, or whatever to prove that the Yazata (for example) give a damn about whom you are sleeping with. Someone mentioned the Yazata created mankind only to be servants, which sounds more like the Annuna-ki to me but that's fine. If they really did create men to be servants/tools, one wonders what we are supposed to do (or CAN do) for such a being other than deliver up worship. And if that's the only requirement, as long as we aren't raping/killing/lying/stealing or otherwise screwing up, why do they care who we have sex with or how as long as they get that sweet sweet worship?</div> </div> </div> </div>Best I can tell, none of the canon 1e pantheons, including the Yazata, claim to have created humans as a slave race. Could be one of the fan pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:56:24-08:00","id":1042539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042535#post1042535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best I can tell, none of the canon 1e pantheons, including the Yazata, claim to have created humans as a slave race. Could be one of the fan pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mesopotamian Pantheon(s) and the Hittite Pantheon are the main contenders in that area. Zoroastianism and the pre-Zoroastirian Persian religious systems are not my forte, but I know for certain that the Mesopotamians and the Hittites perceived themselves as slaves of the divine. The Hittite Gods are especially... bad at dealing with their mortals, frequent attempts at extincting the species by individual deities.<br /> <br /> (As a side, in neither of these cases do the Gods need the worship or belief, they just don't really like the manual labor of getting dressed, farming, feeding themselves, etc. Humanity has to preform these actions, feeding, clothing, cleaning the Gods least they provoke the rage of heaven. The Hittites had a bunch of laws about how to go about this, and big punishments for someone who knowingly, or unknowingly messed up and threatened the existence of the city / empire)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-02-2017, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T13:18:29-08:00","id":1042565,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Manbat, for raising this question. And for approaching it the way you did as well.<br /> <br /> There is probably lots of tension between &quot;things as they are expected to be&quot; and &quot;things as they are in practice&quot;, because well, gods are individuals, and therefore subject to change, while pantheons as systems are all about stability.<br /> So, each pantheon is intimately connected to a culture (in many cases said cultures either died out or changed drastically, but ancient things are more numinous, or feel that way at least). And, naturally, to keep the whole coherent, parts of that whole (individual divine beings) will be forced to compromise a lot. And, since at one point in time they managed to find some common ground and establish certain principles that allowed them to cooperate, oficially introducing new principles or getting rid of existing ones is likely to generate too much internal strife for anybody's liking.<br /> <br /> Which does not mean most (or even many) gods are stuck in the stone age, or whatever detractors imagine.<br /> <br /> Zeus as the patriarch of the Theoi will proclaim that women are inferior to men, yes. But does anyone really think he does not respect Athene? Or would Artemis need official sanction to take revenge for a wrong done to her lesbian faithful?<br /> Ares might just laugh and say that victims of injustice need to &quot;stop crying and take it like adults&quot;, but hey, sometimes it might be the only way.<br /> <br /> Among the Aesir ergi might be srs bsns. But don't expect Odin the allfather to put social norms before efficiency. And the Vanir likely never subscribed to the whole &quot;masculine vs. feminine, dominant vs. dominated&quot; schtick in the first place. They are nature, and nature is much more complex than that.<br /> Loki? Geez, everybody's preconceived notions of &quot;normality&quot; and &quot;appropriateness&quot; are his to play with as he wishes. With Lodur, you're the one who has to keep up.<br /> <br /> The Teotl might represent a culture that had a lot of unreasonable restrictions (and some surprisingly reasonable ones). But they also probably realize that a new epoch/sun demands new approaches, even if Huitzilopochtli is not amused and would like the &quot;good old days&quot; back.<br /> Also, do note that those &quot;good old days&quot; were the days of Nezahualcoyotl and Cuauhtemoc, so not all that is old has to be inferior.<br /> <br /> And no matter how misogynistic Japan used to be (and there still are traces of that, afaik), Amaterasu Omikami still reigns supreme. Nobody dares question her ability, not after that one incident... you know what I mean.<br /> <br /> \u200b Sumerian texts outright say that mortals were created as servants and even slaves for the gods, but that never prevented proud Inanna from falling in love with earthly men, Enki from saving his creations even when it meant going against the decision of the other gods, or Utu from taking an interest in earthly justice.<br /> <br /> Traditionalists that they are, the Devas are still not made of stone, either. Shiva fell in love with Parvati precisely because she is his equal, and Vishnu is happy with whatever helps keep human society, and the world as a whole, healthy, and of course equality of gender, race, varna, etc. does. Why would he object to new ideas that actually help mortals become better and reduce his workload? Consumerism, on the other hand... not so fun.<br /> <br /> And the Tuatha are actually likely to be even more progressive than the average modern European, tbh. Most of them are incredibly dynamic beings, and if sometimes they get too carried away and solve a dispute via decapitation... we could all name a few politicians who could use that treatment.<br /> <br /> Basically, gods are complex. They are neither perfect archetypes who can do no wrong, nor straw bigots who need to be educated by the great and wise modern scions. Inflexible? Sometimes. Some of them. But there might be a better reason behind that inflexibility than &quot;they are self-centered tyrants who would keep humanity under their heel&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1041810#post1041810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The pantheon with the biggest reputation for punishing mortals for the simple crime of being more talented than the gods <i>at anything</i> has just been misunderstood this whole time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hubris is not about talent. It is, at least in theory, about not understanding/accepting your natural place in the grand scheme of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","user":"Xanthias","date":". 02-02-2017, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T13:54:31-08:00","id":1042586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042565#post1042565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hubris is not about talent. It is, at least in theory, about not understanding/accepting your natural place in the grand scheme of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing Devil's Advocate here... IIRC, there's a couple of Greek myths where the mortal in question DOES manage to one-up the relevant God and gets punished for their skill.<br /> <br /> Though only tangentially related... I just imagined Zeus having to be told what transexual or transgender means, because his (biologically male) scion identifies as a trans-woman.<br /> <br /> And when it finally clicks, Zeus's reaction is <i>relief</i>, because of the whole worry that one of his sons will overthrow him, but a DAUGHTER is not a son, so no major danger!<br /> <br /> (Then he might offer to change his daughter's sex to match, because he's Zeus, changing someone's sex is <i>easy</i> compared to turning a human into some kind of snake monster)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:01:04-08:00","id":1042592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042586#post1042586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Playing Devil's Advocate here... IIRC, there's a couple of Greek myths where the mortal in question DOES manage to one-up the relevant God and gets punished for their skill.<br /> <br /> Though only tangentially related... I just imagined Zeus having to be told what transexual or transgender means, because his (biologically male) scion identifies as a trans-woman.<br /> <br /> And when it finally clicks, Zeus's reaction is <i>relief</i>, because of the whole worry that one of his sons will overthrow him, but a DAUGHTER is not a son, so no major danger!<br /> <br /> (Then he might offer to change his daughter's sex to match, because he's Zeus, changing someone's sex is <i>easy</i> compared to turning a human into some kind of snake monster)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also a couple of trans figures in Greek myth already. Caeneus is one of my favorites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:11:40-08:00","id":1042597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042586#post1042586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Playing Devil's Advocate here... IIRC, there's a couple of Greek myths where the mortal in question DOES manage to one-up the relevant God and gets punished for their skill.<br /> <br /> Though only tangentially related... I just imagined Zeus having to be told what transexual or transgender means, because his (biologically male) scion identifies as a trans-woman.<br /> <br /> And when it finally clicks, Zeus's reaction is <i>relief</i>, because of the whole worry that one of his sons will overthrow him, but a DAUGHTER is not a son, so no major danger!<br /> <br /> (Then he might offer to change his daughter's sex to match, because he's Zeus, changing someone's sex is <i>easy</i> compared to turning a human into some kind of snake monster)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which myths/legends do you have in mind?<br /> As for Zeus needing an explanation... he's thousands of years old, even if the term itself is unfamiliar, he understands the concept very well. But the scene you described is entertaining, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:17:52-08:00","id":1042601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042531#post1042531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the issue of traditional values in their respective cultures, I question whether many of those values came directly from the gods themselves or were appended to them by their priests. If there is any constant in religion throughout history, it's that it gets used as a justification for a political or social agenda held by the rulers &amp;/or the clergy. I'd need to see a specific quote from X deity in the Upanishads, Avestas, or whatever to prove that the Yazata (for example) give a damn about whom you are sleeping with. Someone mentioned the Yazata created mankind only to be servants, which sounds more like the Annuna-ki to me but that's fine. If they really did create men to be servants/tools, one wonders what we are supposed to do (or CAN do) for such a being other than deliver up worship. And if that's the only requirement, as long as we aren't raping/killing/lying/stealing or otherwise screwing up, why do they care who we have sex with or how as long as they get that sweet sweet worship?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The reason they created us to be slaves (as I understand it) is that whatever beings created the Yazata (likely the Titans) did so to use them as slaves. The Yazata didn't like that, so they rebelled against their creators, and eventually created humans to be slaves, instead. In other words, the Yazata became the creatures they fought against!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042592#post1042592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's also a couple of trans figures in Greek myth already. Caeneus is one of my favorites.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I remember reading something about Dionysus being a hermaphrodite at one point. But when I brought it up on another thread, I was told that wasn't strictly accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-02-2017, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:22:34-08:00","id":1042603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042597#post1042597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which myths/legends do you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I must have been mixing up slightly with the story of Arachnae, whom IIRC, yes, did boast that she was better at weaving than Athena.<br /> <br /> But the key point I focused on is: She was. She won the contest. She was better than Athena.<br /> <br /> And Athena reacted by turning her into a spider.<br /> <br /> Is it hubris if you can back up your claim and the other party is a sore loser?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:12:42-08:00","id":1042627,"title":"","content":"Hubris means excessive pride or self-confidence (which, let's face it, the entire Theoi are guilty of. Except for Hades). The problem wasn't that Arachnae was better than Athena, it's that she had the nerve to brag about it to everybody she met, until Athena got sick of her shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-02-2017, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:29:42-08:00","id":1042635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042603#post1042603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, I must have been mixing up slightly with the story of Arachnae, whom IIRC, yes, did boast that she was better at weaving than Athena.<br /> <br /> But the key point I focused on is: She was. She won the contest. She was better than Athena.<br /> <br /> And Athena reacted by turning her into a spider.<br /> <br /> Is it hubris if you can back up your claim and the other party is a sore loser?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was she killed Arachne and then turned her into a spider. Did I misremember or is it one of those slight detail changes between accounts?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't being transgender be moot after a certain point? At a certain point either the scion or someone the scion knows can change their physical gender to match. Would there be any fuss at all?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:36:32-08:00","id":1042639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042635#post1042635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't being transgender be moot after a certain point? At a certain point either the scion or someone the scion knows can change their physical gender to match. Would there be any fuss at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every trans person has problems with their genitals if that's what you're trying to say, and even if they were to perfectly pass there's still the stigma around what you were &quot;born as&quot; or &quot;really are.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:46:45-08:00","id":1042643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1041784#post1041784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">d.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Aztecs are another possibility that would not adapt well to the modern world. Their culture had iron clad gender roles and they did NOT approve of homosexuals. Also, they sacrificed people because they believed it staved off the apocalypse. So finding out that human sacrifice is now illegal in modern society probably hasn't improved their relationship.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But what about xochipilli? wans't his job protecting homosexualism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T17:47:53-08:00","id":1042708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042639#post1042639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not every trans person has problems with their genitals if that's what you're trying to say, and even if they were to perfectly pass there's still the stigma around what you were &quot;born as&quot; or &quot;really are.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I seemed to have hit a nerve and for that I apologize. I wasn't trying to say anything. I was simply trying to understand. You have broadened my perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T18:47:33-08:00","id":1042734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042643#post1042643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about xochipilli? wans't his job protecting homosexualism?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't claim to have any knowledge about the Atzlanti beyond what I've learned from here and in 1E. But somebody earlier pointed out that Xochipilli was mocked incessantly by the rest of their pantheon. They were basically the god of everything the Aztecs hated.<br /> <br /> But then again, I suppose if a Scion went onto become a God of baby eating psychopaths, then society would be forced to accept that behavior into their community, now wouldn't they? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-02-2017, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T18:54:24-08:00","id":1042736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042734#post1042734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't claim to have any knowledge about the Atzlanti beyond what I've learned from here and in 1E. But somebody earlier pointed out that Xochipilli was mocked incessantly by the rest of their pantheon. They were basically the god of everything the Aztecs hated.<br /> <br /> But then again, I suppose if a Scion went onto become a God of baby eating psychopaths, then society would be forced to accept that behavior into their community, now wouldn't they? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Drawing parallels between homosexuality being a baby-eating psychopath. Really fucking classy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:00:41-08:00","id":1042739,"title":"","content":"Ouch looks like things are getting heated.<br /> <br /> Well, how about people just do what their players are conformable with and thinks makes for an interesting setting for their characters.<br /> <br /> That's basically all there is too it.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that Neall will eventually come in and tell us what exactly &quot;canon&quot; has to say about Conservative-minded gods versus more Politically Correct-minded gods but fundamentally I think both atamajakki and Nyrufa (who seem to be the main reason this thread has some many pages so far) are right in their assessments, or at very least not wrong, in that the gods are beings that could change for the better or stay the exactly the same as before because telling an all powerful being that their social mores are wrong is pretty hard. That being said, I do hope that Scion 2E doesn't Percy Jackson the gods, for lack of a better term, and wipe away all their negative aspects to the point that they're unrecognizable. Zeus being a serial adulterer is a huge part of his mythos and identity as a god. The same can be side of Shango being a polygamist, Kali being psychotically violent, Dian Cecht being lauded as a hero for committing infanticide, the Deva and Yazata going to holy war against each other. Hell, let's not ignore the fact that many of the gods (sans the Theoi maybe) aren't exactly going to be fans of democracy. These are definitely problematic aspects of mythologies that are thousands of years old, and if anyone wanted to completely ignore them and recast all or most of the gods in Scion as as socially progressive as your typical university sociology professor, than I won't hold nothing against you or Neall if he desires that to be the norm for the game. Sexism, racism, homophobia, transphobia, bigotry towards other religious views (which kinda I of do expect to be a big deal in 2E) aren't things that some groups can or want to deal with.<br /> <br /> What I personally hope for though in 2E is diversity. Some gods are cheering the Women's March in the Overworld, some are contemptuous, many are utterly indifferent, and quite a few just want to destroy the world for no other reason than they can. Again. Looking at you Tezcat.<br /> <br /> That all being, just remember that within the confines of your table you have the opportunity to play however you. So try not to get so hot and bothered about weirdos online who play differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 02-02-2017, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:03:54-08:00","id":1042741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042736#post1042736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Drawing parallels between homosexuality being a baby-eating psychopath. Really fucking classy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im sure he didn't meant it, bad word choice. You still have the right to be offended, but I'm sure it wasn't an intentional attack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:08:53-08:00","id":1042744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042736#post1042736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Drawing parallels between homosexuality being a baby-eating psychopath. Really fucking classy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it's perfectly in sink with the way your argument is going. You're suggesting that just because some new Scions might support gay / transgender people that society will automatically throw away generations worth of prejudice and welcome them with open arms. So if it applies to LGBT and women's rights, then why shouldn't it apply to anything else that society has a history of deeming morally corrupt?<br /> <br /> You seem to have gotten it into your head that the entire world is beginning to support women's rights, and are accepting of the LGBT community. I am telling you right now <b>that is not the case</b>, and if you tried to visit other countries with that idea in mind, you'd be in for a world of disappointment.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can't white wash major changes to society. Don't forget that in 2e, the Gods have been around the whole time. Which means that it is very possible that the church (i.e religion) never fell from power and is still a dominant force in society. Like I said earlier, <b>'Butterfly Effect.'</b> The slightest change to history has far reaching consequences. And if that change to history includes throwing in a bunch of sentient beings, well then they're going to keep adding in their own changes as time goes on and ultimately you're going to get a different version of history than the one we know today.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>Weirdboyz is right, though.the decision is ultimately up to the ST and player group. If you want to play in a setting where society has overcome that stuff, then you can. I, personally, prefer the idea of that stuff being present in my setting. I am sick and tired of seeing the various pantheons misrepresented by modern media of today. They're the reason people think Hades is the Greek devil, and Zeus is some benevolent father!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-02-2017, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:37:43-08:00","id":1042757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042744#post1042744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think it's perfectly in sink with the way your argument is going. You're suggesting that just because some new Scions might support gay / transgender people that society will automatically throw away generations worth of prejudice and welcome them with open arms. So if it applies to LGBT and women's rights, then why shouldn't it apply to anything else that society has a history of deeming morally corrupt?<br /> <br /> You seem to have gotten it into your head that the entire world is beginning to support women's rights, and are accepting of the LGBT community. I am telling you right now <b>that is not the case</b>, and if you tried to visit other countries with that idea in mind, you'd be in for a world of disappointment.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can't white wash major changes to society. Don't forget that in 2e, the Gods have been around the whole time. Which means that it is very possible that the church (i.e religion) never fell from power and is still a dominant force in society. Like I said earlier, <b>'Butterfly Effect.'</b> The slightest change to history has far reaching consequences. And if that change to history includes throwing in a bunch of sentient beings, well then they're going to keep adding in their own changes as time goes on and ultimately you're going to get a different version of history than the one we know today.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>Weirdboyz is right, though.the decision is ultimately up to the ST and player group. If you want to play in a setting where society has overcome that stuff, then you can. I, personally, prefer the idea of that stuff being present in my setting. I am sick and tired of seeing the various pantheons misrepresented by modern media of today. They're the reason people think Hades is the Greek devil, and Zeus is some benevolent father!</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, just maybe, this particular comparsion/argument should be dropped Nyrufa. I don't want to shut you down but atamajakki is understandably touchy about this subject and I doubt she'll back down or agree with your assertions. She's made it pretty clear that idea of any of the female-focused gods being transphobic is a no sell and she's allowed to have that opinion, right. No need to argue when you know its not going to go anywhere.<br /> <br /> Also, by the Gods, I am also tried of seeing Hades being treated as if he's Christian Satan/Lucifer. I mean, syncretism is a thing in mythology but the Hades thing just bothers me to high heaven.<br /> <br /> I blame Disney.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:55:57-08:00","id":1042766,"title":"","content":"I've made my case with numerous examples to support my claims and I managed to do so without ever suggesting anyone play another game or painting a wide swath of a marginalized part of the human race as morally abhorrent, so I think I'm done with this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T20:03:55-08:00","id":1042769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042766#post1042766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made my case with numerous examples to support my claims and I managed to do so without ever suggesting anyone play another game or painting a wide swath of a marginalized part of the human race as morally abhorrent, so I think I'm done with this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's a shame. I was enjoying reading your arguments. I hope you reconsider and come back to the discussion later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 02-03-2017, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T20:09:20-08:00","id":1042772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042757#post1042757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Maybe, just maybe, this particular comparsion/argument should be dropped Nyrufa. I don't want to shut you down but atamajakki is understandably touchy about this subject and I doubt she'll back down or agree with your assertions. She's made it pretty clear that idea of any of the female-focused gods being transphobic is a no sell and she's allowed to have that opinion, right. No need to argue when you know its not going to go anywhere.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also, by the Gods, I am also tried of seeing Hades being treated as if he's Christian Satan/Lucifer. I mean, syncretism is a thing in mythology but the Hades thing just bothers me to high heaven.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I blame Disney.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042766#post1042766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made my case with numerous examples to support my claims and I managed to do so without ever suggesting anyone play another game or painting a wide swath of a marginalized part of the human race as morally abhorrent, so I think I'm done with this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wasn't trying to come across as offensive. Was merely pointing out why it was unrealistic to assume the gods would change their minds over time.<br /> <br /> That kind of rationality might actually work in 1E, since it pretty much says that mortal belief is what shapes the gods. So if mortals believe that stuff is bad, then the Gods would be forced to adapt. But in 2E, that's not the case anymore, so Fate doesn't have an axe hanging over their heads saying &quot;get with the times!&quot;<br /> <br /> Plus, I even gave examples of how the changes Atamajakki wants could have been implemented. It's a simple matter of supplanting whoever is in charge with a more forward thinking individual, at least three pantheons already having a lore friendly method of doing so.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the changes would be impossible, I'm saying they wouldn't happen in the same way it did in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T20:39:21-08:00","id":1042781,"title":"","content":"It's pretty silly to argue that your position is more &quot;realistic&quot; when it concerns the opinions of gods. Ultimately, gods are fictional, and what opinions they would or would not have is a matter of <i>internal consistency</i>, not <i>realism</i>. You can make the gods believe whatever you want them to believe, as long as you can present it in an internally consistent way. And personally, I would rather spend my energy coming up with internally consistent explanations for why the gods might accept LGBTQIA+ people than explanations why they would reject us. We get enough people bending over backwards to justify rejecting us in real life, we don't need more of it in our leisure activities.<br /> <br /> Side note: not to bring cross-fandom drama into this discussion, but this is also my stance on the &quot;biggotry should be more rampant in the World of Darkness because it's supposed to be Darker Than Real Life&quot; argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-02-2017, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T21:43:43-08:00","id":1042802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042601#post1042601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The reason they created us to be slaves (as I understand it) is that whatever beings created the Yazata (likely the Titans) did so to use them as slaves. The Yazata didn't like that, so they rebelled against their creators, and eventually created humans to be slaves, instead. In other words, the Yazata became the creatures they fought against!\\</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you've definitely gotten the Yazata and the Anunna mixed up there, bud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T21:46:05-08:00","id":1042804,"title":"","content":"I figured Charlaquin would come around here eventually. Good to see you.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I suppose this is all a consequence of a much larger discussion as to what Scion is supposed to be about. It is it a game about modern people encountering ancient, all-powerful and perhaps very, very different ideological beings which than breeds an interesting and perhaps disturbing culture clash? Or it an adventure series where valiant heroes fight monsters while Zeus/Shango/Odin/Amaterasu acts as the protagonists cankerous but benevolent mentor figure?<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing that this game can't be American Gods and Percy Jackson at the same time, or that has to be either Grimdark or Noblebright, but I do think that there needs to be some kind of general understanding about where Scion as a game stands when it comes to the Sliding Scale of Idealism vs Cynical. Is it a game where Zeus regularly commits rape by deception, or is he just a lovable lech that can't keep it in his pants? Is it a game where the Primordial vs God War is a mostly unseen conflict that barely affects mortals, or it an apocalyptic nightmare that often gets entire nations wiped from the map? This kinda of relates back to the LBGT acceptance debate in that in a darker game setting those &quot;realistic&quot; issues are probably going to something that I imagine will take up a lot of word space in the Core Book, instead of being perhaps to quickly dismissed as a non-issue in a lighter, fun adventure setting.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Sliding Scale of Idealism vs Cynical could be completely irrelevant if it turns out that Scion is agnostic in what kind of tone it is assumed to have.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, before I can even get a understanding on how the gods would react to modern isms, phobias, and other forms of bigotry I think it would help if we got a confirmation about whether Scion is taking the Aeon route and going with a decidedly optimistic tone. If Scion does goes optimistic it will be interesting to see how Neall makes events and deities like Ragnorak and Kali less grimdark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T22:11:00-08:00","id":1042812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042757#post1042757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I blame Disney.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I was about to note that the 90s movie wasn't the first time that Hades was associated with iconography fitting the Christian Devil, and was going to cite a cartoon from the 30s I remember hearing about that did so.<br /> <br /> I double-checked, and the cartoon I was thinking of was titled The Goddess of Spring from 1934... Which was put out by Walt Disney Pictures. D'oh<br /> <br /> (Though seriously, I wager the practice may have STARTED long before Disney, but the mouse certainly didn't help his reputation)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T22:15:29-08:00","id":1042815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042804#post1042804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured Charlaquin would come around here eventually. Good to see you.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I don't even play Scion! It's like a summoning ritual. Speak of LGBT and she will appear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042804#post1042804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, I suppose this is all a consequence of a much larger discussion as to what Scion is supposed to be about. It is it a game about modern people encountering ancient, all-powerful and perhaps very, very different ideological beings which than breeds an interesting and perhaps disturbing culture clash? Or it an adventure series where valiant heroes fight monsters while Zeus/Shango/Odin/Amaterasu acts as the protagonists cankerous but benevolent mentor figure?<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing that this game can't be American Gods and Percy Jackson at the same time, or that has to be either Grimdark or Noblebright, but I do think that there needs to be some kind of general understanding about where Scion as a game stands when it comes to the Sliding Scale of Idealism vs Cynical. Is it a game where Zeus regularly commits rape by deception, or is he just a lovable lech that can't keep it in his pants? Is it a game where the Primordial vs God War is a mostly unseen conflict that barely affects mortals, or it an apocalyptic nightmare that often gets entire nations wiped from the map? This kinda of relates back to the LBGT acceptance debate in that in a darker game setting those &quot;realistic&quot; issues are probably going to something that I imagine will take up a lot of word space in the Core Book, instead of being perhaps to quickly dismissed as a non-issue in a lighter, fun adventure setting.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Sliding Scale of Idealism vs Cynical could be completely irrelevant if it turns out that Scion is agnostic in what kind of tone it is assumed to have.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, before I can even get a understanding on how the gods would react to modern isms, phobias, and other forms of bigotry I think it would help if we got a confirmation about whether Scion is taking the Aeon route and going with a decidedly optimistic tone. If Scion does goes optimistic it will be interesting to see how Neall makes events and deities like Ragnorak and Kali less grimdark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has to be something individual groups answer for themselves. In fact, it should be something a group decides each time they decide to play a Scion campaign. That's a session 0 talk. If you have an LGBT player, if you have a player who wants to portray an LGBT character, if you have LGBT npcs, and/or if the storyteller wants to explore themes of dealing with homophobia, transphobia, aphobia, etc., that's something the group needs to discuss ahead of time and decide on whether everyone is comfortable with those themes and what everyone's boundaries are. Just like dealing with any other serious subject matter, like racism, sexism, classism, non-consentual sex, or any number of other things that the gods could &quot;realistically&quot; be portrayed as having issues with if the storyteller is so inclined, but have the potential to alienate players if not handled carefully. You have to ask yourself how these themes enhance your story, and you have to ask the players if they are comfortable with a story that explores these themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-03-2017, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T04:41:32-08:00","id":1042884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042812#post1042812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know I was about to note that the 90s movie wasn't the first time that Hades was associated with iconography fitting the Christian Devil, and was going to cite a cartoon from the 30s I remember hearing about that did so.<br /> <br /> I double-checked, and the cartoon I was thinking of was titled The Goddess of Spring from 1934... Which was put out by Walt Disney Pictures. D'oh<br /> <br /> (Though seriously, I wager the practice may have STARTED long before Disney, but the mouse certainly didn't help his reputation)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not only do they depict Hades as being the devil, but they constantly depict the Greek underworld to be nothing but A) Tartarus, or B) An eternity drifting under the River Styx. Mainstream media has completely forgotten about / ignored the Elysian Fields, or the Fortunate Isles!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T06:12:33-08:00","id":1042897,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I have any power over this thread anymore (or if I ever had at anytime), but I didnt wanted this thread to became offensive to anyone. I know homosexuality and transgender are complicated topics, and people are usually uncomfortable talking about it because they never know how to talk about it without offending anyone, so lets just come from the supposition that nobody here is trying to offend anyone. I appreciate everybody who tried to express a his/her opinion to improve the discussion.<br /> <br /> On the topic of Gods changing or not, I think it is obvious they should change, or at least adapt to the modern world, but that doesnt mean much. They would be able to use the technology of the new era no problem, after all they didn't jump from the Ancient times to Now, they saw it all evolve slowly and adapted with it. Obviously would have Gods less high tech (I always think on Demeter on that case, dont know exactly why) but they would be more like a (really old) Grandpa trying to work a smartphone, not like a time traveller. On the opinion side of things, It would change, but it would change with the human opinion. On mythology, Gods are always reacting to the human changes, not creating them. Gods only create things that already exist and are well established (might be that we forgot who actually did, or fate tying Gods to past deeds, or a mix of both) but I dont think Apollo would go on and create a gay-rights campaign in Rome, even if now he would do in Washington. He simply wouldn't do that, mostly because it wouldn't pass on his mind that possibility. I think they should keep their mantles and general concept, but change how they work with them. Zeus were authoritarian, womanizer, cheater and a rapist on Ancient Greece (looking from modern point of view), and still is now, but with a different range of techniques and styles. But some Gods couldn't change too much, or they would escape their mantle. Hera, besides everything that Zeus does, is still married to him. Why? Because she is the Goddess of family and marriage. You can't say she became a defender of women rights when she didn't divorce Zeus, or at least you can't say that without saying she is a hypocrite or have secret plans (The Vengeance of Hera, there is a whole Chronicle on that idea alone).<br /> <br /> And talking about women, atamajakki made a point that women Gods would be supporters of transgender. I need to disagree, because as always, it is a case by case scenario. That would depend, on the God(dess) opinion that is a woman. If she see that a woman is born as a woman (basically have a fully functional womb and female genitalia), then no transgenders allowed. If she see that a woman is have the spirit (or the way of thinking, lets say) of a woman, then transgenders allowed. She might request that you eat a fruit, make a ritual, or start a quest for a MacGuffin that will change your sex officially, even if you dont want. It is all about what she would think that makes a woman a woman: female parts, mind or spirit, attitude, born right. Each God(dess) is a God(dess). And it is all without considering that you will most probably not be dealing with the God(dess) directly, and priests and clerics might have different opinions and interpretations of the will of the God(dess). And is sad atamakakki left the thread, an opinion lost is always a bad thing. She will be missed.<br /> <br /> On Greek mythology, at least, Athena I think would be okay. She wouldn't care much about your gender if you are intelligent and a general good thinker (but I'm not so sure if she would consider him/her to be one of the virgins of Athena). Artemis I don't know. She might only want women born, born like one, but she might have piety of a few transgenders and want to cure their situation (aka changing them to female), and them accepting them. Otherwise, I dont think she would accept on her group. Hera is not a very feminist Goddess on my opinion, but she might deal well with them if she consider adopting a child a way to be a mother. Otherwise, dont think she would give full support, but maybe offer a chance to become a women. -(My opinions on the view of the Goddesses here. If you disagree, please be feel free to express why)<br /> <br /> Besides what is said, Gods dont blast you if you just behave wrongly in relation to their opinions. They dont know, or dont care, about your general personal life as long as you dont rub your face. Wanna be a bottom gay Scion of Zeus, just dont make love in his temple, or him front of his sacred whatever, or scream &quot;Oh My Zeus!&quot; during it and everything should be fine. And dont bring it up while talking to him or on his temple, etc. He will probably know (Zeus is sorta of Omniscient as Lican can say) but he will have more important things to do than blast you to Tartarus. But, if you do something good, something awesome, win an important battle or took the important enemy weapon or whatever that the Gods feel like worth at the time, you now can announce your love on the dinner table and rub it nice and good on Zeus face. He will not like it, but he cant blast you after a victory, and you might gain some points with Apollo. Heck, Hera might like you more if you do that (depend if it is a more sick and tired Hera who enjoy Zeus displeasure or not). The amount of bless and curses you might gain with Gods just for being gay, activist for women rights, for just being a regular women fighting, are very good and interesting. That is why I bring this topic up, I think it work well on the dynamic of growing Gods, from a simple soldier, interchangeable and disposable, to a unique and important general, that people (and Gods) need to swallow their pride to have in their side, to a literal God that can get in arguments with other Gods and opinionated on the destiny of the world. And people opinions on different Gods might bring different ideas of how they work, specially on Gods I'm not familiar with.<br /> <br /> On the realism of the scenario, I dont think it is a topic too worth of discussion. If Gods existed, had powers and affected the world, it would certainly be a different world, but we dont know how. When no even the laws of physics work just fine, how to imagine what would be? It is all about of suspension of disbelief, how much you can accept of &quot;unrealistic&quot; things before saying is too much. Scion is a very unrealistic Game, 1ed even had a small text box about &quot;physics of cool&quot; or something like that. So is a questions of the GM, as always, to decide the world he wants, and as long as the players accept it, it is all fine. Gods always existed, but their actions where hidden or misinterpreted, is all good. Gods never did anything, but due to fate related stuff and processes, many things from the past are now credited to them (like women suffrage or the French revolution), is all good too. All mythologic beings are known and were known, live with us and share our cities and parking spaces, and nobody really cares nor changed how the world is, and the players are playing as &quot;Demi-God Police&quot; solving mundane and other worldly cases, can be a fun game. (I'm imagining an old fat Satyr as the police chief screaming to them because they made some rookie mistake, 80's tv show style). Just decide which world you think is more fun, then deal with it.<br /> <br /> Plus those topics are a good way to differentiate Scion from Percy Jackson. Here the Gods might be really shitty people. (sorry for the bad language, I didn't think in a better term to use).<br /> <br /> To finish, I dont think Neal will come to this discussion. Mostly because is something lengthy and is much more about the GM than the actual game. But would be nice to know if the book will address it, at least on a small table with the general positioning of the Pantheons on different subjects, with special exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:02:28-08:00","id":1042915,"title":"","content":"So, what about polygamy:<br /> <br /> (Just to express the terms before, marriage of 1 man to many female is 1m-f, 1 female to many man 1f-m, many male m-m, many female f-f.)<br /> <br /> Theoi: Officially against it (Zeus opinion would be the official), but mostly at favor of 1m-f. Probably, non officially, open to all kinds. Principal exception, Hera. (if you consider her the Goddess of Traditional Marriage).<br /> <br /> Norse: It was okay to one man have concubines and lesser important women on their houses that they have pleasure with, so probably not a big of a deal for 1m-f. But harshly prejudice to mostly anykind (except for f-f, that might be a God by God case, but seem like they would just consider missing something).<br /> <br /> Egypt: They had Polygamy on Ancient Egypt (1m-f), so they would accept it. 1f-m might be okay too. As far as I researched, no one knows their opinion about homosexuality, so their opinion on other kinds (m-m, f-f) is at GM decision.<br /> <br /> Japanese: It was legal 1m-f prior to 1945 (if my google-fu is working), so it wouldn't even bring much of a discussion. The other kinds however,,,<br /> <br /> Manitouk: The tribes were many, so at least one should accept. Dont know much about them, purely guessing here. (hopping someone who knows better to correct me).<br /> <br /> Deva: 1m-f were accepted, specially thanks to Muslym influence, so should be ok. The multiplicity of ways of Hinduism should accept all kinds, one way or another.<br /> <br /> Tuatha de Dannan: I dont know. I honestly dont know much of them, so no idea.<br /> <br /> Teotl: Seem to be common between the nobility, so, if Scions are by their divine nature nobility, should be okay. Aztec people seem to be very equal right with women, so they should be able to deal with a 1f-m. They arent very nice with homossexuality in a couple case, so many people case would not be very accepted, but the Gods who accept it should accept polygamy in it (as long one the people marrying is somewhat the &quot;husband&quot;).<br /> <br /> Shen: Okay with 1m-f, with different wives on a different hierarchy (bureaucracy even here).<br /> <br /> Orisha: I dont know, I guess might be the same as the Manitouk, but I know even less about African and African descendent religions.<br /> <br /> I imagine if someone asks Zeus about 1m-f he will think &quot;Why someone would want to marry more than one? Just stick with one have sex with the others.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":".  Just add the comentary about Zeus. 02-03-2017, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:09:09-08:00","id":1042918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042915#post1042915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what about polygamy:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was actually about to suggest something like that for Hera. If the laws of marriage are causing her nothing but problems, then as the goddess of marriage, she should just change them to be more suitable to her situation.<br /> <br /> That, or pass her mantle off to a new heir. If she's no longer the deity of marriage, then she's no longer obligated to stay married to Zeus. He can be somebody else's problem, now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:21:16-08:00","id":1042929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042915#post1042915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what about polygamy:<br /> <br /> Tuatha de Dannan: I dont know. I honestly dont know much of them, so no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was probably a practice of Polygamy, but the whole pre-Christian marriage system is very complicated with many tiers of marriage based off social power either partner had. I don't think we can say exactly either way, but in the very least they had a very unique conception of marriage. Kings (there were a lot of Kings, King is a bad translation, better to call them Chieftians to explain how many there were. I think there was 150 by the time of the coming of Patrick and that was very low for Ireland) seem to have been able to have multiple wives, but it is incredibly unclear, and inconsistent.<br /> <br /> So, maybe polygamy, but not at all modern polygamy. The Irish got crazy complicated about marriage, so you'd be juggling that mess. I'd probably say some Scions may be more interested in the ancient systems? Some of them at least. If anyone's interested, UCC's CELT database has a <a href=\"http://www.ucc.ie/celt/women_law.html\" target=\"_blank\">transcribed document</a> on marriage systems. Not primary, and at a glance doesn't seem to contain the oldest stuff, but a middling between Irish and Roman.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Quickly looking around a bit more, <a href=\"http://www.ucc.ie/celt/marriage_ei.html\" target=\"_blank\">This </a>may be more useful for people on the topic of Polygamy for the Irish. It's still Christian period stuff, but pretty much everything for the Irish is. There's a marked presence of Pre-Christian ideas kicking around though. I've not had a chance to read through the whole thing, got to go write an assignment, but it looks decent enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-03-2017, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T09:05:00-08:00","id":1042980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I have any power over this thread anymore (or if I ever had at anytime), but I didnt wanted this thread to became offensive to anyone. I know homosexuality and transgender are complicated topics, and people are usually uncomfortable talking about it because they never know how to talk about it without offending anyone, so lets just come from the supposition that nobody here is trying to offend anyone. I appreciate everybody who tried to express a his/her opinion to improve the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I, a genderfluid transfeminine person who prefers she/her/hers pronouns, have not been offended by this conversation. That said, offending people isn't what you should be worried about. Intent or lack of intent to offend has very little impact on the hurtfulness of words. Instead, you should be concerned with respecting your fellow conversational partners. I'm not going to be offended if someone uses outdated or inaccurate language by mistake, nor will I be upset if people aren't experts on gender studies. But I do expect people to make an effort to respect me, respect trans identities in general, and respect the conversation. So if someone points out that a particular term is offensive, it would be respectful to refrain from using it afterwards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of Gods changing or not, I think it is obvious they should change, or at least adapt to the modern world, but that doesnt mean much. They would be able to use the technology of the new era no problem, after all they didn't jump from the Ancient times to Now, they saw it all evolve slowly and adapted with it. Obviously would have Gods less high tech (I always think on Demeter on that case, dont know exactly why) but they would be more like a (really old) Grandpa trying to work a smartphone, not like a time traveller. On the opinion side of things, It would change, but it would change with the human opinion. On mythology, Gods are always reacting to the human changes, not creating them. Gods only create things that already exist and are well established (might be that we forgot who actually did, or fate tying Gods to past deeds, or a mix of both) but I dont think Apollo would go on and create a gay-rights campaign in Rome, even if now he would do in Washington. He simply wouldn't do that, mostly because it wouldn't pass on his mind that possibility. I think they should keep their mantles and general concept, but change how they work with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to challenge that a bit. Thinking of gods of ancient religions as old-fashioned and therefore hold conservative views on sexuality is imposing modern views on the past. Homosexual sex was actually very common in Ancient Greece, so if anything, modern views on sexuality might seem outlandish and overly restrictive to Apollo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeus were authoritarian, womanizer, cheater and a rapist on Ancient Greece (looking from modern point of view), and still is now, but with a different range of techniques and styles. But some Gods couldn't change too much, or they would escape their mantle. Hera, besides everything that Zeus does, is still married to him. Why? Because she is the Goddess of family and marriage. You can't say she became a defender of women rights when she didn't divorce Zeus, or at least you can't say that without saying she is a hypocrite or have secret plans (The Vengeance of Hera, there is a whole Chronicle on that idea alone).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, she's just ok with her husband having sex with other women (and men, actually).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And talking about women, atamajakki made a point that women Gods would be supporters of transgender. I need to disagree, because as always, it is a case by case scenario. That would depend, on the God(dess) opinion that is a woman. If she see that a woman is born as a woman (basically have a fully functional womb and female genitalia), then no transgenders allowed. If she see that a woman is have the spirit (or the way of thinking, lets say) of a woman, then transgenders allowed. She might request that you eat a fruit, make a ritual, or start a quest for a MacGuffin that will change your sex officially, even if you dont want. It is all about what she would think that makes a woman a woman: female parts, mind or spirit, attitude, born right. Each God(dess) is a God(dess). And it is all without considering that you will most probably not be dealing with the God(dess) directly, and priests and clerics might have different opinions and interpretations of the will of the God(dess).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree that different Gods and Goddesses would have different views on trans issues. One thing we see throughout many ancient religions is that the Gods are people, and many people hold transphobic or otherwise bigoted views. I don't doubt some goddesses could be trans-exclusionary radical feminists. But many would be accepting of trans women as women as well. And since the source mythology doesn't really tell us if Athena was a TERF or not, it's really up to the storyteller to decide those things. Again, if it were me, I wouldn't want to force my players to deal with TERF Gods, unless they specifically expressed interest in that kind of narrative. They have to deal with enough TERFs in real life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And is sad atamakakki left the thread, an opinion lost is always a bad thing. She will be missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't assume she has left the thread entirely. She's probably just not interested in continuing to reiterate the same points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Greek mythology, at least, Athena I think would be okay. She wouldn't care much about your gender if you are intelligent and a general good thinker (but I'm not so sure if she would consider him/her to be one of the virgins of Athena). Artemis I don't know. She might only want women born, born like one, but she might have piety of a few transgenders and want to cure their situation (aka changing them to female), and them accepting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so the idea of transgender being a problem one can be &quot;cured of&quot; by undergoing sex reassignment is very misguided. A trans woman who does not undergo any sort of sex reassignment is still a woman, and a trans woman who does undergo sex reassignment is still trans. Even if we bring Gods and magic into it, transness is a factor of gender, not a factor of sex. It refers to one's gender being different from the gender they were assigned at birth, and genders are usually assigned based on sex at birth. Whether or not a particular God or Goddess holds this misguided view that they can &quot;fix&quot; their trans followers by magically making them &quot;real&quot; men or women is something the Storyteller can decide, but it is very important that this view be clearly presented as misunderstanding of and harmful rob their trans followers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, I dont think she would accept on her group. Hera is not a very feminist Goddess on my opinion, but she might deal well with them if she consider adopting a child a way to be a mother. Otherwise, dont think she would give full support, but maybe offer a chance to become a women. -(My opinions on the view of the Goddesses here. If you disagree, please be feel free to express why)</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a reasonably internally consistent view for Hera to hold; that what she cares about is neither gender nor sex, but motherhood. I like that, it's a cool way to include complex gender issues as a theme in the game, without having to make a God actively transphobic to accomplish it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides what is said, Gods dont blast you if you just behave wrongly in relation to their opinions. They dont know, or dont care, about your general personal life as long as you dont rub your face. Wanna be a bottom gay Scion of Zeus, just dont make love in his temple, or him front of his sacred whatever, or scream &amp;quot;Oh My Zeus!&amp;quot; during it and everything should be fine. And dont bring it up while talking to him or on his temple, etc. He will probably know (Zeus is sorta of Omniscient as Lican can say) but he will have more important things to do than blast you to Tartarus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, that doesn't sound like Zeus at all. Zeus had plenty of man-on-man sex himself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, if you do something good, something awesome, win an important battle or took the important enemy weapon or whatever that the Gods feel like worth at the time, you now can announce your love on the dinner table and rub it nice and good on Zeus face. He will not like it, but he cant blast you after a victory, and you might gain some points with Apollo. Heck, Hera might like you more if you do that (depend if it is a more sick and tired Hera who enjoy Zeus displeasure or not). The amount of bless and curses you might gain with Gods just for being gay, activist for women rights, for just being a regular women fighting, are very good and interesting. That is why I bring this topic up, I think it work well on the dynamic of growing Gods, from a simple soldier, interchangeable and disposable, to a unique and important general, that people (and Gods) need to swallow their pride to have in their side, to a literal God that can get in arguments with other Gods and opinionated on the destiny of the world. And people opinions on different Gods might bring different ideas of how they work, specially on Gods I'm not familiar with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, as someone who is constantly exposed to heterosexual people talking about their sexual relationships, heterosexual couples and heterosexual sex being portrayed openly and romanticized in media, etc. the whole &quot;What you do in bed is your business, just don't rub my face in it&quot; attitude rings <i>very</i> hollow to me. It's just a polite way of saying &quot;I won't actively persecute you for your sexuality, as long as you keep it hidden from me.&quot; And I don't think it's very consistent with the idea of the Gods being distanced and uncarring about insignificant human issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042897#post1042897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the realism of the scenario, I dont think it is a topic too worth of discussion. If Gods existed, had powers and affected the world, it would certainly be a different world, but we dont know how. When no even the laws of physics work just fine, how to imagine what would be? It is all about of suspension of disbelief, how much you can accept of &amp;quot;unrealistic&amp;quot; things before saying is too much. Scion is a very unrealistic Game, 1ed even had a small text box about &amp;quot;physics of cool&amp;quot; or something like that. So is a questions of the GM, as always, to decide the world he wants, and as long as the players accept it, it is all fine. Gods always existed, but their actions where hidden or misinterpreted, is all good. Gods never did anything, but due to fate related stuff and processes, many things from the past are now credited to them (like women suffrage or the French revolution), is all good too. All mythologic beings are known and were known, live with us and share our cities and parking spaces, and nobody really cares nor changed how the world is, and the players are playing as &amp;quot;Demi-God Police&amp;quot; solving mundane and other worldly cases, can be a fun game. (I'm imagining an old fat Satyr as the police chief screaming to them because they made some rookie mistake, 80's tv show style). Just decide which world you think is more fun, then deal with it.<br /> <br /> Plus those topics are a good way to differentiate Scion from Percy Jackson. Here the Gods might be really shitty people. (sorry for the bad language, I didn't think in a better term to use).<br /> <br /> To finish, I dont think Neal will come to this discussion. Mostly because is something lengthy and is much more about the GM than the actual game. But would be nice to know if the book will address it, at least on a small table with the general positioning of the Pantheons on different subjects, with special exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with you on all of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T09:28:41-08:00","id":1042992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042918#post1042918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was actually about to suggest something like that for Hera. If the laws of marriage are causing her nothing but problems, then as the goddess of marriage, she should just change them to be more suitable to her situation.<br /> <br /> That, or pass her mantle off to a new heir. If she's no longer the deity of marriage, then she's no longer obligated to stay married to Zeus. He can be somebody else's problem, now!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure how mantle works on 2ed, but I dont think it would be this easy. As being the Goddess of Marriage is not a title, I don't think she can just pass the mantle to someone else. Is not something like the riddign the sun Chariot of Apollo, that he can train someone else to do. Actually, I would consider she isnt even aware that she is this mantle. She could, at principle, divorce Zeus, but then the Fate would try to force her in hers original place, and if she doesnt come back, fate will find a replacement (maybe a third wife for Zeus), but while she is gone the whole concept of marriage would be shaken over the world, due to her fault, even if she is still trying to help marriages. But you can consider that she might just never had thought of that (or not really considerate) because that is the position she learned a respectable woman of her age should be. She might not like, but is where someone of her position and importance should be, even needing to tolerate what Zeus does. It is how she is, how she was indoctrinated when a child (on Chronus stomach, go figure), what she truly believes is right and correct, even if it is not nice. Or she might be happy with it, as Charlaquin postulated.<br /> <br /> <b>Watcher</b>, thank you for the link on the first page of this thread, that was a very interesting read about different ways of see homosexuality in different pantheons, specially to those that I dont know much. I also found this link <a href=\"http://sourcebooks.fordham.edu/pwh/gayvik.asp\" target=\"_blank\">http://sourcebooks.fordham.edu/pwh/gayvik.asp</a> to what seems to be an article about the topic in Norse mythology, more deeply. On the surface it basically shows their general harsh prejudice against passive homosexuals, but show some more nuances and some historic references.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T09:44:47-08:00","id":1043004,"title":"","content":"Maybe the gods didn't blast individual people (unless they were openly challenging them), but they did respond when society as a whole was getting out of hand. As I said, entire cities were reduced to rubble because they displeased their respective pantheons.<br /> <br /> And then there's the fact that opposing cultures and religions went to war with each other... like, all the friggin time. So even if your native culture is okay with progressive changes to society, there's still the possibility that a foreign power will deem it unacceptable and try to force their views upon your society.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how the Loa would respond to such ideals, since 1E says that they've adopted themselves into Catholocism, but at the same time, they're focused on overthrowing tyrannical oppression (such as slavery) and supporting the community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:04:49-08:00","id":1043014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042992#post1042992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Watcher</b>, thank you for the link on the first page of this thread, that was a very interesting read about different ways of see homosexuality in different pantheons, specially to those that I dont know much. I also found this link <a href=\"http://sourcebooks.fordham.edu/pwh/gayvik.asp\" target=\"_blank\">http://sourcebooks.fordham.edu/pwh/gayvik.asp</a> to what seems to be an article about the topic in Norse mythology, more deeply. On the surface it basically shows their general harsh prejudice against passive homosexuals, but show some more nuances and some historic references.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to help, this topic comes up all the time in our games, so I have a lot of resources on hand for this sort of stuff. Our common pool of players has more LGBTQ people than not, with each of the primary letters, and then some more, so it's a primary topic of a lot of games or characters. In all of the Pantheon Revisions I do, or new Pantheons I am writing (Hittites at the Moment as the first) I am always sure to have a section on LGBTQ stuff, I find the nuisances and differences fascinating and make interesting plot points. For example, the Hittites probably would not care if one of their Scions changed their sex, but would probably have substantial issues if they violated gender roles (they were using a binary gender system keyed into sex). They have a Deity who alternates between sexes, but in doing so is never in violation of the cultural gender roles. When they are functioning as a War Deity, they are always male, when they are functioning as a Love Deity, they are always female. Those little nuisances are totally up my alley, so I find them interesting topics to build characters around.<br /> <br /> I almost perpetually play characters who violate some sort of social system, I find it incredibly enjoyable to have a specific challenge in place, something that I can work with. The aforementioned Anunna Scion, son of Marduk, who was of the stance that mortals were, in fact, people and should be treated with respect and kindness in death is one. But more often I play off sexuality, and specifically gender roles. Reflecting on it, also playing of cultural conceptions of the body pretty heavily. Effeminate, weak Tuatha prophet who self-mutilated ogam words into his bones (shocking the shit out of everyone, including the Tuatha), a bi blind man who refused to carry a weapon, instead purely focused on disarming other people to beat them with their own tools who happened to be covered entirely in burn scars despite having maxed out positive Epic Appearance, that sort of thing. (Edit: I just realized this might not make sense. A warrior without a weapon is a pun used internally such as in the Cattle Raid as a man who has no genitals, or sexual potency. So, by fighting people with <i>their own</i> weapons, that makes a really confusing idea, and then adding to that his otherworldly beauty despite his maiming, it was just a whole host of cultural norm violations. I loved playing him)<br /> <br /> The gay Scion of Thor who can talk his way up and down Yggdrasil, twisting and contorting the Norse logic that forms the cultural position of homophobia into a exaltation of such relationships rather than a condemnation is still on my to-play list. I think I can have him spin some exceptionally confusing arguments on the matter based off their own internal logic and justification, really want to give that a spin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-03-2017, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:13:41-08:00","id":1043016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042915#post1042915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what about polygamy:<br /> <br /> <br /> Deva: 1m-f were accepted, specially thanks to Muslym influence, so should be ok. The multiplicity of ways of Hinduism should accept all kinds, one way or another.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While polygamy is a thing that turns up in stories of kings with multiple wives it's unlikely to have been particularly commonplace in the general populace. Many male Gods and other Divine beings often have multiple wives. That said, what is and is not Polygamy can get kinda interesting in a Pantheon that has such a...<i>flexible</i>, idea of what the Self is. For example, Shiva is married to both Parvati and Kali...<b><i>but</i></b> since Parvati and Kali are the same person, he's still totally monogamous.<br /> <br /> Also, I'll point out that there is at least one example of polyandry in Hinduism...Draupadi, one of the principal characters of the Mahabharata, is married to all five Pandava brothers, through various shenanigans involving past life boons and present life idiocy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:18:05-08:00","id":1043018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I, a genderfluid transfeminine person who prefers she/her/hers pronouns, have not been offended by this conversation. That said, offending people isn't what you should be worried about. Intent or lack of intent to offend has very little impact on the hurtfulness of words. Instead, you should be concerned with respecting your fellow conversational partners. I'm not going to be offended if someone uses outdated or inaccurate language by mistake, nor will I be upset if people aren't experts on gender studies. But I do expect people to make an effort to respect me, respect trans identities in general, and respect the conversation. So if someone points out that a particular term is offensive, it would be respectful to refrain from using it afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I absolutely agree with your approach, and think is the best way to go about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to challenge that a bit. Thinking of gods of ancient religions as old-fashioned and therefore hold conservative views on sexuality is imposing modern views on the past. Homosexual sex was actually very common in Ancient Greece, so if anything, modern views on sexuality might seem outlandish and overly restrictive to Apollo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and Im not imposing that he would find homosexual practice and somewhat more free, but the view of homosexuality is drastically different. We have, for example, the concept of an homosexual, what they wouldnt have in old Greece. In that time was just men making sex with boys, that in their view was female. (or still not complete man). The idea of a man that would solely make sex with men would, specially old men, would be considered very weird, if not meet harshly, specially if that man is thinking in being bottom on the relation, what no man should do because that is what women do. As far as I know, men didnt had sex with other old men, at least not openly. And women with women sex wasnt even considered sex.<br /> But I do think Apollo would consider our prudishness on having sex only in rooms, dressing covering the parts and many other things as definitely overly restrictive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you know, she's just ok with her husband having sex with other women (and men, actually).</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to say, I didnt actually consider that possibility. Mostly because she didnt seem to happy with the situations, specially considering how she treats Heracles in the myths, but she might be okay with it, just not happy that Zeus is giving attention and position to a bastard, or that a bastard is actually achieving something. I think I left my way to see her as a Matrona, old woman of the Gods to blurry that possibility. Thanks for bringing this up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree that different Gods and Goddesses would have different views on trans issues. One thing we see throughout many ancient religions is that the Gods are people, and many people hold transphobic or otherwise bigoted views. I don't doubt some goddesses could be trans-exclusionary radical feminists. But many would be accepting of trans women as women as well. And since the source mythology doesn't really tell us if Athena was a TERF or not, it's really up to the storyteller to decide those things. Again, if it were me, I wouldn't want to force my players to deal with TERF Gods, unless they specifically expressed interest in that kind of narrative. They have to deal with enough TERFs in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is a fair play, and I hope you enjoy it if you ever came to play it. I dont have many friend that would do non-heterosexual characters, so I dont think this would be a topic that would appear much on one of my games, so I wouldnt have a problem in putting in, but I understand tunning it down. It is a game, and it is to have fun after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't assume she has left the thread entirely. She's probably just not interested in continuing to reiterate the same points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope you are right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so the idea of transgender being a problem one can be &quot;cured of&quot; by undergoing sex reassignment is very misguided. A trans woman who does not undergo any sort of sex reassignment is still a woman, and a trans woman who does undergo sex reassignment is still trans. Even if we bring Gods and magic into it, transness is a factor of gender, not a factor of sex. It refers to one's gender being different from the gender they were assigned at birth, and genders are usually assigned based on sex at birth. Whether or not a particular God or Goddess holds this misguided view that they can &quot;fix&quot; their trans followers by magically making them &quot;real&quot; men or women is something the Storyteller can decide, but it is very important that this view be clearly presented as misunderstanding of and harmful rob their trans followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have put that cure in quotes, to really bring up it is purely the potential opinion of a the God(dess). And I need to say that, before ever GMing a game when that topic is going to have a big role I would need to study it more deeply. I'm still not comfortable enough to have a discussion of this topic on my level of knowledge. Actually, I should read more about it right now.<br /> <br /> But it is also very interesting topic too, to imagine how the Gods would react to have this situation, specially if some Scions of a Pantheon are changing to another looking for Gods that can actually understand them. But I would want to be sure that in my game just because a God have bigotry to a group, whatever it is, that doesnt mean he is bad, or evil. Neither a God that is open minded is good. They are just more complicated than that, with flaws and qualities, like any of us, and the players should decided which side to go with. (Another interesting aspect is to put Titans that are open minded facing the close minded Gods. Which side would the Scions choose?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like a reasonably internally consistent view for Hera to hold; that what she cares about is neither gender nor sex, but motherhood. I like that, it's a cool way to include complex gender issues as a theme in the game, without having to make a God actively transphobic to accomplish it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. There is a lot of grey areas that are usually unexplored, and that is the areas I'm looking for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, that doesn't sound like Zeus at all. Zeus had plenty of man-on-man sex himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as a bottom (or passive. Not quite sure what term to use here). Greek mythology was okay with man-to-man action, as long as the man be the top/active and the younger bottom/passive. To Zeus having a male son to be a bottom might be worst than having a daughter. (what I'm still not sure he would like). That is not saying that he couldn't like them, or learn to appreciate them, but as principle he wouldn't like they very much, and if they would start to somewhat humiliated him (or make he feel like it can humiliated him) with potential commentaries as &quot;His seed was not male enough to make a male son&quot; or something that would question his own masculinity, he wouldn't just let it pass. At least in my opinion. Gods, specially Greek ones, carry in what people say about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, as someone who is constantly exposed to heterosexual people talking about their sexual relationships, heterosexual couples and heterosexual sex being portrayed openly and romanticized in media, etc. the whole &quot;What you do in bed is your business, just don't rub my face in it&quot; attitude rings <i>very</i> hollow to me. It's just a polite way of saying &quot;I won't actively persecute you for your sexuality, as long as you keep it hidden from me.&quot; And I don't think it's very consistent with the idea of the Gods being distanced and uncarring about insignificant human issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exact the points. Gods arent uncarring about human insignificant issues. They care about gossip, and how their ego is affected and how other see them. If you are hidding it, or at least not making it too prominent to the wrong people, he will let it pass. To him literally blast you with lighting bolt you need to really piss him off. If Im not mistaken, in Ixios myth, during an Olympus dinner, Ixios (a mortal invited) lusts Hera, what Zeus didnt like. Zeus then illude a drunken Ixios to think he is making sex with Hera, when it was actually a cloud copy of her. When he got back from Olyimpus, and let at earth, after waking, he started bragging about having made sex with Hera, and that is what made Zeus blast him to Tartarus (quite literally). Wasnt the fact of wanting make sex with Hera (and actually think is doing the deed) that makes Zeus blasts the guy, was the possibility of him bragging about having had sex with Zeus' wife.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I agree with you on all of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:26:06-08:00","id":1043022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043018#post1043018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">worst than having a daughter. (what I'm still not sure he would like).</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I'm sitting here totally procrastinating doing a writing assignment, Zeus probably totally loves having daughters more than sons. One of his Sons is Fated to overthrow him, he has no such dangers from a daughter. Although, you can do some <i>great</i> stuff with that narrative with a Trans Scion, while the Theoi do have several figures who move (not always willingly) between Sexes such as Tiresias, I can see Zeus not considering that Fate might be gunning for him from that direction.<br /> <br /> Since Greek Fates are all about, &quot;No matter what you do, you will only bring about your Fate more quickly.&quot; I can see that being a really cool narrative.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:47:31-08:00","id":1043034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043022#post1043022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I'm sitting here totally procrastinating doing a writing assignment, Zeus probably totally loves having daughters more than sons. One of his Sons is Fated to overthrow him, he has no such dangers from a daughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understood it, it was specifically the son he would have with Metis who was prophesied to overthrow him. But since he ate Metis after laying with her and their daughter Athena was born from his head, Zeus was in the clear for ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-03-2017, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:02:34-08:00","id":1043042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043018#post1043018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not as a bottom (or passive. Not quite sure what term to use here). Greek mythology was okay with man-to-man action, as long as the man be the top/active and the younger bottom/passive. To Zeus having a male son to be a bottom might be worst than having a daughter. (what I'm still not sure he would like). That is not saying that he couldn't like them, or learn to appreciate them, but as principle he wouldn't like they very much, and if they would start to somewhat humiliated him (or make he feel like it can humiliated him) with potential commentaries as &quot;His seed was not male enough to make a male son&quot; or something that would question his own masculinity, he wouldn't just let it pass. At least in my opinion. Gods, specially Greek ones, carry in what people say about them.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, one of Zeus' daughters was given the lofty position of 'cup barer' for the gods of Olympus. And she was a legitimate child!<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The blood of two gods runs through me. Surely, Fate has great plans in store for me!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zeus:</b> Be a dear and get daddy another drink, would you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-05-2017, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:02:55-08:00","id":1043043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043034#post1043034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understood it, it was specifically the son he would have with Metis who was prophesied to overthrow him. But since he ate Metis after laying with her and their daughter Athena was born from his head, Zeus was in the clear for ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of gets dicey, it's <i>really </i>interesting! I <i>believe</i> it is because there are several Prophecies running parallel to each other at different times IIRC. Gaia prophesied that Zeus, too, would be overthrown just as his father, and grandfather before him were by his own son. This was done in the wake of the Gigantomachy due to Zeus imprisoning the Giants alongside the Titans.<br /> <br /> Now, what is interesting about this is it allows us to construct a chronology. During the Gigantomachy, Heracles is an important character and Athena is around, therefore we are <i>after </i>Metis being consumed by Zeus. (Metis is his first wife, so it has to be before Heracles is born, since Zeus has to be married to Hera by the time Heracles is born) So, Gaia's Prophecy takes place after Metis' own 'Prophecy' that her son would be mightier than Zeus himself. So, that one is still possibly up and running, Gaia's one that is.<br /> <br /> While this could just be nonsense conjecture, we have <i>another</i> myth (or well play, but it's a mythic play) called Prometheus Bound which has the Theoi going to Prometheus one after another (so this is before Heracles freed him, but after he tricked Zeus) to him on Zeus' behalf trying to get Prometheus to spill the beans, because Prometheus, as the personified force of Foresight knows who the Son of Zeus will be. Prometheus laughs and foils the Theoi through the entire play, and he never reveals the identity of The Son of Zeus even through his daily torture, and then escapes.<br /> <br /> So what we know is there is at least one Prophecy on the topic, possibly two, and they can both be true. Metis, as primordial Wisdom, says that her son will be mightier than Zeus. This is a true statment. Zeus consumes her, and from his head is born Athena. Then when the Giants fight the Theoi, and Zeus tosses them into prison beneath the earth (just like Cronus did with the Hundred Handed Ones, and the Primordial Cyclopses, and as Ouranos did with all of his children) Gaia makes a prophecy that he too will be overthrown by a son of his. So, this continues to be true even after Zeus ate Metis. And adding to this, Prometheus knows who The Son of Zeus is/will be.<br /> <br /> The tricky thing about this is Metis. Since all Fates are true and will come true no matter what for the Greeks, her foresight must be correct. Therefore, she will have a son who is mightier than Zeus. She might not have <i>yet</i>. Just because she was eaten does not mean she is dead, the Theoi don't really die (Pan is a weird exception, Asclepius dies pre-Apotheosis) and they are proven capable of surviving in someone's stomach (Hades and the gang in Cronus). So, she could escape, have a kid with Zeus somehow, and if it's a son, the Prophecy works.<br /> <br /> However, there's another way it can be played. If Metis is inside Zeus, and Zeus has subsumed her entity (which he may have as Zeus becomes an All Knowing figure which he totally was not at the start) then any of Zeus' kids may also be Metis' kids. And since Metis is pure primordial Wisdom, she can probably figure out a way to do this super easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-03-2017, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:05:24-08:00","id":1043045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043034#post1043034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understood it, it was specifically the son he would have with Metis who was prophesied to overthrow him. But since he ate Metis after laying with her and their daughter Athena was born from his head, Zeus was in the clear for ever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fate never specified which Metis would birth his usurper... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:09:43-08:00","id":1043111,"title":"","content":"I heard an interesting idea about Metis' prophecy not so long ago.<br /> <br /> \u200bZeus ate Metis because he feared the child she bore would be the son who overthrows him, yes? What if Athena WAS actually that son? You know......some of the time? <br /> <br /> \u200bThink about it: Athena embodies both traditionally male aspects (War, Strategy, etc.) AND she represents traditionally female aspects as well (Weaving, Household Crafts, etc.) Add her apparent complete disregard for sexual activity and Athena can be a pretty good metaphor for a genderfluid person who is somewhat confused by his/her status. If Athena shifts between male and female aspects, then Zeus should, indeed, be quite worried about Athena if she ever turns a baleful eye his way while &quot;she&quot; is currently a &quot;he.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b(Disclaimer: My pre-emptive apologies if I'm off the mark here about how genderfluidity is or should be represented. My experience with the genderfluid concept is limited pretty much entirely to Alex Fiero in Rick Riordan's Magnus Chase book series.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:34:49-08:00","id":1043121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043111#post1043111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard an interesting idea about Metis' prophecy not so long ago.<br /> <br /> \u200bZeus ate Metis because he feared the child she bore would be the son who overthrows him, yes? What if Athena WAS actually that son? You know......some of the time?<br /> <br /> \u200bThink about it: Athena embodies both traditionally male aspects (War, Strategy, etc.) AND she represents traditionally female aspects as well (Weaving, Household Crafts, etc.) Add her apparent complete disregard for sexual activity and Athena can be a pretty good metaphor for a genderfluid person who is somewhat confused by his/her status. If Athena shifts between male and female aspects, then Zeus should, indeed, be quite worried about Athena if she ever turns a baleful eye his way while &quot;she&quot; is currently a &quot;he.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b(Disclaimer: My pre-emptive apologies if I'm off the mark here about how genderfluidity is or should be represented. My experience with the genderfluid concept is limited pretty much entirely to Alex Fiero in Rick Riordan's Magnus Chase book series.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNow this a cool idea, unnatural1. It actually reminds of a 1E Scion game I was part of back in the day where Athena after getting really tried of Zeus being, well, Zeus, just decides to assassinate him with help of Artemis and Apollo resulting in a huge Theoi civil war with Athena and Ares, whose being supported by Hera and Aphrodite, both gunning for the spot of new Ruler of the Gods. In that scenario it turned out that prophecy about Zeus' downfall was just plain wrong and that any child of the Big Z would one day overthrow him, but the idea that Athena was genderfluid is pretty neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:35:51-08:00","id":1043122,"title":"","content":"I think the issue at hand is a larger one than that of &quot;canon,&quot; which is already fraught when we're trying to subjectively interpret characters and beings whose primary sources are both contradictory and hundreds of thousands of years old; it's bad enough when we're trying to figure out if Het-Heru turns into Sekhmet or if they're different deities that share the same title (and if Sekhmet then becomes Bast or if Bast is her own deity), but when we're trying to establish their opinions on a topic that likely existed at the time but had minimal writing on it. With that in mind, the question is less &quot;how would these gods respond to such topics?&quot; and more &quot;how do you want these topics to factory into your narratives?&quot; and for me the answer is simple: I deal with enough misogyny, transphobia, and everything else in my real world, so I'm in no hurry to wrestle with that in a game of fantasy, especially one that overlaps with my own faith. Anyone trying to say that forcing modern acceptance and morality on the old gods is foolish is doing the same thing by trying to force current conservative (and often rooted in the Abrahamic faiths) ways of thinking onto beings from another age, and is often doing so in a way that deliberately rejects precedent from the cultures and faiths Scion draws from.<br /> <br /> Simply put, <b>I'd rather put my effort into figuring out why the gods would be supportive than why they would not.</b><br /> <br /> The Theoi's signature Purview is that of changing shape, and Greek myth is full of characters changing the sexes of their bodies, to say nothing of the intersex Hermaphroditus. I would ask anyone arguing that Greek homosexuality was explicitly the sole domain of asserting masculine dominance over socially weak submissive tell that to the face of Alexander the Great, who dearly loved Hephaestion as equals, or even offer their prayers up to Roman emperor Hadrian's deified male lover Antinous. Both the Greeks and the Romans not only tolerated but accepted and helped to spread the cult of Cybele/Magna Mater, whose faithful were often self-castrating men who went on to live as women; to suggest that they were transgender in a modern light is imposing modern terminology and thinking on them, but at the same time it's damn hard to argue against something similar happening there. Odin is mocked for her practice of women's magic, but at the end of the day he is the Allfather; if the head of your Pantheon is skirting around traditional gender roles, I see no reason not for that to spread on down to your mortal followers (to nothing of how fluid Loki is).<br /> <br /> I see no reason to suggest that any goddess of womanhood would be some sort of TERF or biological essentialist; if anything, I would suggest the divine would be more capable of seeing inherent womanhood, not less. They are there as patrons and guardians of all women, and I don't feel like any argument to the contrary has solid ground to stand on other than some cruel need to see transphobia reflected in the media they consume.<br /> <br /> EDIT: (In the name of disclosure and to justify why this thread has made me so heated, I'm a transgender woman who leans pretty heavily on Egyptian paganism to keep me going. This is less an academic debate to me and more people trying to argue to me just why transphobia has a place in a game I love and among gods I worship, and I'm not really ever going to stand for that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:36:35-08:00","id":1043124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042603#post1042603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, I must have been mixing up slightly with the story of Arachnae, whom IIRC, yes, did boast that she was better at weaving than Athena.<br /> <br /> But the key point I focused on is: She was. She won the contest. She was better than Athena.<br /> <br /> And Athena reacted by turning her into a spider.<br /> <br /> Is it hubris if you can back up your claim and the other party is a sore loser?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have my copy of Ovid right now, but afair his version goes like this:<br /> Arakhne is so proud of her skill, that when people suggest Pallas herself taught her weaving, the girl is angry and implies the goddess has nothing on her.<br /> Athene appears as an old woman and tries to talk some sense into her.<br /> Arakhne is very rude to the old lady.<br /> Athene reveals her identity. Arakhne is not much humbled, contest ensues.<br /> Athene's work glorifies the gods and reminds of mortals punished for hubris before Arakhne. The girl basically weaves the first political cartoon, humiliating Zeus, Athene's father, in particular.<br /> Athene, outraged, destroys the beautiful, but offensive, work.<br /> Arakhne hangs herself.<br /> Then the goddess turns her into a spider (or, more precisely, the prototypical arachnid).<br /> Surely, the punishment is worse than the crime, but the hubris is pretty evident, and part of the punishment is Arakhne's own doing.<br /> Just like with Pentheus and Niobe, Arakhne blatantly disrespects the gods who did her no wrong, and it is her own pride that turns her encounter with the divine into a tragedy. At first, Athene sets out to teach, not to kill.<br /> Now, it is easy to empathise with rebelliousness. Those possessing authority abuse it so often, and many gods are no exception. Of course those who have the courage to challenge the powerful are admirable for that courage. But they are not always in the right. And authority figures sometimes do know better (I know, hard to imagine with the way most modern politicians are, but still true.) Basic respect when dealing with the matron of her chosen craft would have saved the unhappy weaver girl. And many other badass but stupid figures as well.<br /> <br /> The gods can be temperamental. The gods can be petty, jealous, angry. So can humans. What else is new?<br /> <br /> Also, the idea that Arakhne's beautiful mockery or Marsyas' wild music are objectively superior (or even equal) to the art of Athene or Apollo is too simplistic. We should take note of the the actual substance of their respective works in addition to the pleasing form. When wildness and chaos contend with order and harmony, both sides seem enchanting. Neither wins. Not for long, anyway. And for the ancients, chaos was much more immediately threatening, because they had much less control over their environment than we do. So, perhaps the presumption of those who would challenge the Olympians was not as harmless as it may seem to a modern human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043043#post1043043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While this could just be nonsense conjecture, we have <i>another</i> myth (or well play, but it's a mythic play) called Prometheus Bound which has the Theoi going to Prometheus one after another (so this is before Heracles freed him, but after he tricked Zeus) to him on Zeus' behalf trying to get Prometheus to spill the beans, because Prometheus, as the personified force of Foresight knows who the Son of Zeus will be. Prometheus laughs and foils the Theoi through the entire play, and he never reveals the identity of The Son of Zeus even through his daily torture, and then escapes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's the child Thetis would have given birth to had Zeus pursued her. That's why the gods were so eager to give Thetis in marriage to Peleus.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","user":"Xanthias","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:54:22-08:00","id":1043136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043124#post1043124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIt's the child Thetis would have given birth to had Zeus pursued her. That's why the gods were so eager to give Thetis in marriage to Peleus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yeah, that sounds familiar. I am admittedly terrible at the plays unless I have them right in front of me. I have no idea why, the nitty gritty just refuses to stick in my head. I almost feel like it might be the formatting, or at least the format I originally read them in.<br /> <br /> But, we can still see from that Zeus has that Fate looming over him, Fate's just looking for a mother at this point it sounds like. A Son of Zeus story is something I have wanted to run for a while now, it's sort of the 'big established story' from Mythology next to Ragnarok in my mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043124#post1043124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAlso, the idea that Arakhne's beautiful mockery or Marsyas' wild music are objectively superior (or even equal) to the art of Athene or Apollo is too simplistic. We should take note of the the actual substance of their respective works in addition to the pleasing form. When wildness and chaos contend with order and harmony, both sides seem enchanting. Neither wins. Not for long, anyway. And for the ancients, chaos was much more immediately threatening, because they had much less control over their environment than we do. So, perhaps the presumption of those who would challenge the Olympians was not as harmless as it may seem to a modern human.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a <i>really good</i> way to explain that, I just had to chime in here. The Chaos - Order situation is something we tend to have a very hard time grasping, really well exemplified by our modern conception of Chaos being all about randomness, such as the old 1e Chaos Purview was based around. To the ancient world, Chaos was more of a societal thing, or natural thing. The sun breaking it's pattern, that's chaos. A king who is unjust (for the Irish, many cultures have a king=law thing so the king can't be unjust) is chaos. Killing a king is chaos, etc. No one wanted to take the risk of their city or town falling into strife without any local authority.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:07:33-08:00","id":1043173,"title":"","content":"Can we really say that Odin's magical abilities were 'womanly' though? The dude sacrificed an eye and crucified himself for 9 days (which he <b>survived</b>) to obtain the power he wielded. Sounds like a champion of masculinity, to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> And just as I was writing this, I realized something: Tyr lost his position as All Father when he sacrificed his hand to Fenrir, yet Odin was allowed to maintain his status after sacrificing an eye?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> As for a Zeus usurpation story, that's also one I've been interested in for a while. But the question is whether or not the child would use their power to change things for the better, or if they'd allow their new power to corrupt them. I mean, Zeus, Chronos, and Oceanus didn't exactly have the best reputations. Who's to say the next one won't go full on Sith Lord and cast down Zeus so he can wield ultimate power? Especially since Greek mythology has a raging hard on for tragedies!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Now I'm actually curious to see what Chronos would be like as a Greater Titan of Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-03-2017, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:39:10-08:00","id":1043196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043173#post1043173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we really say that Odin's magical abilities were 'womanly' though? The dude sacrificed an eye and crucified himself for 9 days (which he <b>survived</b>) to obtain the power he wielded. Sounds like a champion of masculinity, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seidr was often stigmatized for a feminine association, yes. That's the whole reason Loki mocks Odin for his magics.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't say pain or sacrifice is inherently masculine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:39:30-08:00","id":1043197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043173#post1043173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we really say that Odin's magical abilities were 'womanly' though? The dude sacrificed an eye and crucified himself for 9 days (which he <b>survived</b>) to obtain the power he wielded. Sounds like a champion of masculinity, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different magic. That was for the Runic Magic he has, Seidr is different. Like, cosmologically I guess? The Runes are more like individual Knacks or Boons mechanics wise.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:55:43-08:00","id":1043206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043173#post1043173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a Zeus usurpation story, that's also one I've been interested in for a while. But the question is whether or not the child would use their power to change things for the better, or if they'd allow their new power to corrupt them. I mean, Zeus, Chronos, and Oceanus didn't exactly have the best reputations. Who's the say the next one won't go full on Sith Lord and cast down Zeus so he can wield ultimate power? Especially since Greek mythology has a raging hard on for tragedies!</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree that the Greeks really love their cyclical issues. The Son of Zeus would probably be faced with that same decision of, &quot;Do you imprison your family?&quot; and if they do, well then, you will be cursed by Gaia too! It makes it really interesting, the only way to break the pattern is to <i>not</i> imprison the generation you overthrow. So, you would overthrow Zeus, but not imprison him (also technically can't kill him since the Theoi are theoretically True Immortal)<br /> <br /> Oh, also, random other thing. Chronos is not Zeus' father. Cronus is Zeus' father. Cronus is sort of your standard Fertility entity, abundance, whatnot. It gets totally confused I believe in the Victorian period, it's why Cronus is running around with a sickle, harvest and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Edit: Holy crap these posts both came off as super snippy, I'm really sorry! I was just quickly tossing up posts while running errands and they came off totally rude, I apologie a ton Nyrufa! I'm astonishingly terrible at communicating frequently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-03-2017, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:05:42-08:00","id":1043216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043206#post1043206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, also, random other thing. Chronos is not Zeus' father. Cronus is Zeus' father. Cronus is sort of your standard Fertility entity, abundance, whatnot. It gets totally confused I believe in the Victorian period, it's why Cronus is running around with a sickle, harvest and whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? I just thought they were the same thing but spelled differently. Looking at the names themselves, it seems like they'd be pronounced identically.<br /> <br /> <br /> And sure, there's a way to overthrow Zeus without imprisoning or killing him... Though Zeus would probably be wishing for death if you decided to go that route.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043196#post1043196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seidr was often stigmatized for a feminine association, yes. That's the whole reason Loki mocks Odin for his magics.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't say pain or sacrifice is inherently masculine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, because anybody gives a shit what Loki has to say on the use of magic! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-03-2017, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:22:48-08:00","id":1043228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043216#post1043216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sure, there's a way to overthrow Zeus without imprisoning or killing him... Though Zeus would probably be wishing for death if you decided to go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Zeus, go to your room! Without dinner, and <i>no floozies!</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;YOU'RE A MONSTER!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:27:54-08:00","id":1043230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043228#post1043228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Zeus, go to your room! Without dinner, and <i>no floozies!</i>&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;YOU'RE A MONSTER!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I think the cycle of usurpation usually involves getting castrated, so I can Zeus' reluctance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:33:07-08:00","id":1043236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043228#post1043228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Zeus, go to your room! Without dinner, and <i>no floozies!</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;YOU'RE A MONSTER!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Was personally thinking of castrating him... I mean, it happened to the last two rulers!<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043230#post1043230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I think the cycle of usurpation usually involves getting castrated, so I can Zeus' reluctance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:33:16-08:00","id":1043268,"title":"","content":"I'm a chronic smartass who's nowhere near as witty as he thinks he is. Snark and making light of certain situations is kind of what I do. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T01:08:37-08:00","id":1043412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042804#post1042804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Scion does goes optimistic it will be interesting to see how Neall makes events and deities like Ragnorak and Kali less grimdark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, who and Kali? I have no idea who you're talking about, because you surely couldn't be confusing the event, Ragnarok, for a deity could you? Because that would be an incredibly silly mistake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1042980#post1042980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I, a genderfluid transfeminine person who prefers she/her/hers pronouns, have not been offended by this conversation. That said, offending people isn't what you should be worried about. Intent or lack of intent to offend has very little impact on the hurtfulness of words. Instead, you should be concerned with respecting your fellow conversational partners. I'm not going to be offended if someone uses outdated or inaccurate language by mistake, nor will I be upset if people aren't experts on gender studies. But I do expect people to make an effort to respect me, respect trans identities in general, and respect the conversation. So if someone points out that a particular term is offensive, it would be respectful to refrain from using it afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems very logical and reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going to challenge that a bit. Thinking of gods of ancient religions as old-fashioned and therefore hold conservative views on sexuality is imposing modern views on the past. Homosexual sex was actually very common in Ancient Greece, so if anything, modern views on sexuality might seem outlandish and overly restrictive to Apollo. </div> </div> </div>That was true of the Greeks, but as has already been mentioned there are at least two pantheons in Scion whose cultures didn't like homosexuality. I'm not arguing against this, just pointing out the fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, you know, she's just ok with her husband having sex with other women (and men, actually). </div> </div> </div>But... she wasn't. She was very specifically furious about it in the myths, she was just unable to punish Zeus due to him being so much stronger than basically everyone else in the pantheon. The fact that she then punished the people he slept with is what tends to make most people lose sympathy for her.<br /> <br /> I feel like it's worth noting that there was at least one occasion where Zeus did sleep with a guy. The fact that said guy [Ganymede] was a young boy [as far as I remember, anyway] is pretty unfortunate though. It's one of the times were Zeus saved his lover from Hera's punishment, though, so that's cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't disagree that different Gods and Goddesses would have different views on trans issues. One thing we see throughout many ancient religions is that the Gods are people, and many people hold transphobic or otherwise bigoted views. I don't doubt some goddesses could be trans-exclusionary radical feminists. But many would be accepting of trans women as women as well. And since the source mythology doesn't really tell us if Athena was a TERF or not, it's really up to the storyteller to decide those things. Again, if it were me, I wouldn't want to force my players to deal with TERF Gods, unless they specifically expressed interest in that kind of narrative. They have to deal with enough TERFs in real life. </div> </div> </div>This is basically my opinion on the whole matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't assume she has left the thread entirely. She's probably just not interested in continuing to reiterate the same points. </div> </div> </div>No comment on this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, so the idea of transgender being a problem one can be &quot;cured of&quot; by undergoing sex reassignment is very misguided. A trans woman who does not undergo any sort of sex reassignment is still a woman, and a trans woman who does undergo sex reassignment is still trans. Even if we bring Gods and magic into it, transness is a factor of gender, not a factor of sex. It refers to one's gender being different from the gender they were assigned at birth, and genders are usually assigned based on sex at birth. Whether or not a particular God or Goddess holds this misguided view that they can &quot;fix&quot; their trans followers by magically making them &quot;real&quot; men or women is something the Storyteller can decide, but it is very important that this view be clearly presented as misunderstanding of and harmful rob their trans followers. </div> </div> </div>I will note that magic would make it easy for someone to change their sex, though, as was demonstrated by a character in 1e. Said character wasn't an awfuly good representation of transgenders on the whole, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That seems like a reasonably internally consistent view for Hera to hold; that what she cares about is neither gender nor sex, but motherhood. I like that, it's a cool way to include complex gender issues as a theme in the game, without having to make a God actively transphobic to accomplish it. </div> </div> </div>No comment on this one, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Man, that doesn't sound like Zeus at all. Zeus had plenty of man-on-man sex himself. </div> </div> </div>I only know of the one example I mentioned earlier. How many others were there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, as someone who is constantly exposed to heterosexual people talking about their sexual relationships, heterosexual couples and heterosexual sex being portrayed openly and romanticized in media, etc. the whole &quot;What you do in bed is your business, just don't rub my face in it&quot; attitude rings <i>very</i> hollow to me. It's just a polite way of saying &quot;I won't actively persecute you for your sexuality, as long as you keep it hidden from me.&quot; And I don't think it's very consistent with the idea of the Gods being distanced and uncarring about insignificant human issues. </div> </div> </div>Another 'no comment' from me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I agree with you on all of this. </div> </div> </div>Same here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 02-04-2017, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T02:12:30-08:00","id":1043429,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 02-04-2017, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T02:17:36-08:00","id":1043431,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go my entire life explaining to people that not every trans person wants a sex change, aren't I?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T02:21:34-08:00","id":1043432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043431#post1043431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go my entire life explaining to people that not every trans person wants a sex change, aren't I?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're saying that because of me, then the answer is no. I am very much aware of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T06:05:06-08:00","id":1043502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043412#post1043412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, who and Kali? I have no idea who you're talking about, because you surely couldn't be confusing the event, Ragnarok, for a deity could you? Because that would be an incredibly silly mistake.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think he meant 'An event like Raganarok or a deity like Kali'.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1675_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1675\" data-vbnamecard=\"1675\">Weirdboyz</a> : I'm not sure if you count this as de-grimdarkifying, but Kali has long been considered an all-loving Mother Goddess by many strains of Hinduism. So Neall wouldn't need to <i>make</i> any real changes to how she's perceived by a majority of Hindus anyway. He'd have to go the other way to make her just a Warrior and nothing else instead of the Warrior Guardian Liminal/Sage type being she actually is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:41:22-08:00","id":1043613,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Samudra. My grammar isn't always great, but that was essentially want I was trying to get across.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, I probably should have figured that there were other renditions of Kali in Hinduism that played up more positive aspects. Thanks for the info.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:15:19-08:00","id":1043673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043136#post1043136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But, we can still see from that Zeus has that Fate looming over him, Fate's just looking for a mother at this point it sounds like. A Son of Zeus story is something I have wanted to run for a while now, it's sort of the 'big established story' from Mythology next to Ragnarok in my mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is a <i>really good</i> way to explain that, I just had to chime in here. The Chaos - Order situation is something we tend to have a very hard time grasping, really well exemplified by our modern conception of Chaos being all about randomness, such as the old 1e Chaos Purview was based around. To the ancient world, Chaos was more of a societal thing, or natural thing. The sun breaking it's pattern, that's chaos. A king who is unjust (for the Irish, many cultures have a king=law thing so the king can't be unjust) is chaos. Killing a king is chaos, etc. No one wanted to take the risk of their city or town falling into strife without any local authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>* Zeus and Fate: I guess one could say he can not completely get rid of the fate of being overthrown because that fate is part of his nature. Zeus is Zeus, and as long as he behaves in a zeus-like manner, as long as he stays true to himself, eventually his own actions will inevitably cause his downfall. Like a proper Greek tragedy. But, since Zeus, for all his faults, is a better ruler than his predecessors, he's not as thoroughly doomed as they were. <br /> <br /> * Chaos and order: thank you, this angle could really use more discussion. But I guess, considering the way tyrants were viewed by many in ancient Hellas, the fall of a ruler would actually represent the restoration of proper order to them. Even a benevolent &quot;monarch&quot; lives constantly aware of a sword hanging above his head. And in Ireland, the Sovereignty Goddess knows full well when a &quot;king&quot; (chieftain, rather) becomes unfit for his position, and easily dumps him for another. What is disruptive is actually a ruler who refuses to submit to this cycle. I would argue that the tension between a desire for safety and stability vs. a desire for self-expression and freedom is impossible to fully resolve on a cultural level, but different civilizations occasionally will value one over the other (temporarily). An unjust ruler is still better than no ruler/foreign ruler in Kemetic or Babylonian political culture, but not for a proud Norse bondi or for Athenian citizens in the age of Perikles. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043216#post1043216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, because anybody gives a shit what Loki has to say on the use of magic! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Everybody who has the slightest idea of who Loki is &quot;gives a shit&quot;. This is a being who, most likely, took part in the creation of humanity, peerless shape shifter, traveler between all the worlds, and if there are secrets Odin, Angrboda and Freyja have managed to keep from him, those are few and far between. Why would he not know what he's talking about?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T14:53:59-08:00","id":1043742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043673#post1043673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Everybody who has the slightest idea of who Loki is &quot;gives a shit&quot;. This is a being who, most likely, took part in the creation of humanity, peerless shape shifter, traveler between all the worlds, and if there are secrets Odin, Angrboda and Freyja have managed to keep from him, those are few and far between. Why would he not know what he's talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You misunderstand; I was drawing attention to the fact he was mocking Odin for the use of magic when Loki's own reputation is no better than his.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T15:14:10-08:00","id":1043748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043742#post1043742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You misunderstand; I was drawing attention to the fact he was mocking Odin for the use of magic when Loki's own reputation is no better than his.</div> </div> </div> </div>Context is important. Loki is mocking Odin for using traditionally feminine magic, seidr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T17:04:47-08:00","id":1043775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043748#post1043748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Context is important. Loki is mocking Odin for using traditionally feminine magic, seidr.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To which Odin could smugly reply <i>&quot;How's it feel being a mom?&quot;</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T17:12:03-08:00","id":1043777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043775#post1043775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To which Odin could smugly reply <i>&quot;How's it feel being a mom?&quot;</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And then you try and tell me they wouldn't be down with nonstandard gender roles...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T17:42:42-08:00","id":1043781,"title":"","content":"Indeed, there is at least one story where Loki turns into a mare in heat in order to help Thor steal a stallion as part of a convoluted plan to cheat some giant contractors out of a bonus for doing the job quickly and the stallion winds up knocking Loki up and they give birth to a super horse with a bunch of legs.<br /> <br /> So Loki really doesn't get to bash someone else for using feminine magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T17:43:31-08:00","id":1043782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043777#post1043777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then you try and tell me they wouldn't be down with nonstandard gender roles...</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The Viking gods probably realized they were being hypocrites and became more accepting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T21:24:49-08:00","id":1043851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043018#post1043018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I need to say, I didnt actually consider that possibility. Mostly because she didnt seem to happy with the situations, specially considering how she treats Heracles in the myths, but she might be okay with it, just not happy that Zeus is giving attention and position to a bastard, or that a bastard is actually achieving something. I think I left my way to see her as a Matrona, old woman of the Gods to blurry that possibility. Thanks for bringing this up.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that I think should be considered is the possibility that the myths people tell aren't necessarily the way events actually happened. People tell the tales of Herakles and claim that Hera hated him and tormented him, and they assume that it is because she was jealous of Zeus's tryst with his mother. What if that's the wrong assumption? Looking to the prophecy that has been brought up a few times already, what if Hera fears that Herakles was the one? She could very well have been trying to interfere with Herakles in the hopes of denying him the opportunity to overthrow her husband. Through that lens, a lot of her jealousy could be explained away as her being angry with her husband for taking stupid chances. If someone had a prophecy hanging over his head that said that he'd die by falling from a great height, his wife would probably be pretty upset if he wouldn't stop skydiving. That could be a similar scenario. If you're going to have a kid overthrow you, why would you want to sow a bunch of wild oats and risk having a lot of them that could fulfill it?<br /> <br /> Another possibility for Hera's treatment of Herakles could be the simple desire to see him achieve godhood and join the rest of the Theoi. The struggles she put him through did help drive him to apotheosis, so one could argue that she was &quot;power-leveling&quot; him so that they'd have another strong warrior among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T22:08:49-08:00","id":1043860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043851#post1043851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that I think should be considered is the possibility that the myths people tell aren't necessarily the way events actually happened. People tell the tales of Herakles and claim that Hera hated him and tormented him, and they assume that it is because she was jealous of Zeus's tryst with his mother. What if that's the wrong assumption? Looking to the prophecy that has been brought up a few times already, what if Hera fears that Herakles was the one? She could very well have been trying to interfere with Herakles in the hopes of denying him the opportunity to overthrow her husband. Through that lens, a lot of her jealousy could be explained away as her being angry with her husband for taking stupid chances. If someone had a prophecy hanging over his head that said that he'd die by falling from a great height, his wife would probably be pretty upset if he wouldn't stop skydiving. That could be a similar scenario. If you're going to have a kid overthrow you, why would you want to sow a bunch of wild oats and risk having a lot of them that could fulfill it?<br /> <br /> Another possibility for Hera's treatment of Herakles could be the simple desire to see him achieve godhood and join the rest of the Theoi. The struggles she put him through did help drive him to apotheosis, so one could argue that she was &quot;power-leveling&quot; him so that they'd have another strong warrior among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bVery intriguing theory. I think I'll adopt this as my new headcanon, because frankly I really like the idea that Zeus and Hera actually do love each other. I have this idea that the Olympians actually are more frightened of the times when Zeus and Hera AREN'T fighting and are on the same page. Basically? If you walk into Zeus' throne room and Hera's storming off in a huff? At least you only have to worry about placating Zeus. If you go into the throne room and see Hera and Zeus being all snuggly with each other and taking turns feeding each other grapes? Oh, crap! One wrong word that offends EITHER one of them, and you're soooooo screwed!<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd in support of your theory? It just occurred to me that Hera ONLY ever seems interested in punishing Zeus' MALE children. Think about it: the guy's got daughters sprinkled all throughout Greek myth. And yet? Hera never seemed to target ANY of them or their mothers. It's almost like Hera doesn't consider them threats or something.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd as far as Hera making life Hell for Herakles? Yeah, that fits too. The whole point of Legend, as defined by Scion, is that the more difficult your life, the better your chances of building your Legend and rising to godhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T22:17:46-08:00","id":1043863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043777#post1043777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then you try and tell me they wouldn't be down with nonstandard gender roles...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One again, Loki <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">was raped </span></b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">by a horse.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">I could bring up a decades old argument about how that would portray gay rights in a negative light, but that would come across as being incredibly bigoted.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-05-2017, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:02:56-08:00","id":1043985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043851#post1043851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that I think should be considered is the possibility that the myths people tell aren't necessarily the way events actually happened. People tell the tales of Herakles and claim that Hera hated him and tormented him, and they assume that it is because she was jealous of Zeus's tryst with his mother. What if that's the wrong assumption? Looking to the prophecy that has been brought up a few times already, what if Hera fears that Herakles was the one? She could very well have been trying to interfere with Herakles in the hopes of denying him the opportunity to overthrow her husband. Through that lens, a lot of her jealousy could be explained away as her being angry with her husband for taking stupid chances. If someone had a prophecy hanging over his head that said that he'd die by falling from a great height, his wife would probably be pretty upset if he wouldn't stop skydiving. That could be a similar scenario. If you're going to have a kid overthrow you, why would you want to sow a bunch of wild oats and risk having a lot of them that could fulfill it?<br /> <br /> Another possibility for Hera's treatment of Herakles could be the simple desire to see him achieve godhood and join the rest of the Theoi. The struggles she put him through did help drive him to apotheosis, so one could argue that she was &quot;power-leveling&quot; him so that they'd have another strong warrior among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a way to go in a game, but I think it might be trick. I mean, if you decide to say that some elements of the legends are not true because they are incomplete or incorrect, this can potentially change all mythology, everywhere. Is interesting, because it bring up some mystery to the players of what is the truth on the myths they already know, but also bring the potential that the legends aren't true, what I feel like invalidating the concept of the game that &quot;the myths are true&quot;. I wouldnt go on this route, at least not in something as canon as Hera hatred for Zeus bastards (I think it is said on the myths that she hates him, or at least made very clear), maybe to something smaller like how the Gods made giant animals (not by a wave of hand, but with some special dust or something) but is a way to go, and I can imagine it working very well. Plus, in the game you need to consider things like the Fate, that would try to make the Gods as they were in the legends.<br /> <br /> And I dont think Zeus and Hera would be arguing all the time. They probably have cuddling moments, and a generally comfortable and happy life. With exception of Zeus escapades, Hera would be happy with her strong, confident, manly husband. I dont remember on the myths of Hera actually hating or even arguing with Zeus, she just attack his children, most probably because in Greek times a woman couldnt attack her husband, but was okay to ostracise the bastards. Just to add, I do not consider they would be in equality level, as greeks doesnt seem to have had a equality in marital life, but she might be happy like that and nobody can judge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043782#post1043782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. The Viking gods probably realized they were being hypocrites and became more accepting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine a few of them getting to this conclusion, Odin specially because he has bigger problems to worry and if the women magic helps he will use it, but all of them seem weird. Gods dont solve problems as we do, because if they did in 1000 plus years of existence they wouldnt have old gruges anymore nor defining flaws and characteristics. They would have accepted what happened, apologized, or simple let it go. Loki would have matured to a less selfish person. Thor would be much less hot headed. Athena would have changed her mind, at least once, in her 2000 long life and lost her virginity, maybe even married Ares (I always ship those two, even if they are brothers. Greek mythology doesnt seem to bother about it, anyway). I would much rather choose a game where this topic is not bring up or all Gods doesnt have, nor ever did, any form of bigotry (we didnt started discussing about race issues, but I'm including it here) than one that they can change, but just on this specific mind set. Gods, at least on the way I see, are thick headed, that is why they keep their same relations with each other and general behaviour during more than a 1000 years (Fate might help too). And seem to reduce consistency of the scenario that they can solve this specific flaw but not the others, and if you try to imagine how those relations and characters would had evolve if they were more changeable beings (able to change something that were most intrinsic to their culture) you are entering a whole new world of &quot;might happens&quot;, &quot;could happen&quot; and fan-fiction.<br /> <br /> But I'm not saying that it is a bad way to play, it is just my opinion. I think it would be easier to simple ignore the topic than to make they change by mere realization, but then you at least can be loyal to the legend of old (that they were bigoted) and make them nice today. I would suggest some event more meaningful, like the heroic sacrifice of a gay Vanir that did what no one else had courage to do and, to honour him, Odin forbade any form of bigotry of Asgard and the realms beyond. That is cool and create a new legend to work with.<br /> <br /> And the fact that the Gods of Olympus have ability to change their sex and forms at will is irrelevant to their opinion on homosexual relations. It would certainly make easier to an open God to try being in the other side of most discussions and views, but a God that is bigoted wouldnt change to try the other side. It never made Zeus more compassionate for humans beings the fact that he can became a human being, and gender roles doesnt have anything to do with their actual (besides temporarily) sex. Now, transgender is another thing that I think is more GM decision than anything else. They didnt had it on the old days, so no record of their actual opinion on the subject, on contrary of the homosexual relations. Looking pantheon by pantheon:<br /> <br /> Theoi: Greek Gods I would treat it as a case by case, because even considering as a Pantheon would be hard to say anything. The official position (aka Zeus opinion) would be most probably not against, but still personally treating anything passive (male, female or in between) as a female. But a transgender female to male would confuse the hell (or should I say Tartarus) out of him.<br /> <br /> Egypt: Again, no clue. Not much information about their opinion on homosexual subject to make a statement there, here is even more GM decision. But I would think they would consider the different gender okay, thanks to the multiple souls stuff. One soul part might be of one gender while the body is of another sex. As the full person is more than the sum of it parts, the final result might be considered different than the usual male or female, but a full result not just an &quot;half man&quot; or a &quot;3/4 woman&quot;. Not necessarily bad or inferior, maybe even superior to some Gods. (Again, not all Gods would comply an opinion of the subject, but no group of Gods ever agrees 100% with anything)(Also, I'm guessing very strongly here, but no one can say for sure, so my guess is a good as any.)<br /> <br /> Norse: Probably transphobic, at least on the same level as with homosexuals. They might treat better a female to male, Im not sure how comfortable Norse people where with gender role variations (I think they are cool with more manly women, but at this point I'm not making any statement), but a male to female would certainly be seem as a form of homosexual.<br /> <br /> Shen: No idea, but probably okay. Aparentelly homosexual relations was very open in old China, transgender should be okay too. But as the Gods of the Chinese Pantheon vary radically in age, I think it is a more case by case.<br /> <br /> Japan: No idea, think okay or neutral. Maybe some ostracism by some gods, but should be okay.<br /> <br /> Teotl: Against. Very, very against. They killed people for a lot less than that. Quetzalcoalt should be okay, as that other God of homosexuals which I dont remember the name, but in general they seem very traditionalist and giving much importance to the function of society to allow people to go different. Besides is possible that they would be okay to a transgender as long as they can fulfill the other gender function, but that basically means &quot;If a man wants to be a women, then use this MacGuffin to be a woman so you can have children, or stay as a man&quot; or &quot;If a woman wants to be a man, or use this MacGuffin to be a man and have children, or go to the army&quot;. (I might be considering the gender roles on the Teotl a little bad here. I dont know if they had more roles for each gender beyond having children and army, but I think none of them would be fulfilled without parenting)(I think Teotl army where men only, if anyone can correct me, please do).<br /> <br /> Maniktou and Orisha: I know nothing much of both, and they are compose of many tribes and villages legends, so I think they should be cool with it.<br /> <br /> Deva: Should be okay. They are, mostly, open minded.<br /> <br /> Tuatha de Dannan: I dont know. Again, I know very little of them, but as Watcher answered me back on the first page, they should be okay with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1041787#post1041787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way the Tuatha approach their own social systems, and morals however, as long as you are over the top, ridiculously bad ass, and the like, they will probably not care.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 02-05-2017, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:34:50-08:00","id":1044002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043985#post1043985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tuatha de Dannan: I dont know. Again, I know very little of them, but as Watcher answered me back on the first page, they should be okay with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we've got limited records, so we have no real substantial evidence in that area. However, as I said, there's a lot of situations where figures are allowed to flat out violate social norms pretty heavily without anyone batting their eye since they were so amazing. CuChulain is the big example of that, if you can get yourself to be recognized as amazing and awesome enough, you can get a free pass on a <i>lot</i> of stuff.<br /> <br /> So, a Trans* Scion may get a bit of pushback here and there, but as long as you could prove your... like, okay, hard to explain, so example. So, if someone pulls it out to insult you in a duel of words (not like an actual concept, but people throw shade at each other a lot as either a prelude to some serious throwing down, spiritually, physically, or socially) you would just need to retort really viciously, and eloquently. If you <i>don't</i> then you'll get targeted for harassment about it, but it'd be less about you being Trans* and more about you failing to defend yourself. Like, if you're a really shit warrior, and someone mocks you for it, and you do a terrible job at retorting, or go, &quot;Well I'm just going to ignore you.&quot; you'll get similarly targeted for ridicule.<br /> <br /> It's sort of weird honestly, the Tuatha can get very 'High-School-y,' at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-05-2017, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:17:04-08:00","id":1044016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043985#post1043985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deva: Should be okay. They are, mostly, open minded.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are actually two characters from Hindu myth one of we would today call transgender and another is probably genderfluid.<br /> <br /> Shikhandi from the Mahabharata was born with female genitals but identified as a man and was brought up as such (through Shiva's directives to his father), even being married to a princess and receiving male genitals from a friendly forest spirit known as a yaksha to consummate the marriage. Shikhandi had been the princess Amba in his previous life, who had sworn to kill the warrior Bhishma for kidnapping her. Through a boon from Shiva she was born as Shikhandi, who went to war with the Pandava in the Kurukshetra was (his father was Drupada, father of Draupadi, meaning he was the Pandava's brother-in-law). There he stood in front of Bhishma and Bhishma, who is apparently transphobic, said he would not fight a 'woman' and put down his bow, at which point Arjuna and Shikhandi shot him down.<br /> <br /> Ila, whose story is a minor tale in the Mahabharata, was born the eldest daughter (sometimes eldest child) of Vaivasvata Manu, was transformed to have male genitalia at birth by the magic of the Gods Mitra and Varuna and brought up as a boy, Sudyumna. Upon reaching adulthood, he entered a sacred grove to Parvati whose magic changed his sex again and Parvati modified the magic somewhat so that Ila/Sudyumna would spend a month as a man and a month as a woman with attendant sex change. And Ila/Sudyumna seems to have spent most of the next couple of years switching from male to female. Of course, ancient writers being what they are and not having the same understanding of sex and gender we do hir gender switches are linked to sex changes but I like to believe Ila/Sudyumna is honestly genderfluid. Anyway, Ila becomes mother to the king Pururavas by Budha (not Buddha) God of the Planet Mercury, a son of the Moon God Chandra. Pururavas would eventually become the founder of the Lunar Dynasty that the Pandavas and their cousins the Kauravas belong to, and Ila eventually attained enlightenment and attained oneness with the Goddess Durga.<br /> <br /> It is also to note that most male gods have feminine forms. Vishnu's Mohini Avatara is probably the most famous, though Vishnu also has Vaishnavi. Brahma and Shiva similarly have Brahmani and Shivani (also known as Maheshavari). Skanda has Kaumari, and Ganesha has Vinayaki. Indra has Aindri and so on. The Goddesses don't have any similar male forms usually...however, in some small strains of Hinduism Krishna is considered an Avatara not of Vishnu, but of Kali, so that counts (and Radha in this case becomes and Avatara of Shiva).<br /> <br /> All in all, while Hinduism doesn't entirely define sex and gender identities the way we do in modern times (like most mythologies) I think it's safe to say that the Hindu gods will not have much in the way of hang-ups when it comes to transgender or genderfluid characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:27:28-08:00","id":1044060,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure the Aesir would have a big problem with trans people either, provided that they serve a valuable role in society.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Norse were a very pragmatic people. When you live in a frozen wasteland and need everyone in your community pulling his/her weight, you really can't afford to be too choosy about who you find acceptable and who you don't. If a trans/genderfluid person is doing his or her job within society, I don't think the Norse would care very much about his or her proclivities.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Gods tend to be the same way, really. Odin, in particular, is also known for being extremely pragmatic, and he himself has engaged in some &quot;womanly&quot; activities. I suppose certain individual Aesir may have a problem with such people, but I don't think they'd have some kind of official &quot;These people are bad&quot; policy toward them.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeck, one of Thor's most famous myths is one where he looses his hammer (representing all his &quot;manly&quot; power) and has to freaking CROSSDRESS in order to get it back. He loses the weapon that represents his extreme masculinity and then he has to dress and act like a woman (using deception and guile were considered a &quot;woman's tactic&quot;) in order to retrieve it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough, it was recently brought to my attention: Loki went with Thor on that mission. Loki. The SHAPESHIFTER. Went with Thor after convincing him to pretend to be Freya in order to retrieve his hammer. Whyyyyyyy couldn't LOKI have pretended to be Freya again? Yeah, I call Trickster shenanigans!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:31:46-08:00","id":1044063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044060#post1044060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure the Aesir would have a big problem with trans people either, provided that they serve a valuable role in society.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough, it was recently brought to my attention: Loki went with Thor on that mission. Loki. The SHAPESHIFTER. Went with Thor after convincing him to pretend to be Freya in order to retrieve his hammer. Whyyyyyyy couldn't LOKI have pretended to be Freya again? Yeah, I call Trickster shenanigans!</div> </div> </div> </div>If you got that thought from the same Overly Sarcastic source I did, they did also mention that the cross-dressing was Heimdall's idea, not Loki's (though I'm sure Loki regrets not coming up with it to this day) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also while Loki could have pretended to be Freya I don't think he could have actually used Mjolnir, so Thor had to be there somehow...and the new bride was much more likely to get closer to the Hammer than some bridesmaid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:33:12-08:00","id":1044064,"title":"","content":"Then again, unless you intend to run a game where women, minorities, and LGBTQ characters (and players) are discriminated against, it's probably best to go with the idea that the various deities are open to gay rights, women's equality, and the rights of people from other cultures. We can argue all day about what we believe the Gods and Goddesses would think, but in the end, a) humans have no idea what a deity would really think about these things anyway, because the information we have is all filtered through the originating cultures and then through Christianity/Islam/whichever faith, all of which have their own inherent biases, and b) it's a game, not a religious reference, so do what works for you and your players.<br /> Do we really want Scion 2nd to state that the Teotl will hate/disown/kill LGBTQ scions? Or that the Aesir only respect &quot;masculine&quot;men? Or that the Chinese and Japanese pantheons hate each other over long-standing cultural problems? For the sake of playability and fun, maybe &quot;accuracy&quot; (whatever that means in this context) needs to be binned in favour of fun and playability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:55:40-08:00","id":1044078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044063#post1044063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you got that thought from the same Overly Sarcastic source I did, they did also mention that the cross-dressing was Heimdall's idea, not Loki's (though I'm sure Loki regrets not coming up with it to this day) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also while Loki could have pretended to be Freya I don't think he could have actually used Mjolnir, so Thor had to be there somehow...and the new bride was much more likely to get closer to the Hammer than some bridesmaid.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYep! I just discovered the insane joy of Overly Sarcastic Productions, and I just loved their video on the Poetic Eddas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bAnd yes, the cross-dressing may have been Heimdall's idea, but I'm betting Loki pulled some kind of Epic Manipulation-y hijinks to convince Thor that HE should be the one in the dress, rather than.......oh you know........THE SHAPESHIFTER?!!<br /> <br /> \u200bBut yeah, good point about the hammer. Thor still had to be there. But still, you'd think Thor could've just dressed up as Njord or something. You know, the whole &quot;Dad giving the bride away&quot; thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:57:36-08:00","id":1044079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044064#post1044064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, unless you intend to run a game where women, minorities, and LGBTQ characters (and players) are discriminated against, it's probably best to go with the idea that the various deities are open to gay rights, women's equality, and the rights of people from other cultures. We can argue all day about what we believe the Gods and Goddesses would think, but in the end, a) humans have no idea what a deity would really think about these things anyway, because the information we have is all filtered through the originating cultures and then through Christianity/Islam/whichever faith, all of which have their own inherent biases, and b) it's a game, not a religious reference, so do what works for you and your players.<br /> Do we really want Scion 2nd to state that the Teotl will hate/disown/kill LGBTQ scions? Or that the Aesir only respect &amp;quot;masculine&amp;quot;men? Or that the Chinese and Japanese pantheons hate each other over long-standing cultural problems? For the sake of playability and fun, maybe &amp;quot;accuracy&amp;quot; (whatever that means in this context) needs to be binned in favour of fun and playability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo. This thread's yet to give me a single reason why I feel like bigotry needs to have a place in my Scion games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:09:17-08:00","id":1044083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043985#post1043985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a way to go in a game, but I think it might be trick. I mean, if you decide to say that some elements of the legends are not true because they are incomplete or incorrect, this can potentially change all mythology, everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know what they say: <b>History is written by the victors</b>.<br /> <br /> Of course there's the possibility of these legends being incomplete or false, we only have one side of the argument to go by!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:13:18-08:00","id":1044086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044064#post1044064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, unless you intend to run a game where women, minorities, and LGBTQ characters (and players) are discriminated against, it's probably best to go with the idea that the various deities are open to gay rights, women's equality, and the rights of people from other cultures. We can argue all day about what we believe the Gods and Goddesses would think, but in the end, a) humans have no idea what a deity would really think about these things anyway, because the information we have is all filtered through the originating cultures and then through Christianity/Islam/whichever faith, all of which have their own inherent biases, and b) it's a game, not a religious reference, so do what works for you and your players.<br /> Do we really want Scion 2nd to state that the Teotl will hate/disown/kill LGBTQ scions? Or that the Aesir only respect &quot;masculine&quot;men? Or that the Chinese and Japanese pantheons hate each other over long-standing cultural problems? For the sake of playability and fun, maybe &quot;accuracy&quot; (whatever that means in this context) needs to be binned in favour of fun and playability.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI suppose it would be cool if Scion 2E at least draws some attention to how the Pantheons might view these issues. But they could do that in a way that looks more like presenting storytelling options, rather than setting down hard-and-fast setting rules.<br /> <br /> \u200bInstead of saying &quot;The Teotl WILL kill any Scion who isn't 100% hetero on sight!&quot; The books could say &quot;Historically, the Teotl, and their people, had a very dim view of homosexuality, and that could be an element of your story, should you wish it to be.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bDifferent gaming groups may want to do different things, so it's a good idea to present as many options as possible. If you WANT to deal with the social issues of being an LGBTQ Scion in a setting in which several Pantheons may have a problem with that? Then sure, go with the traditional depictions. If you don't want to do such things, just ignore that and make up your own rules. Both play styles are equally valid.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yeah, drawing the reader's attention to the fact that these issues existed, and may still exist, is a good way to let them know what kind of world they could build for his or her purposes, but it should be made clear that more modern viewpoints can be used as well. It's really all about planning your story and deciding which Scion themes you wish to emphasize within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:21:29-08:00","id":1044090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044060#post1044060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAlthough, it was recently brought to my attention: Loki went with Thor on that mission. Loki. The SHAPESHIFTER. Went with Thor after convincing him to pretend to be Freya in order to retrieve his hammer. Whyyyyyyy couldn't LOKI have pretended to be Freya again? Yeah, I call Trickster shenanigans!</div> </div> </div> </div>The world would have been so much poorer without the story of Thor the bride. Who would pass up such a spectacle?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:25:33-08:00","id":1044093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044090#post1044090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The world would have been so much poorer without the story of Thor the bride. Who would pass up such a spectacle?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYep. That's why my headcanon says &quot;Loki may not have come up with the idea of Thor crossdressing, but once the plan was proposed and accepted, Loki used all his Trickster-y wiles to ensure that it unfolded the way that it did.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:54:48-08:00","id":1044114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044090#post1044090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The world would have been so much poorer without the story of Thor the bride. Who would pass up such a spectacle?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm kind of upset I've never actually read anything about Sun Wukong, now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=61nuXrvqNgI\" data-code=\"61nuXrvqNgI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/61nuXrvqNgI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-08-2017, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:06:42-08:00","id":1044514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043985#post1043985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a way to go in a game, but I think it might be trick. I mean, if you decide to say that some elements of the legends are not true because they are incomplete or incorrect, this can potentially change all mythology, everywhere. Is interesting, because it bring up some mystery to the players of what is the truth on the myths they already know, but also bring the potential that the legends aren't true, what I feel like invalidating the concept of the game that &quot;the myths are true&quot;. I wouldnt go on this route, at least not in something as canon as Hera hatred for Zeus bastards (I think it is said on the myths that she hates him, or at least made very clear), maybe to something smaller like how the Gods made giant animals (not by a wave of hand, but with some special dust or something) but is a way to go, and I can imagine it working very well. Plus, in the game you need to consider things like the Fate, that would try to make the Gods as they were in the legends.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem with &quot;all myths are true&quot; is the fact that in many cases there are so many different versions of the same myth in the same culture. Most of them started as oral traditions, and as anyone who's played telephone can attest, things get muddied the longer they are passed around. In the myth of Arakhne, everyone agrees that there was a contest that resulted in Arakhne being transformed into a spider, but different versions can't even agree on who won the contest. A person who wished to depict Athena in their games as compassionate might take the tactic of going with the version where Arakhne was devastated by her loss and hung herself, and Athena took pity upon her and made her a spider so that she could weave forever. One who wished to depict Athena as more of a bitch could go with the version where Arakhne wins and Athena throws a tantrum. Arakhne's punishment could be for winning the contest, but it could just as easily be a punishment for hubris and lack of respect for the Gods. It is the same with Herakles. The myths agree that Hera caused a whole lot of trouble for him, but the reason for why the trouble was caused could still be up in the air. Hell, even if she actually did hate Herakles, the reason why she did so could vary. Even if she doesn't hate Herakles and had good intentions, nothing guarantees that Herakles doesn't hold a grudge about it. For a game like Scion, these distinctions are important, but should be decided on a game-by-game basis depending on the needs of the story. If you want the Gods to be respectable, then when a Scion says, &quot;You guys aren't so great. I know your stories, and you did this, this, and this, so spare my your bullshit about needing to act in a virtuous manner,&quot; the Gods should be able to respond with, &quot;No, you don't know the full story. Here's what really happened back then...&quot; If you want a game where the Gods are unworthy and the Scions are the only redeeming thing to ever come out of a pantheon, then they instead respond with &quot;So what? You're my kid and you'll do as I say, not as I do.&quot; I've had one game where Hera changed sides in the war because she was sick of Zeus cheating on her. Most games, it's more that Zeus starts hitting on the character, character smirks, and Zeus responds with, &quot;She's right behind me, isn't she?&quot; Hera herself in those games tends to be quite benevolent and often proves to be a valuable ally to the player character, despite the fact that the characters are seldom if ever married in a traditional monogamous union (the characters usually being either &quot;not the marrying sort&quot; or the sort that says &quot;If I'm going to get married, I'm going to marry all the men and women that I love. Wanna join?&quot;). <br /> <br /> TLDR: The myths are true, but the version and context of said myths must be decided based upon what's good for each individual game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T14:54:25-08:00","id":1044735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1043042#post1043042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, one of Zeus' daughters was given the lofty position of 'cup barer' for the gods of Olympus. And she was a legitimate child!<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The blood of two gods runs through me. Surely, Fate has great plans in store for me!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zeus:</b> Be a dear and get daddy another drink, would you?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIn a lot of societies, the court position of &quot;cup bearer&quot; tends to be highly respected and influential, since it's both something that conveys a great deal of trust, and because it means you're standing at the side of the monarch all the time.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's a lot like thinking that it's really minor and undignified to be the person who has to sleep at the foot of Louis XIV's bed and help him get dressed in the morning, when it actually means that you're the second most powerful person in France.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr how being the person who has to carry Oda Nobunaga's sandals and help him put them on and take them off means you're an insignificant servant, and then you're a commander of his armies strong enough to set yourself up as successor after he gets murdered.<br /> <br /> \u200b(This thread is giving me mixed messages about how the game describes its gods and setting, so I can't really contribute a perspective until I see an actual book)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T21:22:30-08:00","id":1044878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044735#post1044735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIn a lot of societies, the court position of &quot;cup bearer&quot; tends to be highly respected and influential, since it's both something that conveys a great deal of trust, and because it means you're standing at the side of the monarch all the time.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's a lot like thinking that it's really minor and undignified to be the person who has to sleep at the foot of Louis XIV's bed and help him get dressed in the morning, when it actually means that you're the second most powerful person in France.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr how being the person who has to carry Oda Nobunaga's sandals and help him put them on and take them off means you're an insignificant servant, and then you're a commander of his armies strong enough to set yourself up as successor after he gets murdered.<br /> <br /> \u200b(This thread is giving me mixed messages about how the game describes its gods and setting, so I can't really contribute a perspective until I see an actual book)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well, Zeus did end up replacing her with Ganymede, so... she still got jipped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T22:26:32-08:00","id":1044909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044878#post1044878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, well, Zeus did end up replacing her with Ganymede, so... she still got jipped.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Not at all relevant to this thread, but &quot;jipped&quot; has its roots in some pretty profoundly racist stuff regarding to Romani. Use it at your own peril.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T01:36:55-08:00","id":1044960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044909#post1044909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Not at all relevant to this thread, but &quot;jipped&quot; has its roots in some pretty profoundly racist stuff regarding to Romani. Use it at your own peril.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Learned THAT years ago. Hoo boy did <i>that</i> make me uncomfortable. Stopped using THAT word, let me tell you.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how after years of playing Exalted I get informed that the term &quot;Half-caste&quot; (In Exalted, Half-Caste was used to describe the children of Celestial Exalts that inherited portions of their parents' power) was actually a racial slur usually used to refer to mixed-race children in India. Dropped the phrase like a hot potato.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T01:52:35-08:00","id":1044964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044909#post1044909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Not at all relevant to this thread, but &quot;jipped&quot; has its roots in some pretty profoundly racist stuff regarding to Romani. Use it at your own peril.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see the connection now that I think about it... Good thing I don't use that word very often, huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:53:50-08:00","id":1045007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044960#post1044960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Learned THAT years ago. Hoo boy did <i>that</i> make me uncomfortable. Stopped using THAT word, let me tell you.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how after years of playing Exalted I get informed that the term &quot;Half-caste&quot; (In Exalted, Half-Caste was used to describe the children of Celestial Exalts that inherited portions of their parents' power) was actually a racial slur usually used to refer to mixed-race children in India. Dropped the phrase like a hot potato.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sounds about as awkward as when I found out women apparently don't like being referred to as ma'am, because it supposedly an insult. I'm sorry, I thought ma'am was a term of respect when addressing a woman! When the hell did it become offensive!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-07-2017, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:46:56-08:00","id":1045031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044878#post1044878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, well, Zeus did end up replacing her with Ganymede, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe position was already open on account of the fact that Hebe became married to Heracles.<br /> <br /> \u200bSome would regard that as a bit of a step up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T09:14:45-08:00","id":1045130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1045007#post1045007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Sounds about as awkward as when I found out women apparently don't like being referred to as ma'am, because it supposedly an insult. I'm sorry, I thought ma'am was a term of respect when addressing a woman! When the hell did it become offensive!?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've never heard the term being considered offensive in its own right, but individuals might take offense to it. I think it would mostly be considered insulting if they perceived insincerity or condescension in its use. If they think &quot;ma'am&quot; is being used as a placeholder for &quot;you foolish idiot who doesn't know a damn thing&quot;, of course they'll be offended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T09:40:42-08:00","id":1045163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044960#post1044960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Learned THAT years ago. Hoo boy did <i>that</i> make me uncomfortable. Stopped using THAT word, let me tell you.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how after years of playing Exalted I get informed that the term &quot;Half-caste&quot; (In Exalted, Half-Caste was used to describe the children of Celestial Exalts that inherited portions of their parents' power) was actually a racial slur usually used to refer to mixed-race children in India. Dropped the phrase like a hot potato.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never actually heard of it being used in India...from what I can find Half-Caste seems to be a term used by Europeans primarily to refer to children of colonist and colonized, and was not limited to just India.<br /> <br /> To be honest I've never been able to hear the word Caste in itself (when used in Exalted) without wincing slightly because it always brings to mind the long, complex and almost always negative history of the Caste System in India.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T09:48:40-08:00","id":1045166,"title":"","content":"Can't seem to delete this post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 02-07-2017, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T09:51:38-08:00","id":1045173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1045130#post1045130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've never heard the term being considered offensive in its own right, but individuals might take offense to it. I think it would mostly be considered insulting if they perceived insincerity or condescension in its use. If they think &quot;ma'am&quot; is being used as a placeholder for &quot;you foolish idiot who doesn't know a damn thing&quot;, of course they'll be offended.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another part is that some consider it being called old.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:16:31-08:00","id":1045235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1044079#post1044079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bingo. This thread's yet to give me a single reason why I feel like bigotry needs to have a place in my Scion games.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about interesting conflict? I'm not saying that need to have bigotry in your games to make them interesting, but I don't believe including it makes the game unplayable or is an example of the GM being a sadist in most cases. Some of the greatest films and stories of all time have been based around a character or a group of characters nobly fighting aganist some kind of bigotry in their lives. Classics like Guess Whose Coming to Dinner and To Kill a Mockingbird, and more recent films like Pride, the Help, and Hidden Figures all deal with this and their great because of it.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, and this just my personal thing, but I've always enjoyed the framework of Scion being a game where modern people and ancient gods where forced by happenstance to work together even though their morals, social norms, desires, and even identities may clash. I've never really seen that as a narrative barrier but as an opportunity see how my characters would have traverse such anarchic political and cultural worlds.<br /> <br /> But, hey, if Scion is your escape from all that crappy reality than I can respect that and hope that the Core Book provides us both of what we want from the game. I just hope that what I said maybe shows that having bigotry as an element in a game isn't always a bad thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:04:59-08:00","id":1045273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread's yet to give me a single reason why I feel like bigotry needs to have a place in my Scion games.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that's fair, but I think it's also fair to hear out why other people might want to do so in their &quot;my Scion games&quot;, without going immediately to the assumption that it implies a desire for or satisfaction with bigotry.<br /> <br /> I'd say that White Wolf games have had a consistent tendency to attract people who enjoy settings with a measure of verisimilitude (i.e. things that present a sufficiently convincing simulation of what is real). Different people will have different standards of what is convincing; if I recall and read you correctly, you have elucidated in detail on how you do not find it convincing for any or many gods to retain perspectives that modern society regards as bigoted, and there's nothing wrong with that. At the same time, I think it's okay for other people to have standards of verisimilitude that can't really buy the idea that all of the cosmic authority figures have sufficiently ideal perspectives from the outset, and I don't think that necessarily represents a person unable to conceive of a world without bigotry as having difficulty buying into a world in which powerful figures do not include flaws in such a way.<br /> <br /> \u200bI know that applies to people who have also been victims of bigotry; for one person who will want their fun to consist of escape into a more ideal reality, I have known other people who have faced prejudice who would look at a world resembling our own in which that prejudice and the struggle against it is absent as being even a little bit insulting. That their own standard of escapism consists of flowing into a world where their struggle still exists, and they can play out scenarios in which they fight against it directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:26:55-08:00","id":1045293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1045130#post1045130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've never heard the term being considered offensive in its own right, but individuals might take offense to it. I think it would mostly be considered insulting if they perceived insincerity or condescension in its use. If they think &quot;ma'am&quot; is being used as a placeholder for &quot;you foolish idiot who doesn't know a damn thing&quot;, of course they'll be offended.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I was answering a question for them and said <b>&quot;no, ma'am&quot;</b> and they glared at me and said <b>&quot;I'm not a ma'am.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Ma'am<br /> Mam<br /> <br /> noun<br /> <br /> A term of respectful or polite address used for a woman<br /> <br /> A term of address for a ranking female officer in the police or armed forces<br /> <br /> A term of address for female royalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-07-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:34:38-08:00","id":1045302,"title":"","content":"Ma'am is polite, but it also has a connotation that the person you're referring to is old. Any offense likely stems from that; you're being respectful but calling them an old lady.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:41:44-08:00","id":1045312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1045273#post1045273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI think that's fair, but I think it's also fair to hear out why other people might want to do so in their &quot;my Scion games&quot;, without going immediately to the assumption that it implies a desire for or satisfaction with bigotry.<br /> <br /> I'd say that White Wolf games have had a consistent tendency to attract people who enjoy settings with a measure of verisimilitude (i.e. things that present a sufficiently convincing simulation of what is real). .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's one of the major reasons why I got hooked on White Wolf games... That, and the unique (to me, at the time) concept of playing a game from a monster's sympathetic point of view. I thought it was interesting to find a role playing game that potentially dealt with mature themes, without instantly associating the word &quot;mature&quot; with &quot;sexual.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-07-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:42:49-08:00","id":1045483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1045293#post1045293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I was answering a question for them and said <b>&quot;no, ma'am&quot;</b> and they glared at me and said <b>&quot;I'm not a ma'am.&quot;</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI lack context, but can think of at least three reasonings for that specific wording in a response; somebody assuming that the term is not being used sincerely, somebody annoyed at connotations to the term that might make it archaic, and somebody disliking the term being applied to them for thinking that it isn't really valid (similar to the old joke about NCOs taking umbrage at being called 'sir').<br /> <br /> \u200bI personally wouldn't use it because I regard it as being respectful in a very... for want of another term, patriarchal sense. I look at it as being like chivalry; the attitude of respect for women distinct from men and as a kind of obligation for a man of class, rather than just treating women with the same respect one would for any person.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:32:44-08:00","id":1045550,"title":"","content":"They could've also not been a woman!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T19:14:19-08:00","id":1045566,"title":"","content":"But it does lead to the next question: which term do you use? Lady? Miss? Mrs? Ms? If you <i>don't have a name</i>, and have to respond to a customer, what do you use if you can't say &quot;ma'am&quot; or &quot;sir&quot;? I get that it's presumptuous if they are gender-fluid/neutral, but when you are just helping them, in a retail/library/service industry way, what do you do? It's a bit more complicated than it used to be, and some of the social customs are still being worked out. Being huffy or rude to someone who's just trying to help out is unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:24:24-08:00","id":1046027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1045566#post1045566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you <i>don't have a name</i>, and have to respond to a customer, what do you use if you can't say &quot;ma'am&quot; or &quot;sir&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way that I am responding to you now.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf a term like &quot;ma'am&quot; is archaic, then needing to use formal honorifics when addressing a customer certainly is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:17:07-08:00","id":1046414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1045550#post1045550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could've also not been a woman!</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible, though in my experience, despite what certain people like to claim, most people I've met won't flip into a rage if you use the wrong pronoun.<br /> <br /> Though from my customer service days, I'd be willing to bet that if someone is outraged at being called 'ma'am'? 90% chance that it's a woman who equates being called 'ma'am' with being old and dammit they're not old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T01:21:37-08:00","id":1046680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1045031#post1045031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe position was already open on account of the fact that Hebe became married to Heracles.<br /> <br /> \u200bSome would regard that as a bit of a step up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it, that's actually a pretty big step down. You go from being the Cupbearer of Olympus, symbolizing that you are all-but completely trusted by the king and queen [who also are your parents] and anybody else allowed to drink from it to... your [formerly] half-mortal step brother's wife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T05:13:58-08:00","id":1046721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1046680#post1046680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that I think about it, that's actually a pretty big step down. You go from being the Cupbearer of Olympus, symbolizing that you are all-but completely trusted by the king and queen [who also are your parents] and anybody else allowed to drink from it to... your [formerly] half-mortal step brother's wife.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Can you really say they were the most trusted, though? I mean, it's not like she could have poisoned any of them. They're immortal, after all!<br /> <br /> I mean, unless she had Hind's blood or something? I think I remember the old Hercules TV series depicting that Hind's blood was a lethal poison for Gods. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But, yeah, being married off to the God of Strength, who has a long history of psychopathic outbursts, courtesy of the Goddess of Marriage...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1045550#post1045550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could've also not been a woman!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, she made no move to tell the rest of the class, or even correct me on what I should call her. Just said <b>&quot;I'm not a ma'am&quot;</b> and left it at that. So, she probably thought I was calling her old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-10-2017, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:42:49-08:00","id":1051516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1046721#post1046721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Can you really say they were the most trusted, though? I mean, it's not like she could have poisoned any of them. They're immortal, after all!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI wouldn't say it's about logic, but literary shorthand. To the audience of such mythic narrative, bearing the cup of royalty denotes prestige.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T18:22:06-08:00","id":1051789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1041985#post1041985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's to say gods cannot change? Mars the noble, agricultural patron of the Romans is a far cry from the insufferable brute he was as Ares, after all.<br /> <br /> To me, locking in all of the gods to a very backwards, conservative mindset is an entirely too limiting view of things, one that suffocates interesting story potential at best and is actively looking to artificially echo existing oppression at worst. It's absurd to me to say that the gods can figure out a cell phone but absolutely have to come down hard on homosexuality or women's rights, especially given hundreds of thousands of years of cultural shift among their followers since their ancient heydays. Odin's already practiced &amp;quot;womanly&amp;quot; magics, Loki has already given birth, the Theoi are drowning in homosexuality... there's zero reason in my eyes to pin current conservatism on these figures.<br /> <br /> You're welcome to have your gods be stuck in the past if that's what you want to play, but to me Scion is a game of <i>modern </i>mythology: these gods aren't dusty throwbacks, they're here and alive and just as much a part of the world as you or me. </div> </div> </div> </div> Zues gave birth as well in a sense, he supports his daughter Athena and Artemis in their choices which include rejecting marriage and traditional female occupations, ect... <br /> <br /> Honestly the Gods would be practical and just as in the real world, religions adapt to changing circumstances or die out. <br /> <br /> So I can see conservative sects, but I see the Gods usually being apolitical, they more concerned with the Titans and divine politics then if you had sex with another dude or a threesome or your trans, etc..., humanities hangs usually did not extend to the Gods, the Greeks worshipped a Goddess of war, yet it was men who were expected to give their lives to the meat grinder of war, not women, so the culture's values are not the Gods values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T19:48:04-08:00","id":1051816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1051789#post1051789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Zues gave birth as well in a sense, he supports his daughter Athena and Artemis in their choices which include rejecting marriage and traditional female occupations, ect...<br /> <br /> Honestly the Gods would be practical and just as in the real world, religions adapt to changing circumstances or die out.<br /> <br /> So I can see conservative sects, but I see the Gods usually being apolitical, they more concerned with the Titans and divine politics then if you had sex with another dude or a threesome or your trans, etc..., humanities hangs usually did not extend to the Gods, the Greeks worshipped a Goddess of war, yet it was men who were expected to give their lives to the meat grinder of war, not women, so the culture's values are not the Gods values.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Athena was a goddess of strategy, wisdom and tactics. Ares was the god of war. In other words, they recognized women for being more self composed, while men were the blood thirsty soldiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T08:16:52-08:00","id":1052012,"title":"","content":"But again, this isn't &quot;the game of ancient Greek cultural values.&quot; Apart from the fact that we see past cultures through the lens of time, incomplete records, and modern interpretation, the point here is; play what works for you. Who knows what the Gods really think? Hell, maybe the fall of Greece came about because the Gods and Goddesses didn't like how they were being represented by Athens, and so they stopped supporting them. It's a fictional universe - have fun with it. And don't feel that you have to make your pantheons sexist/racist/homophobic just because historians and theologians say they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 02-20-2017, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T09:17:36-08:00","id":1052030,"title":"","content":"I'd bet you money that the Spartans didn't view Ares as a savage brute, and the Romans certainly didn't view Mars in that way. Remember that who is telling the story influences the telling, and also remember that in Scion these characters have had hundreds or thousands of years to grow and change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T09:38:32-08:00","id":1052036,"title":"","content":"That's definitely true, atamajakki. But just because someone's changed over the years doesn't mean it's always a positive change. Ares might have become less bloodthirsty by the 21st century but Hephaestus could have become a GamerGater!<br /> <br /> A horrifying thought I know but just as possible. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T10:52:10-08:00","id":1052057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1052036#post1052036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definitely true, atamajakki. But just because someone's changed over the years doesn't mean it's always a positive change. Ares might have become less bloodthirsty by the 21st century but Hephaestus could have become a GamerGater!<br /> <br /> A horrifying thought I know but just as possible. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the stuff of nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:15:11-08:00","id":1052181,"title":"","content":"What's a GamerGater?<br /> <br /> And I doubt Ares became less blood thirsty. If modern warfare has taught us anything, it's that Ares didn't think we were killing each other fast enough!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:39:02-08:00","id":1052267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1052181#post1052181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's a GamerGater?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone who's definition of &quot;ethics in game journalism&quot; is to go after the less than 1% of critics and journalists who discuss social representation issues, and completely ignore the issue of ad revenue shaping coverage of big company games. While not all GamerGaters are personally motivated by misogyny, the movement was specifically born out of the hellpit of 4Chan with the goal of going after feminists who dared to treat video games as a medium worthy of taking sereiously as socially relevant art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:39:33-08:00","id":1052656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1052181#post1052181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I doubt Ares became less blood thirsty. If modern warfare has taught us anything, it's that Ares didn't think we were killing each other fast enough!</div> </div> </div> </div>Two words: free will.<br /> It's hardly fair to blame the gods for everything that is wrong with society when we humans are perfectly capable of messing stuff up on our own. <br /> For what it's worth, modern warfare is practically the opposite of how war was expected to be waged in the heroic age. <br /> Imagine two armed humans, looking each other in the eye, determined to slit each other's throats.<br /> That's where you meet Enyalios. <br /> WMDs? So not his style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:38:12-08:00","id":1052935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1052656#post1052656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two words: free will.<br /> It's hardly fair to blame the gods for everything that is wrong with society when we humans are perfectly capable of messing stuff up on our own.<br /> For what it's worth, modern warfare is practically the opposite of how war was expected to be waged in the heroic age.<br /> Imagine two armed humans, looking each other in the eye, determined to slit each other's throats.<br /> That's where you meet Enyalios.<br /> WMDs? So not his style.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If the gods wanted us to exercise free will, we wouldn't have a concept of good and evil.<br /> <br /> But the 1st edition describes Ares as being some kind of battle crazed maniac. It even says veteran soldiers consider WMD's to be <i>less destructive</i> than him. I don't know if his description has been edited with 2nd edition, or not, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T20:09:24-08:00","id":1055516,"title":"","content":"Alright this may come across as a non-sequester but given that I already sarcastic mentioned the possibly of Hephaestus being a GameGater I like to seriously bring up possibility of Eris gaining the Mantle of Goddess of Trolling, Flame Wars and Youtube Comments in the modern day.<br /> <br /> She doesn't care what your sexuality or gender identity is so long as her defending it or attacking it pisses off a bunch of people and cause them to argue with each other online!<br /> <br /> Now that is horrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T21:51:59-08:00","id":1055536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1055516#post1055516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright this may come across as a non-sequester but given that I already sarcastic mentioned the possibly of Hephaestus being a GameGater I like to seriously bring up possibility of Eris gaining the Mantle of Goddess of Trolling, Flame Wars and Youtube Comments in the modern day.<br /> <br /> She doesn't care what your sexuality or gender identity is so long as her defending it or attacking it pisses off a bunch of people and cause them to argue with each other online!<br /> <br /> Now that is horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I feel like trolling and flame wars would fall under something Loki would dive on in a heartbeat. He gets to anonymously prank people across the world and start mass amounts of panic / chaos without leaving the comfort of his Hall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T07:41:49-08:00","id":1055647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1055536#post1055536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like trolling and flame wars would fall under something Loki would dive on in a heartbeat. He gets to anonymously prank people across the world and start mass amounts of panic / chaos without leaving the comfort of his Hall?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who needs Muspel giants? This is how you engulf the world in flame!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:36:04-08:00","id":1056301,"title":"","content":"Gods change with the times. Ancient Greek culture doesn't exist anymore, and it changed considerably over the course of antiquity. Pederasty arose among the aristocracy at a particular point for particular reasons related to power dynamics and prescriptive gender roles, and in time it disappeared as a practice. There's nothing essentially Greek about it. Moreover, there's no reason to believe that the cultures of the ancient Greeks and their gods were identical in all respects to begin with, as evidenced by the frequency with which mortals in ancient Greek literature express mystification at the ways of the gods and how their sense of right and wrong do not always seem to line up with those of mortals. In addition, Zeus is depicted as a dynamic figure in the mythic literature, to the extent that the character of his reign shifted over time.<br /> <br /> Therefore, there's no reason to imagine that Zeus would hold a static opinion about something that was dictated by the cultural values of the mortals who worshiped him millennia ago. That's on top of the fact that ancient Greek gods were never much for micromanaging the cultural practices of their worshipers in the manner of Yahweh. How and whom people married was never regarded as much of a religious issue, much less one the gods expressed strong opinions on. If Zeus's behavior in the myths is any indication, he always regarded mortal institutions like marriage as beneath his notice to begin with.<br /> <br /> In other words, I think there are a lot of Christianizing assumptions built into the original question. The same goes for the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 02-28-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:10:39-08:00","id":1056438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056301#post1056301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pederasty arose among the aristocracy at a particular point for particular reasons related to power dynamics and prescriptive gender roles, and in time it disappeared as a practice. There's nothing essentially Greek about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Japan had it, too. Between Samurai and young boys. So long as the relationship was consensual.<br /> <br /> Although Japan and China never quite seemed to have gotten rid of it. Just look at the age of consent over there. I did... like 2 or 3 times to make sure. And now ecchi anime makes a bit more sense to me!<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> But I stand by my belief that the Gods wouldn't be keen on changing their minds, at least not in first edition. The entire reason they retreated from the World was because <b>they didn't</b> want human culture to influence them. They were afraid of the effect human ideas had on them, so they said &quot;fuck it&quot; and jumped ship.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition, where human belief no longer directly influences their identities, the potential for them to change might be even less than it was in 1st edition, since our ideas mean squat to them. Also, I casually point to real world examples of religion for anybody who claims the passage of time alone results in progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-28-2017, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:04:19-08:00","id":1056456,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing, though. Unless someone is actually planning on running a game where Godly rape, pederasty, sexism, racism, and homophobia are integral parts of the game, there's absolutely no good reason to assume that the Gods <i>haven't</i> changed over time. Or that <i>human society</i> has changed, even if the Gods stay the same. Would you run a modern game, but based on the worst pieces of morality of the Bible as it was 1800 years ago, because &quot;that's what this book and stories tell me that [fill in your deity] thinks&quot;? Not much fun to be had with stoning heretics, selling your daughters into marriage, beating your slaves and wives [just don't break the &quot;rule of thumb&quot;], discriminating violently against homosexuality, and so on. This isn't history - it's a game. There is no good reason to assume that the Gods wouldn't change their views, or that humanity wouldn't change it's cultures, to become something different, and a hell of a lot more fun to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:12:15-08:00","id":1056459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056456#post1056456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing, though. Unless someone is actually planning on running a game where Godly rape, pederasty, sexism, racism, and homophobia are integral parts of the game, there's absolutely no good reason to assume that the Gods <i>haven't</i> changed over time. Or that <i>human society</i> has changed, even if the Gods stay the same. Would you run a modern game, but based on the worst pieces of morality of the Bible as it was 1800 years ago, because &quot;that's what this book and stories tell me that [fill in your deity] thinks&quot;? Not much fun to be had with stoning heretics, selling your daughters into marriage, beating your slaves and wives [just don't break the &quot;rule of thumb&quot;], discriminating violently against homosexuality, and so on. This isn't history - it's a game. There is no good reason to assume that the Gods wouldn't change their views, or that humanity wouldn't change it's cultures, to become something different, and a hell of a lot more fun to play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I would run a modern game with that stuff, because that's exactly what drew me to White Wolf's role playing in the first place. The fact that it deals with real world issues, to a certain extent. What would my character actually have to go through if they became a vampire / werewolf / monster / god / whatever?<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying you should cram these things down players' throats straight out of the gate, but I'm also not saying you should just pretend they don't happen. Because they do happen, and they are still happening in the real world, today. Realism is part of White Wolf's charm, <i>at least to me personally.</i> I'm not going to start throwing it around every corner and claim &quot;This is how we do shit!&quot; but I would make it crop up occasionally in the story, to remind players who / what they're dealing with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:15:21-08:00","id":1056460,"title":"","content":"Also, there's a real difference between the perception of the deities of the most popular modern religions, and the Gods of mythology. The Greek Gods [and those of the Norse, Egyptians, Aztecs, and so on] were perceived as directly involved in the lives of humans, often interacting personally to have children with mortals, bless certain heroic types, curse the unlucky, and generally interfere in the affairs of humanity. I'm not aware of any stories that have the major Gods of modern faiths directly and tangibly involving themselves in the same way. Modern relations with the deities are a lot more static and distant [in that way] than the legendary ones were, and so I don't feel that you can say &quot;[insert faith here] has the same rules now as it did back then, so the Greek/Mayan/Inue deities should be similarly unchanging&quot;. In the end, it really comes down to this: what's going to make a more engaging game? Heroic legends and larger-than-life deities that change the world, or static, restrictive, outdated morality and social roles? I know which one I would rather play...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:22:39-08:00","id":1056464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056460#post1056460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not aware of any stories that have the major Gods of modern faiths directly and tangibly involving themselves in the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Prophets, Avatars, Saints... Three examples of modern religious deities directly involving themselves with mortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prophets</b> = Mortals who act as the mouth piece for their respective deities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Avatars</i> = Gods walking around in mortal guise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Saints</u> = Mortals capable of channeling the power of their gods and allowing them to act through the mortal vessel.<br /> <br /> <br /> And then, of course, we have Messiahs, who come to deliver a chosen group of people into paradise of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:28:23-08:00","id":1056469,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between saying, &quot;bad things exist in the world, and I want to include them in my chronicle/game for dramatic effect and realism&quot;, and saying &quot;The Aztec Gods are completely intolerant of homosexuality and adultery, and Tlazolteotl will come and kill you if you do these things, so don't&quot;. One provides a dramatic framework for conflict and role-playing [if done well], while the other just provides for oppression of certain groups of people, or justifies discrimination and intolerance &quot;because the Gods demand it&quot;. Yes, perhaps that really was the case, once upon a time, and it isn't far off the mark in some places even now. But I don't know about you, but I have no interest in playing a game that takes place in a world where the worst parts of religious intolerance and bigotry <i>are central to the game</i> - I can look at the real world for that. I game to escape, to play characters that can make a difference, can improve things, can change their world for the better - and be part of something better. And since Scion is a game specifically <i>about</i> the Gods and their Scions, there wouldn't be a tidy way to shuffle the bad stuff into the background if one assumes that the religions haven't changed their views on women, LGBTQ people, people from other faiths/cultures, rape, slavery, adultery, and so on. Saying that the Gods have changed leads to a better, more player-friendly world, and that's a good thing. Sticking to outdated dogma doesn't make it a better game, or a better, more &quot;realistic&quot; experience. There can still be drama and conflict; but it doesn't have to be based on the negative views of a presumably-unchanging Zeus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:33:53-08:00","id":1056473,"title":"","content":"Your examples are valid, except that they all represent <i>mortals</i> who claim to be speaking for a deity. I'm talking about the sort of tales where Hanuman fights monsters on Earth, or Athena challenges mortal weavers to a contest, or Tlazolteotl comes down to tempt the chaste [Avatars are different, true, but mostly confined to Hinduism in the largest part. And the Hindu Gods are one of the pantheons handled in Scion, and so would be included in the sort of world I'm speaking of]. Those are larger-than-life, legendary tales of the sort that Scion is trying to replicate, not &quot;a game of mortal heralds of unseen deities who try to change things through words&quot;. No offense meant to the faithful out there - I'm just arguing that the game in question is served better through the presumption of more modern thinking among the pantheons and their faithful, because otherwise, a) it won't be very welcoming to a good section of the audience, and b) it won't be &quot;our modern world with some changes&quot;, but a far less progressive, tolerant game world indeed. And I don't think that's what the designers have in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":".  Edited to comment on Avatars. 03-01-2017, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:23:08-08:00","id":1056579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056469#post1056469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between saying, &quot;bad things exist in the world, and I want to include them in my chronicle/game for dramatic effect and realism&quot;, and saying &quot;The Aztec Gods are completely intolerant of homosexuality and adultery, and Tlazolteotl will come and kill you if you do these things, so don't&quot;. .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not telling them don't do it, I'm telling them it's not going to be a smooth ride. Scions have at least some capacity to manipulate Fate, after all. That means they can get away with stuff that regular mortals can not, so long as they don't push their luck.If somebody wants to play a gay / skirt chasing Aztec Scion, they'd be perfectly free to do so. But just like Hercules, they're going to have some trials to overcome if they want to make it to Godhood. And, should they make it that far, there is always the possibility that they can splinter off and found a new pantheon with a new dogma. Like you said, religions change over time, and I'm sure the more modern Scions are responsible for the majority of those changes. There are roughly 20,000 different branches of Christianity that have cropped up in only 2,000 years since its foundation, every one of which claims they've got it right and everybody else has it wrong. I could see something similar happening to the other pantheons as their children rise to power.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I wouldn't cram the story full of it, but it would be an occasional thing now and then. Like reality once said, &quot;the world isn't one big liberal arts college campus.&quot; There are mean people in the world, there have always been mean people in the world. Intolerance has been an integral part of the human condition ever since the species first emerged on this planet. I'm not interested in a game that pretends humanity achieved world peace and nothing bad ever happens to those who are different. Because that is unrealistic, and does not accurately represent our world, which is where White Wolf games are generally supposed to be taking place.<br /> <br /> I completely understand that you use gaming to escape. I do too, most of the time. But as I said before, the thing that initially drew me to this franchise was its grounding in the real world with a splash of supernatural element. That's what makes the franchise stand out from the countless other power fantasy role playing games on the market. It does something different, and I have no interest in watering it down, because then it loses that spark of individuality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-01-2017, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:34:41-08:00","id":1056631,"title":"","content":"Oh, no, I'm not saying, &quot;take out all the conflict&quot;, because that would also take out all the story potential. I'm saying that I do think that the Gods would change in their views of the world, both from a game perspective (because OPP doesn't want a game where Zeus is an active rapist and the Azecs are homophobes), and from a &quot;reality&quot; perspective, because being interactive with these darn apes has that effect on them. It's more interesting, more dynamic, to have a Goddess of Feminism or a God of LGBT Rights involved in the game than just presuming that Artemis is still a cliche of the old Greek &quot;women are either virgins, mothers, or whores&quot; outlook. If that doesn't work for you, you can certainly make any changes you want to, but the writeups of the Gods that we've seen so far would indicate to me that OPP is definitely open to the thought that &quot;the God's have changed with the times&quot;. And that, for me, makes a more interesting and dynamic world to game in.<br /> (Oh, and why is it that when people discuss War Gods in the modern world, they only talk about Ares/Mars? There are war deities in most cultures, and they would have just as much impact in a Scion universe as Ares does...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:15:29-08:00","id":1056639,"title":"","content":"Another point about the topic of &quot;What would the Gods think&quot; - why is it that the assumption of their unchanging nature only applies to social issues? The argument is made that the Aztecs would still be intolerant to LGBT people, and that the Greeks wouldn't be pro-feminism, because that's what we have as information from the past in our real world. So do we also assume that they are similarly rigid in their thinking about medicine [no modern equipment, just leeches, chirurgeons and mystical healing cauldrons], technology [no human-made advancements, just what Ptah gives us], travel [no airplanes - the Greeks punish those who fly too close to the sun], Astronomy [why study the heavens? Everyone knows the sun is a mystical chariot/mournful Goddess racing across the sky], meteorology [why study the weather when you can change it by appeasing the Storm God of your choice?], and on and on. If you say, &quot;the Gods don't change&quot;, then you open up a really big can of worms that covers pretty much all of human history and achievement, because it means they don't change their views on <i>anything</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:16:15-08:00","id":1056676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056631#post1056631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Oh, and why is it that when people discuss War Gods in the modern world, they only talk about Ares/Mars? There are war deities in most cultures, and they would have just as much impact in a Scion universe as Ares does...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because he's the most immediately recognizable one. I've noticed one of the major problems with Scion in the past is that most people don't know much about the collective pantheons, but do understand parts of a specific group. I, for example, had no idea that the All Father, Odin was the Norse god of death and war, because pantheon chiefs aren't commonly associated with those purviews.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> As for the gods not changing in regards to social issues, I brought up the point earlier that <i>&quot;those in power make the rules.&quot;</i> Anybody who tried to tell the Gods &quot;No&quot; or &quot;this is wrong&quot; was severely punished for it. Why? Becuase they have power, and you don't. If one of the Greco-Roman gods wanted something (like sex), well then, they were going to get some! And if you had the gall to reject them, then they were going to take it by force, and probably curse you for your insolence.<br /> <br /> Also, they are terrible at letting go of old grudges. Just read the Odyssey, a guy gets lost at sea for decades for the simple crime of not making an offering to Poseidon before he set out to sea!<br /> <br /> <br /> That doesn't sound like the mindset of somebody who's open to change. It sounds like somebody who possesses way too much power and has let it go to their heads. Scions have a modicum of that power, so they have the potential to rise above and make some impactful changes. But ordinary mortals won't be so lucky; who's going to take the gods seriously if they allow a bunch of short lived, woefully inept servants (whom they claim to have created) start telling them how to behave properly?<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to keep the technological and medical changes to society, you can very easily do that by claiming the people responsible were Scions, themselves. They probably didn't make it to godhood, but they did use their talents to improve the lives of mankind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:25:54-08:00","id":1056728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056639#post1056639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point about the topic of &quot;What would the Gods think&quot; - why is it that the assumption of their unchanging nature only applies to social issues? The argument is made that the Aztecs would still be intolerant to LGBT people, and that the Greeks wouldn't be pro-feminism, because that's what we have as information from the past in our real world. So do we also assume that they are similarly rigid in their thinking about medicine [no modern equipment, just leeches, chirurgeons and mystical healing cauldrons], technology [no human-made advancements, just what Ptah gives us], travel [no airplanes - the Greeks punish those who fly too close to the sun], Astronomy [why study the heavens? Everyone knows the sun is a mystical chariot/mournful Goddess racing across the sky], meteorology [why study the weather when you can change it by appeasing the Storm God of your choice?], and on and on. If you say, &quot;the Gods don't change&quot;, then you open up a really big can of worms that covers pretty much all of human history and achievement, because it means they don't change their views on <i>anything</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, in Scion 2ed it is more dynamic than just &quot;they dont change&quot;. But the fact they can, doesnt mean that they would. Is even more dynamic than just a brush over all saying &quot;open minded&quot; or &quot;bigoted&quot;.<br /> <br /> The point is not that they doesnt change, they do, but not all of them. I certainly dont think all Theoi would have the old standards of Male-Female, Hierarchy, Bloodlines as they had, but I think of brushing aside and saying that none of them would keep it is weird, specially if the reason is just &quot;they got better&quot;. I think many would change (Apolo, Athens, Artemis), many wouldnt care since the old times (Ares, Hephaestus, Hades, Hermes) and many wouldnt have changed (Zeus, Poseidon, Demeter), for each topic, for each subject. Is just something that you dont need to change to live in society. Being bigoted doenst make you Anachronic.<br /> <br /> Not saying that some Gods wouldnt be Anachronic (Demeter I think wouldnt be up to the latest technologies) but, to most of them, technology is not good nor bad. It is just things that evolved. Morals are harder to change than just adapting to the how things work nowadays (plus, technology took centuries to get where we are, and mostly social issues are widespread from 20th century, 19th century at most). No God would be against evolving technology if this evolution doesnt impact their ways (Pan or the Vanir would, if evolving technology means destroying nature), because there is no statement on technology. A car is not bad because you use a cart, unless you have some strong attachment or is moral/religious to you the use of a cart. Is a question of principle to Zeus, for example, that he is right, because he is Zeus, and Zeus is right. And he is hardly going to change any day soon. Many deities might seem it as a &quot;how things should be&quot; and that the new ways are a &quot;corruption&quot; of how things should be. I admit, most of reasons of a person (or God) keeping a moral standard are applicable to technology, but the religions and situations in which technology is part of the dogma are rare (Amish is an example). There would be extremists, like Ptah Clerics living only of what Ptah created, but they are human extremists, not necessarily the most liked of their Gods (and if they are, the Gods themselves are extremists, why not?).<br /> <br /> Human made technology would mostly doesnt bother the Gods, and they might take or improve something (like clothes or Hephaestus creating their own Golden flying Ferrari) because it is just stuff, and neither people, nor Gods really do care about stuff. Morals people do care a lot, and some will fight for them to the death.<br /> <br /> I agree, the official Gods in Scion 2ed will be all open minded, and probably not have a single line of mention about bigotry, slavery or pederasty of any kind, and I understand why they are doing it. Not all players of Scion are coming from Vampire the Masquerade, and mostly want just some good Epic fun. But are some that want something darker, more &quot;reality like&quot;. So we are going to try to discuss how to make it the game we want.<br /> <br /> It is all about choosing the tone for your game. You want every God to still have his ancient point of view and be mostly an asshole to anyone and anything that is not in their moral compass? Full tone for you. You want a game that, mostly of Gods still act as they were, or with small variations, and just some individuals break the old models? High tone. You want a game were some changed, some dont, and it is all about the individual God and their experiences? Medium tone. You want a game with some Gods, individually, having some bigotry, but as group they are open minded? Low tone. You want a game with no bigotry whatsoever? 0 Tone. Choose what you prefer, with all the in betweens. (my choice is medium to high)<br /> <br /> It should be a God by God thinking, to be sure where in the bigot-o-meter each God will be, in each variation of bigotry. I try to give a overlook of each pantheon to give a general idea of each one, but each God is a God, as each person is a person.<br /> <br /> With that said, from now on, I will be talking considering that you want, in higher or lower tone, bigotry and similar nasty things in your game. If you dont, I don't see a point in discussing what kind of Game you prefer vs. the kind of Game I prefer. Is not really about &quot;realism&quot; or &quot;escapism&quot; or anything, is about the kind of game each of us want. But any opinion is always welcome.<br /> <br /> Time to open another can of worms and start another discussion. We discussed the God's opinion on female rights, homosexuality, transsexuality and polygamy, so lets go for something less polemic and gender oriented: Slavery. This is a topic most for villains/antagonists that are in the world of Scion but are not necessarily with the Titans. Like a Scion of Ares who won a bunch of battles, and uses his god given right (literally) to slave his enemies. Many civilizations had slavery as part of their social life, but they were not necessarily like slavery was in Colonial America.<br /> <br /> Theoi: As far as I understood, the ancient Greek seem to have had different treatments of slavery. The slavery for mines seem to be very close to our Colonial America in terms of terrible conditions (maybe worst), but house slaves seem to have been treated better. They were part of the family nucleus, could have a family, eat with the owner, gather money (to buy his own freedom) and in many cases seem to have even independent jobs, just paying a mensal cost to his owner. At least in Athens there were laws against hurting too much a slave, and murdering one have a serious punishment (not as much as a free citizen, but more than just a fine (maybe exile)), but they could not own property nor practice gymnastics, politics or pederasty. Sparta seem to have had few, and mostly to the upper class, and outside of Athens slave were just property. There were also debt slaves, slaves that became slave to pay his creditors. Most slaves seem to come from War, as was on the war rules of the time that the winner have total control over the loser.<br /> <br /> In Rome there were enough slaves to be a social class, they seem to be treated worst than Greek slaves (at least in Athens) but they became true free citizen when they became free, what didnt happen in Athens. The Romans also improved the rules for slavery as time passes on the empire, even starting to consider that a abandoned slave is a free man. (They also tatooed in some slaves forhead &quot;Catch me, I'm a runaway&quot;, so if this slave fled people would know he is a runaway slave).<br /> <br /> I think the Theoi in modern world would be ok with the idea of not having slaves in society. There would be no rule against (Ganimedes is still working after all), but some Gods might be very unhappy and unsupportive with a Scion who kept slaves for no good reason. (I think Athena and Apolo in first place, but most Gods I think would be adapted to the non-slave society, even Ares if he is okay in following today's war standards). Zeus would be an exception, being mostly okay with a Scion with slaves.<br /> <br /> Norse: Norse seem to had have a caste of slaves, literally, and they seem to had no right, besides &quot;should not be killed&quot;. He is a man-property, and as a Norse you cant kill other fellow man. Their life condition seem to had vary from very bad to not very good, but they could get freedom by payment, by being freed by his owner or someone else, or even on a will. Still the slave have many things he should do to his owner, as paying him some money and should be helping him anytime he need and voting on the same person as him. That condition would pass in 2 generations.<br /> <br /> I think they would be not against, in general, but definitely would be surprised if someone still tried to have a slave in modern day. Something like &quot;Wow, didnt seem that idea in a while&quot;. I'm not quite sure where they would go when they die, but if they follow their masters on death (while still slaves), there would be probably a few in Asgard.<br /> <br /> Egypt: Slavery in Egypt seem to be of 3 kinds: By debt or free will, where you give up/loose your possessions and freedom to became a slave to someone (with with and children); Slavery by War or Crime, in which the slave where property of the pharaoh, and he give them to temples, people or mines, or use them as work force for any kind of service; or Slavery by Social Obligation: seem like a forced labor many citizens needed to do to the pharaoh as a form of &quot;tax labour&quot;, and they where paid by their work and skill, and where not property. Seem that, was a moral principle that they treat well their slaves, and was rules against children doing heavy labour. The slaves where in all levels of work, from government offices to temple workers and mostly of skill simple works. Slavery seem to be in small scale in old Egypt, and mostly on the hand of pharaohs and on International commerce.<br /> <br /> I know less about Egyptian society, but I think the Gods would be, again, not have any rule against. As Egyptian society, and deity system, is very much based on ancient rules and unchangeable sense of moral, they would still find acceptable to own slaves. Not all Gods would be okay with it, necessarily, but there wouldnt be a rule to punish you if you tried.<br /> <br /> Old Japan: Seem to have happened, but was banned in the 16th century. Does not exist many relates about it. But is known cases of Japanese soldiers using populations in &quot;forced labor&quot; works during WW2.<br /> <br /> For the Gods I would go with &quot;It is forbidden, unless really necessary.&quot;. Seems that all is acceptable in Love and War.<br /> <br /> Those pantheons I know little to nothing. This is my best uneducated guess, and please anyone, correct me if I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> Teotl: Aztec slavery seems very curious. Slavery was personal, not hereditary, the slave could have possessions, could not be sold unless he accepted, could be free if marring or having children with their master or if could prove is being mistreated, and very good slaves could became free after the death of the owners. Mostly of those rights are ignored if a authority considered you incorrigible. You could choose to became a slave instead of taking the usual punishment for many crimes (Usually death) or by debt or if your family sold you. You could also sell yourself, be free long enough to enjoy your money then go to slavery. Also, slaves seem to have had quite okay lives. Also Also, this: &quot;Another rather remarkable method for a slave to recover liberty was described by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manuel_Orozco_y_Berra\" target=\"_blank\">Manuel Orozco y Berra</a> in <i>La civilizaci\u00f3n azteca</i> (1860): if, at the <i>tianquiztli</i> (marketplace; the word has survived into modern-day Spanish as &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tianguis\" target=\"_blank\">tianguis</a>&quot;), a slave could escape the vigilance of their master, run outside the walls of the market and step on a piece of human excrement, and then present their case to the judges, they would grant that slave freedom. They would then be washed, provided with new clothes not owned by the master, and declared free. As any person who was not a relative of the master could be declared a slave for trying to <i>prevent</i> a slave's escape, people typically would not help the master prevent the escape.If,one slave was not behaving it would be considered death.&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure what to say about this slavery, nor about the Aztec God's opinion, so I'm passing my guess on this one. So, if anyone has anything to say about it, please do.<br /> <br /> Shen: I dont know much about Chinese history, and this seems very complicated and with a lot of nuances, so I'm not going to guess on this one. Someone knows better than me about it?<br /> Deva: Seem like they forbidden slavery in 200 BCE, and kept like that until Muslims got in contact with their society, and start imposing, plus the Vedas doenst seem to talk very well about it. So I would go with slavery is forbidden, is the antithesis of freedom.<br /> Manitouk: Plenty of tribes. I would guess, not slave as we think about it, but some level of &quot;war prisoners doing work&quot; or something like that. Just a guess.<br /> Orisha: Those I know they had slaves, but I cant say much beyond that. The Gods would seem to be okay with the concept of &quot;War slave&quot; and &quot;Debt Slaves&quot;, but they might have rethought their opinions after Colonial America. Or not, many of the slaves how came to America where sold by other African people, so it is hard to tell.<br /> Tuatha de Dannan: I dont know. I honestly dont know much of them, so no idea. (basically, my magic works to summon Watcher)<br /> <br /> Just to say, this all is about slavery, not race. Those slavery system happened with all kinds, shapes, colours and ethnicities of people, both as masters and as slaves, so there is no good guys here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:31:59-08:00","id":1056735,"title":"","content":"Odysseus blinded Poseidon's son. He was kind of justified in being pissed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:44:03-08:00","id":1056780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056728#post1056728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Shen: I dont know much about Chinese history, and this seems very complicated and with a lot of nuances, so I'm not going to guess on this one. Someone knows better than me about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's safe to assume that Chinese slaves were NOT treated well at all!<br /> <br /> If you need evidence, look up the concept of &quot;foot binding&quot; which they used on women to both prevent them from running away, as well as make their feet slip into smaller shoe sizes. <b>WARNING, </b>it's probably not a good idea to look it up if you have a weak stomach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:45:02-08:00","id":1056782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056728#post1056728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tuatha de Dannan: I dont know. I honestly dont know much of them, so no idea. (basically, my magic works to summon Watcher)</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha! You're good at your summoning spells.<br /> <br /> The Irish had slavery as a core institution, with their main unit of currency, a <i>Cumal</i>, being a female slave. I believe it's three <i>Cumal</i> to a cow. Or other way around, I'm on campus right now and don't have my books on hand. Anyways, yeah, big slave culture. Not based on race or anything, mostly a result of the Irish being pretty focused on internal raiding. Capture slaves from a neighboring people you are raiding, that sort of thing. I don't know if we have a ton of details left, but I know that slaves are mentioned in the legal texts. One of the many variations on marriage is a man marrying a <i>Cumal, </i>not too sure if they had any guest rights or anything. I would assume not. I would suggest their slave system was focused on youth pretty heavily since the biggest detail of slaves in mythology is the Fomori taking a tithe of 1/3 of all children born to every household in Ireland under the reign of Bres. <br /> <br /> If the Tuatha returned from being dead in a game, they'd probably snatch up a bunch of slaves. Most likely when they try to retake Ireland from the mortals. Their Scions might get given some, but I don't know if we know enough about the institution to really flesh it out much past that. It would be a sign of wealth, slaves or cows. I'd suggest to go with the cows, you essentially generate interest more quickly and with way less moral qualms. Sure your cow can't do the weaving for you, but as a Scion you probably don't have a huge need for labor.<br /> <br /> To add to that, the Fomori shouldn't get a bad rap for that. The Fomori are just a foreign colonizing force that put pressure on Ireland, same as the Tuatha, and The Sons of Mil. All of them would happily impose tithes of slaves, and resources on anyone else. The Fomori just committed the crime of clashing with the Tuatha really, the Fomori and the Tuatha are pretty much the same as each other, no cackling evil or anything. I suspect they pick up their 'evil monster' tag later on, I would wager in the Victorian period, due to the Fomori having some sort of maiming thing going on with them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:01:36-08:00","id":1056900,"title":"","content":"I guess it matters whether we'really saying &quot;in the Scion 2nd edition world of OPP&quot; or &quot;in a real, parallel world where the God's were/are real and their worship continued until 2017.&quot;<br /> To the first: Do I think OPP is going to officially have the worst aspects of religions in their game? No. Do I think they should? No. Do I think someone will explore it through fan-made supplements? Sure. And they have every right to do so. If your style and group are okay with it, fill your boots. <br /> To the second: I tend to agree that not all deities would change, and that many things we take for granted would not come to pass. But there are as many alternate world ideas as there are humans with imagination, and I'm not going to pretend that I know how a God (or even more so, a Goddess) would think, or that I know more than someone else on how that would turn out. There is no right or wrong in a discussion about divinity in an alternate world. I run my own long-term game in such a world, and I have my own thoughts, but I'm not going to suggest they are better or worse than anyone else's.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T20:16:55-08:00","id":1056957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056900#post1056900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it matters whether we'really saying &quot;in the Scion 2nd edition world of OPP&quot; or &quot;in a real, parallel world where the God's were/are real and their worship continued until 2017.&quot;<br /> To the first: Do I think OPP is going to officially have the worst aspects of religions in their game? No. Do I think they should? No. Do I think someone will explore it through fan-made supplements? Sure. And they have every right to do so. If your style and group are okay with it, fill your boots.<br /> To the second: I tend to agree that not all deities would change, and that many things we take for granted would not come to pass. But there are as many alternate world ideas as there are humans with imagination, and I'm not going to pretend that I know how a God (or even more so, a Goddess) would think, or that I know more than someone else on how that would turn out. There is no right or wrong in a discussion about divinity in an alternate world. I run my own long-term game in such a world, and I have my own thoughts, but I'm not going to suggest they are better or worse than anyone else's.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The major factor in this question is that these are polytheistic religions, as opposed to monotheism. When you have multiple deities, you have multiple goals and opinions, and that results in internal conflict.; Some gods will probably change, especially if it supports their world view. But others will reject the change because it disturbs their comfortable life style. The most realistic way to portray that is to include both sides of the spectrum in the same game. Some gods &quot;got better&quot; over time, while others clung to the past.<br /> <br /> In that sense, they're not much different from humans. There are lots of people who look at the way the world is changing, and disapprove of it, believing that things were better back in their time. (I, for example am nervously skeptical about the emphasis society is placing on cyber interaction, as opposed to dealing with people in person). While there are also people who welcome and adapt to the changes, because they find it easier / more enjoyable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T12:50:51-08:00","id":1057197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056780#post1056780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's safe to assume that Chinese slaves were NOT treated well at all!<br /> <br /> If you need evidence, look up the concept of &quot;foot binding&quot; which they used on women to both prevent them from running away, as well as make their feet slip into smaller shoe sizes. <b>WARNING, </b>it's probably not a good idea to look it up if you have a weak stomach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to derail the discussion there, but footbinding had <i>nothing</i> to do with slavery. Such a &quot;lotus foot&quot; was a mark of beauty and nobility, not of servitude. I mean, still horrible sexist crap, but a whole other kettle of fish from slaves and how they were treated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056728#post1056728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Old Japan: Seem to have happened, but was banned in the 16th century. Does not exist many relates about it. But is known cases of Japanese soldiers using populations in &quot;forced labor&quot; works during WW2.<br /> <br /> For the Gods I would go with &quot;It is forbidden, unless really necessary.&quot;. Seems that all is acceptable in Love and War.<br /> <br /> Shen: I dont know much about Chinese history, and this seems very complicated and with a lot of nuances, so I'm not going to guess on this one. Someone knows better than me about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, historical East Asian slavery is kind of ... fuzzy around the edges. There's very much historical development there, and very few clear definitions. In general, if one talks about cultural perceptions of slavery, one encounters a problem of definition - what is slavery? Do models as different as the Roman one, the Aztec one, the Ottoman one, the US one really deserve the same label? Often we find a lot of nuance within a culture, the treatment of debt slaves, war captives, slaves of different ethnicity, and so on being very different. When cultures with such different social conceptions encounter one another, miscommunications arise, further pointing out that there is no such thing as kingship, slavery, piracy, queerness, or whatever, but only ever culturally specific &quot;Irish kingship&quot;, &quot;Mesopotamian kingship&quot;, &quot;Medieval Japanese piracy&quot;, &quot;Caribbean piracy&quot;, &quot;Song Dynasty queerness&quot;, &quot;21st century Western queerness&quot;, and so on (a problem which is also totally the topic of my B.A. thesis, but I digress). This fundamental indivdual-ness is something to keep in mind when cultures who hold such related but different institutions clash, as they are wont to do in Scion. I'll still talk about &quot;slavery&quot; below, but even if we can't avoid using problematic terms (because there are no appropriate replacements), we should keep in mind that, how and why they are problematic.<br /> <br /> Back to East Asian slavery in particular, though. I can't say all that much about China, because I don't have as much background there as with Japan, but the bottom line is: That concept changed constantly. There were different sources for slaves over time: debt slaves in the young state of Ancient China that meted out severe punishments to create order in this newly created thing; war captives in the Golden Age of expanding Medieval China, centre of the world; and whole ethnic groups in the multi-ethnic mega-state of Early Modern China. The history of China until the Revolution of 1911 can, simplified, be viewed as an ever-turning wheel of ethnic groups, religions, philosophies etc. changing in dominance, spinning around an axle of core values. That can, of course, be said about e.g. Europe as well, but I find that the changes in China, where no creed or philosophy was ever as powerful as Christianity or Islam, are more fluent. Thus, attitudes to social institutions like slavery could change fundamentally from dynasty to dynasty and even from ruler to ruler. Some tried to abolish slavery, others codified it; some made slaves into court eunuchs, others drew eunuchs from the free population, others tried to abolish <i>that </i>institution. And the reason I make such a big excourse into history there is that if there is one pantheon that does constantly change, it's the Shen, most of whom are deified mortals from a wide array of historical eras, who would thus have grown up in wildly different environments regarding such issues. So basically, most of what I can say is: It's complicated.<br /> <br /> With Japan, you see even more of that fuzziness. Slavery did exist in Japan for most of the country's history, but weirdly, it did so mostly in name only. It seems as if slavery never was really important in pre-modern Japan, and that the slave population was never very big. I read quite a few works of Japanese historical literature and historical documents, but I've never encountered a single slave therein; I've been told there is evidence, but it's sparse. There were no big slave markets, and more of a kidnapping of certain people by certain other people until <i>yet</i> different people managed to free them or not. Really big was the slave trade the Japanese then held with the Portuguese, but that lasted not even 50 years until Toyotomi Hideyoshi, as part of his general anti-European policy, outlawed it (don't cheer him too much, though, he also robbed peasants of basically all their rights and had lots of Christian converts executed, so ...). Essentially, the attitude of the Kami would be ... they've heard of it, but never held much interest, and gotten off the habit centuries ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1041769-what-would-the-gods-think?p=1056728#post1056728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orisha: Those I know they had slaves, but I cant say much beyond that. The Gods would seem to be okay with the concept of &quot;War slave&quot; and &quot;Debt Slaves&quot;, but they might have rethought their opinions after Colonial America. Or not, many of the slaves how came to America where sold by other African people, so it is hard to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't claim to be an expert on the relationship between African and Euro-American slavery, but the issue <i>is</i> more difficult than &quot;Africans sold Africans, so they were okay with it&quot;. This is where my aforementioned concept of miscommunication comes into play: The Yoruba idea of slavery was fundamentally different from the Western one. Slaves in traditional Yoruba society were mainly war captives, debtors, and criminals, though locally also an ethnic caste. There were jobs that were only done by slaves, and not only just the nastiest ones: Gate guardians and royal emissaries, for example, were exclusive slave offices. Slaves weren't chattle, but a social rank/caste with certain (though of course still inferior) rights, and had at least a certain degree of legal protection against maltreatment. They were allowed to own property and to marry both other slaves and free people; the children of two slaves would also be slaves, but those of a slave and a free person would be free. On the other hand, however, the slave caste was also the source for the relatively rare human sacrifices of the Yoruba.<br /> <br /> Beginning with the Portuguese explorations of the 15th century, the Yoruba kingdom of Ijebu, which bought it slaves from the far bigger and more powerful kingdom of Oyo, became one of the biggest exporters of African slaves to the Euro-American sphere. Not only did this extreme demand in slaves permanently change West African culture, intensifying the need for destructive wars to claim new, profitable captives, but it also confronted the sold slaves with a violently different concept of such servitude. People in Africa, in the Yoruba kingdoms, for a long time simply had no idea how much more brutal slavery abroad was, and we have strong historical pointers that they would never have let the trade become this big had they known about it. When word of the conditions in the Americas did reach the homeland through returning freedmen, we can actually see even many prominent slave traders turning into stalwart enemies of their profession, fighting against the ill-treatment of their &quot;merchandise&quot; - look up people like Madam Tinubu.<br /> <br /> So if you want to get an idea of how the Orisha view slavery, it may best be expressed as &quot;Yoruba slavery good, other slavery bad&quot;. And I think that could be applied to many, if not all cultures. There was slavery in almost every part of the world, at least at some point in history, and the slave owners there probably thought they were doing right. In the 19th century, the Cuban elites railed against British efforts for Abolition as slavery was supposedly the best that could be done for the slaves' salvation, yet derided the Muslim slave trade in the Mediterrannean. Chinese dynasties which were okay with their own slaving system balked at the mutilated and castrated slaves some of their allies sent them as gifts. As I said in the beginning, it's less fruitful to ask how a civilisation sees an abstract concept of &quot;slavery&quot;, and more so to ask what it counted as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}